Tbong Khmum Provincial Commissioner Shares Experience in Implementing Safe Village-Commune Policy, Receiving Good Rankings for 3 Consecutive Years (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): On June 25, 202, Major General Ben Roth, Tbong Khmum Provincial Police Commissioner, shared his experience in implementing the safe village-commune policy, which the province received a good ranking for 3 consecutive years.
Lt. Gen. Ben Rath continued that in order to implement the policy of safe villages and communes to achieve good results for 3 consecutive years, the provincial leaders at all levels have constantly memorized 9 policies with disciplines. 5 must take the 4th grade exam, must confirm the results and 4 other principles for implementation.
The lieutenant general raised the question of why Tbong Khmum province has ensured security, safety and order?
The youngest provincial commissioner for Tbong Khmum has been established for seven years, while he himself has been the provincial police commissioner for three years, so on behalf of the provincial police leadership, The Village, Commune, and Safety Policy Competition is a security measure.
The Tbong Khmum Provincial Commissioner said that in order to implement this policy well, the police at various checkpoints throughout the province have been tasked with disseminating the 9 points of the village, commune, and safety policy to the people by observing the local police. Be flexible according to the situation. In particular, his police took on some of the most sensitive social issues to spread to the public, such as traffic accidents, drug problems and so on.
Lt. Gen. Ben Rath stated that through good relations with the people with the authorities, the crimes in the province have gradually decreased, and these are the results of disseminating the law and the policy of safe villages and communes. To local people.
According to the report, in 2019, Tbong Khmum Province maintained security and order in the process of organizing the Commune / Sangkat Council Election, 4th Mandate, Senate Election, 4th Legislature and Election. The 6th legislature proceeded smoothly and without fear, intimidation, threats and violence, as well as many other important ceremonies and events.
