(Phnom Penh): On Thursday, June 25, 2020, the Cambodian Red Cross, chaired by Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, received a donation of hand soap, gel and promotional materials on measures to prevent Kovid-19 from the International Committee. Red Cross (ICRC).
On that occasion, the Cambodian Red Cross also donated these items along with 9,050 T-shirts to the 25 branches of the Cambodian Red Cross for capital and provinces for humanitarian operations.
On that occasion, Mr. Roman Paramonov expressed his appreciation to the Cambodian Red Cross for its effective humanitarian mission in the past, especially in contributing to the Royal Government of Cambodia in the fight against Kovid-19 in Cambodia. With success that can be considered a model for the world.
At the same time, the Secretary-General brought the remarks of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, who sent greetings and deep memories to the 25 branches of the Cambodian Red Cross, especially to express his appreciation. All the branches that have taken care to work hard to help the most vulnerable and vulnerable people in a timely manner are worthy to assist the public authorities in the field of humanitarian.
At the same time, the Secretary-General outlined the structure, roles and responsibilities of the Branch-Executive Committee and instructed all branches on how to use the communication network, how to make reports and other outreach work to increase work efficiency.
In addition, she recommended to all branches to prepare for and respond to floods this rainy season, as well as fires, hurricanes, typhoons and other natural disasters.
(Preah Sihanouk): Senior Minister Kun Kim, Vice President and Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, on June 25, 2020, visited and inspected the living conditions of the families of Cambodian veterans living on social land concessions. In Tumnup Rolok commune, Stung Hav district, Preah Sihanouk province.
The visit and inspection of the lives of veterans was also attended by Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Sihanoukville and Honorary President of the Cambodian Veterans Association of Sihanoukville, as well as other relevant officials.
In return for the merits of the veterans who have made significant contributions to the cause of the motherland and to alleviate the hardships of the veterans, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has decided to provide approximately 302 hectares in Tumnup Rolok commune, Stung Hav district, Preah Sihanouk province for housing for veterans.
About 182 families of veterans have been selected to live in housing provided by the government. In addition to a house and 30 meters by 40 meters of residential land, a family of veterans also received 1 hectare of arable land.
During the visit to inspect the lives of the veterans, Senior Minister Kun Kim, Samdech Techo's Chief of Staff, visited and inspected the lives of the veterans in their homes and informed them of their memories and care. High on their well-being from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen.
Senior Minister Kun Kim told the veterans that even though Samdech Techo Prime Minister and Samdech Kittipritthbandit did not reach the veterans' homes, Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit were always with the veterans. In addition, both Samdechs always remind the relevant associations and authorities to pay attention to the livelihood and solve all the problems of veterans.
In addition to showing the memories and care of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittiprit to the veterans, Senior Minister Kun Kim, an association leader who actively works for the benefit of the veterans, also reminded the veterans. Fighters to work hard to grow crops on land provided by the Royal Government. At the same time, animals should be raised to earn extra income to support the livelihood in addition to the money provided by the Royal Government every month.
Senior Minister Kun Kim in front of Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, the provincial governor, also urged the relevant authorities in the province to pay attention to solving the problems of veterans and intervene to facilitate the activities of veterans, such as farming and animal husbandry. Etc. to help them earn a living.
Veterans in the above areas have been living in a better living condition after they received houses and land for cultivation from the Royal Government. They also thanked the Royal Government, especially Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, who always pay high attention to the well-being of veterans.
