(Phnom Penh): The Governor of Tbong Khmum Province, Mr. Cheam Chansophoan, on the morning of June 25, 2020, presented the achievements and progress of Tbong Khmum Provincial Administration through the press conference of the Government Spokesperson's Unit on "Progress and Work Direction". Continuation of Tbong Khmum Provincial Administration.
Business: There are 127 companies and 104 enterprises registered with the Ministry of Commerce, 141 business licenses have been issued, 7 provinces have 7 markets and the Cambodian Border Model Market (Dar Market) has 68 booths.
The trade volume between Tbong Khmum and Vietnam in 2019 was about 373 million USD, of which exports were about 202 million USD and imports were about 171 million USD. The trade volume in 2019 compared to 2018 increased by about $ 97 million, equivalent to 26%.
* Tourism: Tbong Khmum has the potential to develop tourism as a priority on natural, cultural, historical and processing resorts. This development aims to improve the quality of tourism in terms of contributing to the conservation of natural resources, sustainable development and high responsibility, and development to improve people's livelihoods, provide employment opportunities, generate income, reduce migration and help Contribute to climate change mitigation.
Tbong Khmum Province has resorts such as: Preah Theat Basrey Resort, Luang Preah Sdach Kan Resort, Rubber Plantation, Hong Waterfall Resort, Anlong Chrey Development Village Resort, O'Ktong Resort, Ta Se Doung Krom Resort, Chamkar Chhoukrath Resort, Memot Museum, Community Tourism Class OBT basic training and there are many tourist destinations for leisure and relaxation during national holidays and other holidays.
Water Resources and Meteorology: Tbong Khmum Province protected 1,600 meters of river banks, restored 4,200 meters of canals, repaired 2,600 meters of dams, maintained 7 annual and permanent irrigation systems, constructed 2 diversion dams, and maintained gate construction. 5 water points, maintenance of 7,500 meters long dams, repairing 5 dams and constructing 2 sluice gates.
Border work: Tbong Khmum province borders Tay Ninh province, Socialist Republic of Vietnam, with two districts along the border: Ponhea Krek and Memot. Tbong Khmum province has 7 border checkpoints, including 1 international border checkpoint, Trapeang Phlong, 2 bilateral border checkpoints (Dar and Tonle Cham) and 4 border checkpoints (Choam Kravien, Daun Rath, Chan Moul and Tonlong).
The provincial administration pays close attention to security and development in the border area in line with the Royal Government's goal of "turning the border area into a town" by achieving the following key achievements:
First, the corridor was completely eliminated and the sale or lease of farmland, farmland or houses along the border to the people of Vietnam was completely stopped until now.
Second, border security is thoroughly monitored and strengthened through weekly, monthly and annual meetings of the Provincial Administrative Unity Command.
Third, establish a provincial border development commission, which is a mechanism for leading and implementing border development work with a clear vision.
* Land and construction management: In 2019-2020, the provincial administration received a total of 73 land complaints, of which the provincial administration resolved 13 cases, withdrew 11 complaints, rejected 7 cases and continued to resolve 42 cases.
