The death toll from a 7.4-magnitude earthquake that struck the Pacific coast of southern Mexico on Tuesday has risen to seven, with at least two homes destroyed. Thousands were completely damaged. This is according to the report from the local authority quoted by the Xinhua news agency on Thursday afternoon, June 25, 2020.
Pictures on social media show the rock blocking a mountain road between Oaxaca and the coast. Many buildings in the area around the epicenter were severely damaged. Buildings in the city of Mexico City, hundreds of kilometers from the epicenter, were also hit by the quake, forcing people to flee from buildings and stand in the streets.
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Khun Haing in charge of Special Mission and Chairman of the National Task Force for Local Assistance in Po Sen Chey District at the Public Forum this morning, June 25, 2020, expressed his support for all requests made by village representatives. Each raised and urged the Board of Governors to address them as much as possible to any request that is beyond the capacity to resolve, please send to the capital or national level to resolve together.
The support of Senior Minister Khun Haing was made after the dissemination and consultation forum of the 3rd mandate Por Senchey District Council, which had 15 representatives, raised questions and requests orally. Through another 27 letters, he requested the Khan Council and the Board of Governors of Po Sen Chey District to facilitate and solve for the people, most of which are: roads, sewers, garbage, clean water and gambling.
The outreach and consultation forum was held at Wat Tangkasang South, Sangkat Kakap II, Mr. Khieu Khinath, Khan Council Representative and Mr. Hem Darith, Governor of Por Senchey District, and was attended by 247 people from 73 villages.
This forum focuses on security, public order, local development and the environment to identify key issues as a priority for the district administration to consider reforms in the implementation of its program to improve the quality of life of the people in the district. Especially poor people to have a better life.
The questions and suggestions collected from this forum have great potential, which enables the district administration to reflect the shortcomings, inactive points that the district administration has implemented in the past to consider and improve in accordance with Practical accuracy at the grassroots.
It should be noted that during the dissemination and consultation forum of Por Senchey District Council, 3rd mandate in 2019, 79 issues were received from the people, of which 52 issues were resolved and the remaining 27 issues were added to the request. Blessings today and the Board of Governors will continue to work to resolve. Despite the difficult situation, Cambodians can get high-paying job opportunities with International Ezrach
