Thai authorities deport three Cambodians back to Cambodia after nearly five years in prison for illegal border crossing
(Oddar Meanchey): Three Cambodian citizens were sent back to Cambodia by the Thai authorities through Choam International Port in Cheung Phnom Village, Trapeang Prey Commune, Anlong Veng District, Oddar Meanchey Province on the afternoon of June 24, 2020, after serving almost 5 years in Thai territory for illegal border crossing.
According to the report of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Police, on June 25, 2020, the three Cambodian citizens sent by Thailand were arrested by Thailand on September 08, 2016 for crossing the border to cut rosewood. Illegal entry through Chamkar Kor checkpoint in Banteay Meanchey province and detention in the province of Amnat Charoen, Thailand.
