National Bank of Cambodia Introduces Three Measures to Contribute to Stabilizing Prices and Improving Monetary Policy Efficiency for the Next Quarter
(Phnom Penh): On June 24, 2020, the National Bank of Cambodia organized the 51st Meeting of the Monetary Policy Committee with the participation of Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia and Chairman of the Monetary Policy Committee.
The meeting discussed the current state of the world economy, progress and challenges of macroeconomic and financial stability in Cambodia, as well as monetary policy to be implemented in the future.
At that meeting, the National Bank of Cambodia decided on three monetary policy positions to contribute to maintaining price stability and improving the effectiveness of monetary policy for the next quarter, including:
1: Intervene in the exchange market as necessary to maintain exchange rate stability. 2: Continue to supply liquidity in KHR through guaranteed liquidity operation (LPCO) in appropriate size. 3. Continue to strengthen the widespread use of the riel in accordance with existing measures and measures through market mechanisms. General knowledge: The last breath of the monarchy in China
