Cambodian Derivatives Exchange and the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia Collaborate to Promote Derivatives Market by Providing International Training Courses
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Derivatives Exchange and the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia have partnered on an international derivatives training partnership to increase access and training opportunities for the public derivatives brokers.
Cambodian Derivatives Exchange works closely with the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia in organizing this training, based on the scope of the collaboration. Fully support the participants, organize the exam process according to the standard and promote the promotion of this training course continuously.
"Nothing can stop us from achieving our dreams and nothing can stop our aspirations for human resource development, derivatives market promotion and boosting our national economy," said Chhay Leakena. "Even though the whole world is being affected by the Kovid 19 pandemic, our sector remains strong and we are using modern technology to make it more prosperous and productive."
Mr. Lawrence Kook said, “Cambodian Derivatives Exchange has always had the honor of being a long-term partner of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, and through the combination of the leadership skills of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia with its experience and expertise. We have high expectations for this international training. ”
He added that the presence of online derivative training courses will make it easier and more efficient for participants or participants as they do not need to be present at the training site and the training process is Minimal constraints as social gaps were applied during the Kovid 19 epidemic. Therefore, the launch of this training course is fully welcomed.
Mr. Su Socheat said, "Allowing universal participation is a core benefit of this international derivative training course, meaning that both people in the provinces and those living abroad can participate in "This training can save them resources and time, as well as help them become qualified individuals in terms of understanding, skills and experience in the derivatives market."
Mr. Sou Socheat added, "We are very pleased with this achievement and are very pleased to be working with Cambodian Derivatives Exchange, a prominent and highly professional central counterpart." "Through this partnership, we will work together to benefit our people, our country and the derivatives market as a whole."
Please be informed that the first international training course will start soon. The Ministry of Economy issued a Prakas on the implementation of withholding tax on interest on domestic and foreign loans of banks and microfinance institutions.
