Source: CNN (Wednesday, June 24, 2020) The University of Battambang organized the first workshop on "Preparation of Self-Assessment Report"
The workshop is under the Higher Education Improvement Project (HEIP), funded by the World Bank. The three trainers from the General Secretariat of the Accreditation Committee of Cambodia (ACC) were: Dr. Rath Chhang, Deputy Secretary General of the Accreditation Committee of Cambodia, Mr. Sea Ith, Director of the Standards Department and Mr. Tep Ship, Deputy Director of the Department of Standards and Chief Officer of the ASEAN Youth Education Quality Assessment.
The purpose of this workshop is to strengthen the institutional capacity and capacity building of the Management and Evaluation Officer of the University of Battambang. In addition, the workshop aims to disseminate additional knowledge on the 9 quality standards, 73 indicators, evidence, data collection methods and to share experiences with relevant officials of the University of Battambang in the preparation of self-assessment report (SAR).
The University of Battambang will submit a report on self-assessment (SAR) on the implementation of national standards for evaluation by the Accreditation Committee of Cambodia next year and submit a report of the Accreditation Committee of Cambodia to the Global Board. Battambang High School in 2021.
Ms. Sieng Em Totim, Rector of the University of Battambang, stated that this workshop will provide basic knowledge and important input in preparing a quality and effective self-assessment report (SAR) in accordance with the strategic plan of the University of Battambang and In accordance with the policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
The Rector also expressed his deep gratitude to the Royal Government of Cambodia, the World Bank, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, especially Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Dr. Ros Sovacha, Secretary General of the Accreditation Committee of Cambodia. The trainer came to present and Mr. Mak Ngoy, Director General of the General Department of Higher Education and Chairman of the Higher Education Improvement Project.
Please be reminded that for the prevention of Kovit 19 disease, the University of Battambang has prepared to measure the temperature, wash hands and alcohol, wear masks and have a safety gap for educators who participate in accordance with the procedures of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and the Ministry of Health. Also. Ministry of Public Works Continues Education Campaign to Disseminate Road Traffic Law to Banlung City, Ratanakkiri Province
