(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, on June 24, 2020, emphasized that under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Cambodia can manage the situation of Kovid-19 well through Establish a series of necessary socio-economic measures.
The Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth made the remarks at the official launch of the "Cash Support Program for Poor and Vulnerable Families During Kovid-19" under the chairmanship of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, held at Peace Palace this morning, June 24, 2020.
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth stated that "Under the wise, skillful, firm and realistic leadership of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, Cambodia has been able to manage the situation well and reduce this negative impact to within the circle that can "Managed by the introduction of a series of necessary socio-economic measures."
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth emphasized that in this framework, Samdech Techo Prime Minister has paid special attention to the plight of people affected by Kovid-19.
The Deputy Prime Minister added that under the guidance of Samdech Techo, the Economic and Financial Policy Committee has set up a working group to study the feasibility and mechanisms to alleviate the hardships of the people, resulting in the design and implementation of assistance programs. A new society, the "Cash Support Program for Poor and Vulnerable Families During Kovid-19," is the subject of an official launch today.
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth further stated that this program was launched due to the good achievements of the Royal Government's public financial management reform, especially due to the remarkable and proud results in Collection of state budget revenue in the last 5 years.
In addition, combined with the strict management, strict discipline and high efficiency of public spending of the state, both in terms of allocation and operational aspects, including the timely and vigorous introduction of editorial measures. Expenses of government ministries and institutions during the Kovid-19 crisis.
