In the first half of 2020, the rate of mine casualties decreased to 42%
(Battambang): Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Deputy Chairman of the Mine Authority, confirmed that in the first half of 2020, the number of victims of landmines and munitions was 36, which shows a decrease of 42% compared with In the first half of 2019, there were 62 victims of landmines and landmines.
This confirmation was made on the occasion that Senior Minister Ly Thuch, accompanied by Samdech Techo Prime Minister, presided over a meeting with the people and erected a billboard to raise awareness about mines and explosive remnants of war in Samlot District, Battambang Province. Cooperation between Battambang Provincial Mine Action Authority and Sir Bobby Charlton Foundation this morning, June 24, 2020.
