On behalf of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, the Senior Minister expressed his deepest gratitude to all the people of Samlot District who have joined the Royal Government of Cambodia in maintaining and supporting peace for the nation under the win-win policy of Samdech. Techo to end the war at the end of 1998 throughout Cambodia.
The Senior Minister stated that the reason for raising the mine awareness banner in Samlot district is because the mine casualty rate in the first half of 2020, Samlot district has the highest casualty rate is Eleven people, or 31 percent of the country's 36 victims.
Buth Ratana, Director of the Cambodia Foundation, confirmed that the Sir Bobby Charlton Foundation has recognized that the clearance of landmines and explosive remnants of war takes decades after the end of the war. This is why the Foundation cooperates with the Mine Authority to install mine awareness education billboards to remind and send safe messages and avoid these dangers.
