An earthquake measuring 7.0 on the Richter scale is more likely to cause severe damage if it hits a town. For example, in 2017, Mexico also experienced such natural disasters. A magnitude 7.1 earthquake shook the city of Mexico City, killing at least 355 people in the capital and surrounding states.
