(Pursat): The stingrays, another rare species in Cambodia, have been hunted, trampled and killed. Piles of meat and carcasses of wild animals that have not been collected by hunters were found by the rangers and officials of the Wildlife Alliance on June 23, 2020 while patrolling to prevent and suppress natural resource crimes in the area. Wildlife Sanctuary, South Cardamom Mountain National Park, Pursat Province.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesman for the Ministry of Environment, expressed his deep regret over the loss of the bull and condemned the perpetrators who often committed the crime of trapping and hunting rare animals, despite the Ministry of Environment and authorities. Involve efforts to protect, conserve, increase education, not to hunt wildlife anyway.
