Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that traps and rifles are hidden killers of wildlife in Cambodia, all of which need to be prevented and suppressed from being taken into protected areas. He said more than 10,000 traps had been removed from protected areas and more than 300 rifles and ammunition had been seized in the first four months of 2020.
