Tomorrow morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen announces the implementation of the program to provide cash to poor and vulnerable people due to Kovid 19
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the morning of June 24, 2020, will announce the implementation of the program to provide cash to about 600,000 poor and vulnerable people with Kovid 19 disease. The ceremony will take place at the Peace Palace.
The 19 global epidemics of Kovid are causing a severe economic crisis. For Cambodia as well, the economy has experienced an unprecedented deficit in the last 20 years. Cambodians are also struggling because Kovid 19 causes a loss of monthly income.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen has decided to release a national budget package to alleviate the hardships of the poor and vulnerable people during the 19 19 outbreak of Kovid. Last May, the government instructed all national teams to conduct research and update the identification of poor families during the 19 epidemic of Kovid so that the government can provide cash to alleviate their hardships.
While inspecting the construction site of a new airport in Kandal province, Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced that the Royal Government will provide about 25 million US dollars per month to help about 600,000 families in need.
According to a recent sub-decree on cash subsidies recently obtained by Fresh News, poor and vulnerable families who receive benefits must have a valid equity card based on poverty level: 1 (poor) or poor level 2 (poor) and went to verify the list of cash support programs for poor families during the fight against Kovid 19 at any commune hall.
The sub-decree also states that the amount to be provided per month is between 16,000 Riels to 120,000 Riels. The level of cash to be subsidized is based on the type of poor family in level 1 or level 2 and also divided according to the type of household in the capital and rural areas.
In the past, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has also instructed all national working groups to bring food and supplies to help the poor and vulnerable to Kovid 19.
It should be noted that as of June 23, 2020, Cambodia has identified 130 cases of Kovid 19 disease. Of those, 127 have been treated and three are being treated at the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital.
