Until the end of the war on September 2, 1945, many countries in the world suffered heavy casualties, even those involved in the war and those involved in ending the war suffered considerable damage. Human life, wealth, infrastructure to the point of a complex socio-economic crisis.
Moreover, when the German army faced obstacles, the army commander often ordered the immediate killing of Russian prisoners of war without any tolerance as a psychological tactic to intimidate the enemy. This made the Soviet Union the most devastated country during World War II.
In Asia, we also suffered a lot of tragedy, that is, when the Imperial Japanese army came to China and clashed from 1937-1945. The Sino-Chinese war was devastating, with 7 million civilians and 2 million Chinese soldiers killed, but official Chinese reports show that Wings up to 20 million people.
The Japanese invasion of China in 1937 was also a barrier between Japan itself and the real enemy, the Soviet Union. At that time, China did not have a central government, and much of this vast territory was ruled by generals, including the Kuomintang Republican Party led by Zhang Kai-shek and the Chinese Communist Party led by Mao Zedong.
Even more tragic is the Chinese army's lack of sophisticated weapons, as they have only ancient swords, spears, and artillery, making it vulnerable to Japanese troops armed with sophisticated artillery.
Hungry and suffering from the Japanese aggression, the Chinese people were forced to revolt against the Japanese army without thinking of death. This is similar to the Russian people who fought against the German army.
