Five-star chef interested in duck beak and did not expect that Cambodia has this type of shell
(Koh Kong): After visiting the duck beak farm of Peam Krasom community, Koh Kong province, the chefs from Le Royal Hotel showed great interest and said that the Khmer duck beak is very good and its features are good. Color, texture and taste.
After proper cooking, the meat is very delicious, and if processed, foreign guests like to eat and are addicted. This was stated by the leader of the 5-star Le Royal team, who recently visited the Peam Krasop community in Koh Kong province to learn about Khmer duck beak shells.
After inspecting the location of the duck beak farm directly and after cooking the shellfish meat there, Mr. Srun Kakada, the leader of the 5 star chef team of Le Royal Hotel, confirmed that the duck beak shells really exist. Good quality of meat, color and including the environment of the marine environment is pure natural, making the meat grow well and taste very delicious.
The duck beak breeder, who has many years of experience, added that each year, the community raises duck beaks from 10 tons to 100 tons. This yield is also based on the capital availability of each of them.
Confirming to the media in this regard, Mr. Net Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment, said that in fact, duck beak is a famous dish abroad that is popular and expensive. However, if you look at Cambodia, most people do not know this delicious food. In fact, Cambodia also has this type of shell, which is a local product from the Peam Krasop Nature Reserve in Koh Kong province.
The Secretary of State stated that in the past, some people did not know that duck beak was rich in the Peam Krasop area in Cambodia, and therefore to strengthen conservation as well as create a local economy, Mr. Say Sam Al The Minister of Environment has taken care to connect the Peam Krasop community with this marketing section to help you have the right market and sell at a reasonable price.
The Secretary of State stated, "Indeed, for a large number of Europeans and foreigners, duck beak is well known and very popular. It is also expensive, but for some Cambodians it is less familiar. How much is this? "In fact, people in the community have been raising it since the 1990s, and we sell it to neighboring countries, especially Vietnam, Thailand, and there is little local food."
Regarding the market issue, Mr. Neth Pheaktra also said that the Ministry of Environment does not link our conservation with the creation of a community economy and their products are sold outside. When a product has a market, they make money. Tbong Khmum Constituency Deputies Bring Candles to 4 Wats in Tbong Khmum District
Mr. Prach Chan said that our country today is constantly growing in all fields, especially in the field of Buddhism, because the country is peaceful, which came from the right and strong leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. Prime Minister of Cambodia.
According to Prach Chan, entering the rainy season is a rule that the Samma Samputa has commanded for all monks and apostles to follow for three months, from the 1st day of the month of Assad to the 15th day of the month of Assoch. Vesa is an important festival in Buddhism, an important time for monks and nuns to study the Dharma and discipline consistently according to the Buddha's teachings.
