* First: Transport and economic infrastructure:
One 400-megawatt Lower Sesan 2 dam, inaugurated under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia in December 2018, is currently operating to supply electricity to Electricite du Cambodge.
The four major river bridges are the 1,057-meter-long bridge over the Sekong River, the 1,731-meter-long bridge across the Mekong River, the 260-meter-long Kong Sen Chey River Bridge, and the 240-meter-long upper Koh Tonsay Senchey Bridge across the Kong River.
National road through 3 provinces, 7 national roads from Kratie border to Trapeang Kriel international gate, 86.6 km, National Road 9, connecting Stung Treng-Preah Vihear border to Stung Treng city, 72.9 km, National Road 78 From O'Pong Moan point, Stung Treng city to Sre Pok bridge, Ron Kiri province, 65 km.
