Prepare the embankment of the river bank to protect the embankment and enhance the beauty of the town to reach 270 meters. Establish 2 roundabouts in Stung Treng town and 7 parks.
* Second: Border area development and bilateral cooperation:
Construction of red gravel road along the Cambodia-Laos border in the province, with the completion of 200 km and 7 concrete bridges from 18 to 36 meters. Develop land, housing, social concessions for families, the competent forces stand along the Cambodia-Laos border line, 500 houses and equipped with solar power as a gift from Samdech Techo Prime Minister and Samdech Kittiprittbandit.
The movement of government officials, the armed forces, traders, and people to plant palm seeds on both sides of the road along the Cambodia-Laos border has reached 180,000, equivalent to 90 kilometers.
* Third: Strengthening security, public order and social security:
Implement measures to crack down on all kinds of crimes, including crimes of natural resources, forests, land, fishing, wildlife, drugs, illegal cross-border crime, human trafficking and theft, robbery, illegal gambling, etc. Implement the plan of safe village, commune policy and community security movement through the participation of local people.
Implement education and dissemination measures on compliance with road traffic laws and protection of road safety and order, as well as the elimination of illegal checkpoints. Organize the construction of 34 commune / sangkat administrative police stations. At present, the commune / sangkat administrative police stations have strong and suitable buildings in 21 communes / sangkats and are continuously improving 13 communes / sangkats.
* Fourth: Promotion of agriculture and agro-industry:
* Fifth: Improving livelihoods and addressing people's requests:
Samaki Stung Treng Market, more than 9,000 square meters with a total of 1,286 booths donated by Samdech Techo Prime Minister and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, was built to solve the difficulties of 623 affected stallholders. Due to the fire at Stung Treng Stone Market in April 2016.
Resolving the compensation policy from the Lower Sesan 2 dam development project in 6 villages of 3 communes in Sesan district with 860 families equal to 3,960 affected people. Currently, the settlement is almost 100 percent complete, with only a handful of families remaining.
Systematic and separate land registration for local people reached 24,500 plots. Expansion of the electricity network to the living quarters of the people. At present, households have access to electricity increased by about 50%, equivalent to more than 16,000 households across the province.
Establish 20 ecotourism resorts in the Mekong, Sekong, Sesan, Srepok and indigenous communities.
Resolved 58 land disputes, equal to 1,449 families, with the satisfaction of the people and is continuing to resolve 3 more cases.
Expand the supply of clean water for people to use in towns, cities and districts, which currently has the Water Supply Authority in Stung Treng City and in some communes, there are currently 9 community water networks. In 2021, the province will have a water treatment plant that can supply 12,000 cubic meters of water per day, a development investment project of the Asian Development Bank.
* Sixth: Promote and develop health, hygiene, environment, education:
Strengthen and expand the infrastructure of the health sector, a provincial hospital building, a total of 14 health centers and 3 new health posts, as of 2015 in the province, there are only 7 health centers. In the province, there is a health secondary school for the training of human resources for intermediate and primary health care professionals for the Northeast region, with an average of 180 medical students per generation.
Build education infrastructure at all levels, which currently has 1,299 schools at all levels, equivalent to 4,538 classrooms, including 60 school buildings donated by Samdech Techo Prime Minister and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, equivalent to 367 classrooms; 7 offices equal to 21 rooms.
* 7th: Strengthening governance and institutional development
Prepared to build a master plan for land use of municipalities and districts, achieved 1 master plan for Stung Treng city, is continuing the procedure in 2 districts and prepares 3 more local studies.
Construction of commune / sangkat administration buildings was completed in all 34 communes / sangkats. As of 2015, only 17 communes / sangkats have administrative buildings according to technical standards. Municipal, district and administrative buildings in accordance with the standards of 3 out of 6 municipalities, districts and provincial unit buildings and 4 OWSOs.
Organizing 462 positions, roles and responsibilities of civil servants in provincial administrations, departments, units around provinces, municipalities and districts according to the legal documents. Develop human resource capacity as provincial, municipal, district and commune civil servants on a regular basis each year, with an average of 15 training sessions per year, equivalent to 1,200 people.
