(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. Neth Vantha, Director of the Fire Prevention and Extinguishing Department of the Ministry of Interior, said that in the first six months of 2020, the number of fires increased 266 times from the previous year.
This statement was made on the occasion that he was invited to co-lead the organization of large-scale firefighting training 2020 of Aeon Mall Phnom Penh (Aeon 1) this morning, June 23, 2020.
He said that the problem that caused the fire was caused by three factors, including: 41% electricity, 39% electricity consumption and 20% can not grasp the cause. The fire brigade carried out 573 operations using 1,238 vehicles, equivalent to 5,392 cubic meters, and local authorities responded 11 times in a timely manner, while 50 cases were out of control.
