Wild animals in the forest, Sang Ruk Vorn found dead in a row, two more deer died by hunting
(Phnom Penh): Two deer were found dead and rotting in the Sangkha Ruk Vorn forest in Oddar Meanchey province, suspected of being shot by a hunter. The Ministry of Environment has expressed its deepest condolences for the loss of these two rare animals.
According to a release from the Ministry of Environment, the bodies of the two deer were found on June 22, 2020 by monks while inspecting the forest.
After receiving the information from the monks, the park rangers at Phnom Andong and Rong Dek headquarters went down to the scene immediately. The deer was presumed to have been shot by a hunter and died six to seven days ago. The team, together with the monks, prepared to send the bodies of the two deer to be buried.
Please note that Sang Ruk Voan Community Forest covers more than 30 hectares in 3 districts, including: Samrong, Chongkal and Anlong Veng districts. This forest is classified as a protected forest and protected by a sub-decree of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Sang Ruk Voan Community Forest has been handed over by the Royal Government to Venerable Bun Salout to organize a campaign to protect forests and wildlife in Anlong Veng district from the encroachment of loggers, hunters, wildlife and aquatic animals, as well as illegal mining. And so on.
Sangkh Rok Voan Community Forest contains many species of wildlife and biodiversity. In recent times, despite efforts by monks and Ministry of Environment officials, many rare animals in the forest have been affected by poachers.
