(Phnom Penh): Mr. Hing Sideth, Director General of the General Department of Vocational Technical Education and Training (TVET), stated that the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training is currently preparing a policy request from the Royal Government to apply for permission to reopen the factory. More than that, laboratories at technical and vocational education and training institutions.
He stated that the request to reopen, keeping the social gap, hygiene and adhere to the guidelines of the Ministry of Health.
Speaking in an interview with Fresh News' "Weekly Special Guest", Hing Sideth confirmed that the ministry's request was made because technical and vocational training focused on practical application and that the skills were acquired. Through practical work in a workshop or laboratory.
"On the other hand, the current situation is that the number of trainees studying at technical and vocational education and training institutions is small, which makes it easier to organize social and sanitary gaps during their actual work in the factory," he said. "Labs, labs, proficiency tests and final exams are different from general education schools, which have a large number of students."
However, for technical and vocational education and training, distance learning or online training has also been introduced, with the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training continuing to implement systematic training. Training remotely or online (theoretical study) and for practical application, the Ministry will ask the head of the Royal Government for permission to reopen.
