Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng: Mutual Assistance Will Strengthen Cambodia-China Relations
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, stated that the mutual assistance between Cambodia and China will further strengthen the bilateral relations between the two countries. As the two governments stand shoulder to shoulder in defending the 19 Kovid virus.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng made this remark on the occasion that he allowed Mr. Wang Vinthean, Ambassador of the People's Republic of China to Cambodia, to pay a courtesy call and hand over 19 items of Kovid vaccination equipment of the Ministry of Security. Of the People's Republic of China at the Ministry of Interior on June 22, 2020.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng thanked the Ministry of Public Security of the People's Republic of China and the Government of China for their continued support of Cambodia, both the Government of the Party and the Ministry of Public Security, for their continued support of Cambodia and the Ministry of Interior. Cambodia as much as possible.
Prince Sar Kheng thanked and congratulated the Chinese government on its efforts to achieve a glorious victory in the prevention of Kovid 19 and said that the materials provided by the Chinese friends are very real. Demonstrate care and consideration to come to Cambodia as a friend to participate in the fight against Kovid 19.
Through the Ambassador, the Prince also thanked the leadership of the Ministry of Public Security of the People's Republic of China for its continued attention to help strengthen and expand the relationship between the Ministry of Public Security of China and the Ministry of Interior of Cambodia in particular. In the field of security.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also expressed his hope that through the spirit of mutual support, this will contribute to further strengthening the relationship and cooperation between the two institutions, as well as between the government and the people of both countries. Second, on behalf of the leadership of the Ministry of Interior, the Prince is always ready to provide cooperation with the Chinese side and the Chinese Embassy in support of various matters under the Ministry.
At the same time, Mr. Wang Winthean thanked the Deputy Prime Minister and brought greetings from the Chinese leadership and Mr. Zhao Kerjie, Minister of Public Security of the People's Republic of China to the Crown Prince.
He said that despite the outbreak of Kovid 19, relations and cooperation between the two countries continue to function normally and continue to improve, especially reflected through the contributions of the King of Cambodia and Samdech Techo Director. Ministers to support the resources contributing to the fight against this infectious disease when the disease first started.
Wang Wentian said that the materials handed over to the Ministry of Interior at this time, although not a large number, but he agreed with the prince's statement that the material aid shows the spirit of the Chinese people and the Ministry of Public Security of the Republic. Chinese people to the people and the Ministry of Interior of Cambodia.
Wang Winthean recalled that over the past year, law enforcement cooperation between the two countries has been improved, although the two countries are fighting Kovid 19. Achieving this good result, he would also like to thank the leadership of Prince Kralahom in this work.
He hopes that the good cooperation between the two countries' law enforcement forces will serve the common interests of the people and the two countries in the field of security in the future.
Please note that the 19 Kovid protective equipment donated by the Ministry of Public Security to the Ministry of Interior of Cambodia on this occasion includes 500 sets of medical glasses, 10,000 pairs of medical gloves, 10,000 KN95 masks, 50,000 medical masks and 500 sets of medical protective clothing. The equipment costs about 600,000 yuan ($ 85,000).
