SEC signs MoU with Chinese company on consultation and technical support for Cambodian market development in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): This morning, June 22, 2020, the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia signed a Memorandum of Understanding between
The Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia and Rui Feng Than Fu Investment Co., Ltd. on "Consultation and Technical Support for the Development of the Commodity Market in Cambodia".
Commodities Market Development is a wholesale market for financial and non-financial products associated with the futures market (selling futures products now. Example: Sell 10 tons of rice now, but the rice will be harvested later 6 more months).
In addition, the presence of this market will help attract foreign investors, link the Cambodian market to the world market, which will help improve the Cambodian trade balance, promote the agro-industrial sector, which can boost production and production. In domestic production and for export, these will also help reduce unemployment in Cambodia and reduce poverty, as highlighted just now.
Mr. Chin Sin said that the signing of the MoU with the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia on this occasion, because the two countries have comprehensive strategic cooperation, promoting the one-way belt policy, so his company will establish a model business in Asia. Southeast and promote the Cambodian market to become an international market, creating a prominent market and hundreds of ways.
He said that to increase and deepen cooperation with the Royal Government of Cambodia and enterprises in these key areas to provide support and contribute to economic development and increase employment for the people of Cambodia to achieve the principles and cooperation. A win-win operation between Cambodia and China.
