Police said that before the incident, two women, the mother of the child, rode a motorcycle in a taxi with two people on their way back from the provincial referral hospital, which took the child to examine and treat the injuries caused by the traffic accident last year. Two to three days ago, when he arrived at the scene, a bulldozer driven by 14-year-old Tem Saroeun, a resident of the commune, turned onto the red gravel road.
