Russian President Vladimir Putin has said he will run in the next presidential election if a constitutional amendment allows him to run for re-election. He did so in the referendum. This was released by CNN on Monday, June 22, 2020.
Under the current Russian constitution, Putin is required to step down in 2024, when his term expires as president. But amendments to the constitution are expected to pave the way for him to remain in power until 2036. The amendment to the constitution has already been approved by the Russian parliament and Supreme Court, but has yet to go through a referendum.
"I have not yet made any decision and I have not ruled out the possibility," Putin said in an interview on Sunday. "That is, if the constitution allows or provides opportunities, we will all see."
Russia will hold a referendum on constitutional amendments on July 1, and if approved, Putin could run in the 2024 presidential election.
