Spokesman for the General Commission: On June 22, another 857 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, within 53 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to June 22, 2020, the traffic police nationwide inspected And fined a total of 72,586 vehicles, including 53,220 motorcycles and 19,366 vehicles of all types.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that during the 53 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine the offending vehicles went well.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment, who led a group of journalists to wildlife sanctuaries in Preah Vihear and Kampong Thom provinces recently, said that there are a total of 119 vultures in wildlife sanctuaries across Cambodia. There were 11 fire vultures, 71 gray vultures and 37 brown vultures.
Mr. Net Pheaktra said that the results of the vulture census in 2019 showed that Cambodia has 137 vultures, compared to 2020, a decrease of 18 and the area with the most vultures is in the border. Siem Pang Wildlife Sanctuary in Stung Treng Province and Chep Wildlife Sanctuary in Preah Vihear Province.
The presence of these three species of vultures has attracted a large number of foreign tourists and provided eco-tourism benefits to the community on a regular basis, including the Dangplit Natural Resource Conservation Community in the Chep Wildlife Sanctuary. This eco-tourism service is also available. This community is located in Russey Trip commune, Cheb district, Preah Vihear province.
The team waited patiently until almost 8 o'clock before a few crows came down to eat the carcass of the cow, which is about 200 meters from the factory. After a while, the brown vultures, the majority and the vultures, came down to eat the delicacies for the census day, then the vultures, the minority, flew down after the vultures with caution. Than other vultures.
The team's camera took pictures of each of them with great joy, while the census team tried to focus their attention through the animal scanner or telescope to carefully count the number of rare animals in our homeland.
Despite the delicacy of the food, the vultures seem to be wary of the surroundings. After a while, the food healed, the stomach was full, and the vulture stopped hovering near the project. The census team also counted 34 vultures, including three fire vultures, nine gray vultures and 22 brown vultures in the Chep district wildlife sanctuary.
Mr. Nong Ruon, a resident of Dangplit Natural Resource Protection Community, said that the community was established in 2004 on an area of 2,400 hectares, and in 2008 the community added additional ecotourism services to earn additional income from the project. Non-timber forest products, farming and animal husbandry.
For foreign visitors to the wildlife in the Dang Phlit community, they have to pay for the purchase of cow carcasses from the villagers to feed the vultures, with a cow costing between 1,600,000 riel and 2,000,000 riel. In addition, guests pay $ 10 for food, $ 8 for chefs, $ 10 for tour guides and other accommodation services.
It should be informed that the conservation activities of natural resources and ecotourism activities in Dang Phlit community are also supported by USAID Prey Lang Baitong project. Forest patrols help communicate with the tourism market, tour operators to bring tourists to visit the wildlife in the community and so on.
Mr. Chhit Sam Ath, Director of Prey Lang Baitong Project, continued that Prey Lang Baitong Project is still cooperating with the Ministry of Environment and Dang Phlit Community and will continue to support patrol equipment so that the conservation of natural resources can continue to be sustainable, especially to encourage people. The community can carry out all this work on their own when the project expires.
Chhit Sam Ath also warned that when wildlife sanctuaries are lost, wildlife could be lost later, and when there are no forests, it is clear that tourists will have no tourism products to visit. No more visiting here until then, people will lose income from this tourism service for sure.
