Minister Mam Bunheng stated, "In order to improve the management of our patients and doctors' history more easily, quickly, efficiently and accurately, today the Ministry has launched the Smart Hospital digital hospital system at Preah Ang Duong Hospital." The first in Cambodia and the next will be in other hospitals across the country.
"With this digital system, patients can make an appointment with a doctor at any time and without having to wait long or miss an appointment," he said. In addition, the system will automatically remind you when to see a doctor and get information from the Ministry of Health.
The health information app on mobile phones and digital card lift will make it easier for patients to get to know their past medical history and take it to the hospital without the hassle of keeping and fearing losing documents and taking a long time. Talk to your doctor.
At the same time, Professor Lou Ly Kheang, Director of Ang Duong Hospital, said, "Smart Hospital is very useful and convenient, as patients can make an appointment with a doctor and remind them of their appointments and their medical history." For doctors, it is also easy to speed up the extra work to manage the history of all patients.
(Banteay Meanchey): Mr. Oum Rath, Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, will meet with the Governor of Sa Kaeo Province, Thailand tomorrow morning, June 23, 2020 to propose the reopening of Poipet-Khlong Leuk International Port (name of Thai side) after closing. Entered for a while due to Kovid 19.
According to a letter from the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Administration, which submitted a request to the Thai side on June 17, 2020, to meet at the Aranyaprathet District Customs Office in Sa Kaeo Province to open the Poipet-Khlong Leuk International Border Gate. .
It should be informed that the Poipet International Gate was decided by the Cambodian and Thai sides to temporarily close all entrances and exits except for the traffic of trucks to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 disease.
The Minister of Tourism and the Governor of Siem Reap continue to promote the implementation of tourism safety measures to ensure that Siem Reap is a safe tourist destination
(Siem Reap): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Mr. Tea Seiha, Governor of Siem Reap Province, on June 22, 2020, held a meeting to review the implementation of legal regulations for the implementation of tourism safety rules (Step 1) for businesses. Six tours during the Kovid-19 epidemic crisis to tour operators and tour operators at Siem Reap Provincial Hall.
Minister Thong Khon stated that in the current situation, the necessary implementation of some necessary safety measures in daily life and socio-economic activities such as hygiene and sanitation, food security and safety gap should be encouraged. .
In particular, in the field of tourism, new business models need to be considered to adapt to the actual socio-economic situation, in which businesses can implement digital solutions through the use of technology as an aid and need to strengthen capacity and quality, especially increase productivity to be ready. Already, for sharper competition, the market is narrower and the supply chain is shorter.
The five additional recommendations of Minister Thong Khon to the Siem Reap Provincial Administration for further implementation include:
* First, request the Siem Reap Provincial Administration to strengthen the management of tourism businesses by focusing on two main points: Require tour operators to arrange for the measurement of heat, spraying alcohol, hand washing for all entry and exit of business locations, or if additional arrangements. Having an automation machine for the above tasks is even better, requiring everyone passing through the business location to register or provide an absolute identity.
* Second: For land and waterway tourism transportation services, please request the Siem Reap Provincial Administration to strengthen the implementation of maintaining the safety gap, especially when queuing for tickets and when traveling and maintaining the safety gap can be through the cut. Reduce storage capacity.
* Third: For tourism resorts and tourism communities, request the Siem Reap Provincial Administration to advise all relevant departments to carry out this work together, with the Department of Tourism as a specialized staff.
* Fourth: Request the Siem Reap Provincial Administration to compile statistics on employees working in the tourism industry and to cooperate with the Department of Tourism Vocational Training to gather all these staff to receive the necessary training.
* Fifth, I would like to ask all the private sector in the tourism sector to understand and join together with the Royal Government of Cambodia in its efforts to overcome this difficult stage.
He added that the introduction of tourism safety rules is not for the purpose of restricting the performance of tour operators, especially in order to maintain the confidence of national and international tourists in the quality of services in line with the slogan "Your safety. It is our duty ”in line with the New Normal Life trends.
Mr. Thong Khon also reminded the Siem Reap Provincial Administration to continue to develop infrastructure in the city, to promote clean and green campaigns, and to ask the private sector and all stakeholders in the tourism sector to promote and implement the measures of the Royal Government, the Ministry of Health and the Ministry of Tourism. To prevent, protect and maintain safety, trust and provide comfort to tourists traveling to Siem Reap.
A woman died in a fire in a hut guarding a plantation in Samaki Meanchey district, Kampong Chhnang province.
(Kampong Chhnang): A shocking case occurred on the night of June 21, 2020 in a plantation hut where a woman's body was found lying near the ashes of a fire, with part of her body on fire. The upper bouts featured two cutaways, for easier access to the higher frets.
