* History of the White House
During the 19th century, the White House became a symbol of American democracy. In the minds of most Americans, the White House is not a presidential office, but a temporary office and residence where the president serves the people.
The "White House" has a total of more than 130 rooms. The main building still houses the residence of the same presidential family, along with a variety of living rooms, all decorated in 18th and 19th century styles. Parts of the main building are open to the public.
The White House is now one of the most important historical sites in the United States, attracting more than 1.5 million visitors each year. The White House is part of the American National Park System in Washington, D.C., and was recognized as a museum in 1988.
The assertion of Samdech Techo Prime Minister was made this morning, Monday, June 22, 2020, on the occasion of Samdech inspecting the construction site of the new Phnom Penh International Airport in Prek Sleng commune, Kandal Steung district, Kandal province.
