The perpetrator who drove the RX400h with fake license plate hit the police was arrested and sent to court
(Phnom Penh): A young man who drove a RX400h car with a fake license plate was arrested by the Phnom Penh Municipal Police Traffic Police and sent to court for legal action on June 21, 2020. .
The Information and Quick Reaction Team of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police told Fresh News that the perpetrator, Puth Monorom, did not listen to the traffic police at the construction site, was constructing a road at the Chom Chao roundabout and was driving at high speed. Caused a traffic officer to fall. After research and inspection, it was found that the perpetrator used the wrong license plate by wearing another license plate.
The perpetrator was charged with three different points, firstly, obstructing the authorities while performing the work, secondly, using a fake license plate (wearing a different license plate) and thirdly fleeing the scene. Hence in order to avoid responsibility.
On the afternoon of June 21, 2020 at 2:00 pm, the perpetrator was prepared by the Phnom Penh Road Traffic Police Office and sent to court to follow legal procedures. Kratie City Police Cracked Down on Cockfighting Locations and Seized Many Artifacts While Gambling Addicts Flee
