Mr. Sun Chanthol: Officials must connect with the people to meet the needs of the people
(Kandal): In addition to his leadership and management role at the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol was also assigned by the Royal Government to chair the Royal Government Working Group to assist Koh Thom district. In this role, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol has the main task to help develop the locality of Koh Thom district, solve problems and help improve the lives of people in Koh Thom district.
Almost every weekend, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol leads his team to Koh Thom district and travels through the villages of the people to visit and find out about the problems and needs of the people.
On June 21, 2020, the Minister, who received much praise for the work of leading and managing the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, continued to lead his subordinates to visit people in Chroy Takeo and Chheu Khmao communes, Koh Thom district. Kandal Province.
Just like last week, visiting the local people, Mr. Sun Chanthol and his officials chose bicycles as a means of riding in the villages of the people. While riding a bicycle in the village, the Minister, who is also a native of Koh Thom district, was always greeted by the people.
Mr. Sun Chanthol said that cycling to meet and greet people creates a friendly atmosphere that creates a good connection between officials and people. He added that cycling in all directions also made him and officials more aware of the living conditions and living conditions of the people.
In addition to visiting residents at home, Mr. Sun Chanthol's field trip also organized a get-together and give some gifts to the people. During the meeting, Mr. Sun Chanthol presented the people about the efforts of the Royal Government led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen to lead and serve the nation.
Mr. Sun Chanthol also mentioned some of the national difficulties caused by Kovid 19 disease. Mr. Sun Chanthol said that the Royal Government, headed by Samdech Techo, has made great efforts to solve the crisis caused by this disease.
Mr. Sun Chanthol asked the people about the difficulties caused by this virus. However, the Senior Minister affirmed that the Royal Government will make every effort to ensure the well-being of the people and lead the country through this difficult obstacle.
Mr. Sun Chanthol also reminded people to continue to pay attention to health care and be very careful about the spread of Kovid 19. He said that this global epidemic should not be underestimated, as Kovid 19 has not yet disappeared from the planet.
The Minister reminded the people to continue to take care of their health by following the rules of the Ministry of Health and not to be negligent.
During the visit, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol distributed scarves, masks, alcohol and hand soap to about 400 families in 20 villages in Chroy Takeo and Chheu Khmao communes, Koh Thom district.
Mr. Sun Chanthol called his activities with local officials as a way of connecting life with the people. He said that as officials with the duty to serve the nation and the people, going to the grassroots is to help see clearly the concerns and needs of the people. Kampong Speu Provincial Department of Commerce Holds Two-Day Trade Fair to Promote AIMS Project and Promote Khmer Agricultural Products
