(Kampong Thom): Under the leadership of the head of the Royal Government, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Cambodia has made progress in all areas after the political victory, with infrastructure everywhere being built from the city to the countryside.
However, Kampong Thom province has developed and constructed road infrastructure as a project to improve rural roads from red gravel to double-decker pavement (DBST) with the assistance of the Asian Development Bank (ADB) to the countryside as a battle zone between Cambodian troops. Red and government troops, the most difficult place for the people.
Mr. Mom Cham, Director of Kampong Thom Provincial Department of Rural Development, said that Kampong Thom province under the leadership of Mr. Sok Lou, the provincial governor, has built a 122-kilometer-long 400-meter road, which is divided into four lines, the first line is more than 40 kilometers long. Meters from Banteay Stong commune, Stong district to O Angkor village, Prasat Balang district.
The second line is more than 20 km long from Ta Ok village, Prasat Sambo district to Ngon village, Ngon commune, Sandan district. The third line is more than 20 km long from National Road No. 6 from Ta Ream village, Tbeng commune, Kampong Svay district to Smoh village, Phan Nhem commune, Prasat Balang district, and the fourth line is 33 km long from National Road No. 62, Sala commune. Sector to Kraya commune in Prasat Balong district.
He said that all these roads have been built since 2018 and will be completed by the end of 2020, with a back width of 8 meters and a pavement of 6 meters.
At the same time, Mr. Mom Cham requested all people to help maintain cooperation and participate together, especially those who live on the national road, do not throw garbage or other waste on the road or in the mouth. Drainage, which causes water blockage when it rains, pours soil higher than the road and does not overload.
The people who live on the streets as well as the people who have traveled are very happy with the quick and easy access to the road, which used to be difficult to travel by cart and flooded. There are also requests to other people to help maintain and not to be overweight to use the road for a long time.
