Minister of Tourism announces to help develop Teuk Chob Khnar Po community to become an attractive eco-tourism community
(Siem Reap): On the occasion of meeting with the community of Teuk Chub Khnar Po ecotourism in Khnar Po commune, Sot Nikum district, this morning, June 21, 2020, Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, announced to the community that he will help develop This community to become a model ecotourism community in Siem Reap.
Mr. Thong Khon further stated that in the past, within the framework of the inter-ministerial working group, the Ministry of Tourism has cooperated with the Ministry of Environment, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and other stakeholders to help organize the management and development of some ecotourism and ecotourism communities. These tourism communities have become role models not only at the national, regional and global levels.
These communities include: Chi Phat Ecotourism Community in Chi Phat Commune, Chhay Areng District, Thmar Bang District, Koh Kong Province, and Koh Trong Tourism Community, Kratie Province, Kampong Phluk Tourism Community in Siem Reap Province, Banteay Chhmar Tourism Community, Banteay Meanchey Province, Mlup Baitong Ecotourism Community, Kampong Speu Province.
Minister Thong Khon added that the inclusion of a responsible tourism activity could help generate additional income for the community if the community knows how to sustain and jointly take advantage of the forest. All of that by preparing to become a tourist destination, providing good tourism services, hospitality, especially safety measures, tourism, hygiene, clean environment in the context of the Covid-19 phase.
Mr. Thong Khon added that for the challenges of the community water ecotourism, such as the difficulty of access to the community, telephone service, internet, electricity, garbage use and so on. He will ask the relevant institutions to help solve this problem as well. Separately, for the very difficult 3 km road, the Ministry of Tourism will help repair it first.
It should be noted that the forest ecotourism community of Teuk Chob Khnar Po area is bordered on the north by Tbeng commune, Banteay Srei district, on the south by Chan Sar commune and on the west by Kantraing commune, Prasat Bakong district, on the east by Popel commune. The commune consists of 8 villages north of National Road 6, about 8 km from the national road and about 30 km from the provincial town of Siem Reap.
Khnar Po Community Forest was established in 1998 with the consent and consent of the people in all villages of Khnar Po Commune, Sot Nikum District and under the management of the Forestry Administration of the Ministry of Agriculture and Forestry. Fishing.
The community forest covers a total area of 1,022 hectares, including about 90 hectares of mangrove forest, which has the potential to create an attractive new tourist attraction for Siem Reap.
