CPP's luxurious headquarters building completed
(Phnom Penh): The new building of the luxurious headquarters of the Cambodian People's Party has been completed after more than two years of construction.
On the morning of June 21, 2020, Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, Vice President of the Cambodian People's Party and Secretary General of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP), signed an agreement to receive building achievements from a group of builders.
The new presence of the CPP headquarters will be an important venue for the party, which is leading the Royal Government and is highly responsible for the fate of the nation and the people of Cambodia.
The groundbreaking ceremony for the new building of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) headquarters was held on November 11, 2018. The building is 150 meters long, 74 meters wide, the height of the building in front of the public square to the top of the diamond is 48 meters high. The ground floor has more than 500 parking spaces and a front yard for public parking for 300 cars. Upstairs is a public meeting hall for about 10,000 people.
The building has five floors, with a 3,000-square-meter hospitality hall that can seat more than 4,000 people, and a cafeteria on the south side of the building that can seat 120 people at a time. .
The architects of the building point out that it was built under a new style called contemporary style due to the combination of three styles. The three styles are: 1) Angkor Wat style, 2) Banteay Srei style and 3) Kandal style. The combination of these three styles is called "contemporary style".
