Letter to readers: Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Guide to Peace of Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): War is easy to create but only to end the war, which is difficult Women, wine and power. Contrary to the war veterans who sacrificed all kinds of sacrifices, even life and happiness with their wives, children, families.
Despite the lack of encouragement from the Cambodian people 100%, a Cambodian peace guide who gave his life to save Cambodian lives and to be the guide to end the war, he relentlessly fulfilled his role to untie the knot. This war successfully ended the war.
As the son of a farmer, he was educated in a pagoda and decided to enter the jungle to take up arms against the Sihanouk movement. Countless jealousies. This is the normal life of a revolutionary, where no revolutionary is started, there are people who love it or there are people who hate it.
From Comrade Hun Sen to Mr. Hun Sen, His Excellency Hun Sen to the present day, Samdech Hun Sen, known to the world as the strong man of Cambodia, now he (Hun Sen) deserves another historical title from the institution. The National Assembly, the institution representing the people, is the title of the "Guide to Peace in Cambodia."
We still remember that after the Paris Peace Agreement of October 23, 1991, the Khmer Rouge did not implement this agreement and went to the polls in 1993. The one who was able to separate the political and military forces of the Khmer Rouge and was able to lead the integration of the Khmer Rouge military forces and the people to return to live under the same constitution after 1998 was Samdech Hun Sen.
All of these reasons are due to the fact that Samdech Hun Sen, former Vice President of the Cambodian People's Party, now President of the Cambodian People's Party, is most apt to receive the honor of the National Assembly as the "Guide to Peace of Cambodia."
War is easy to create, but the end of war is not easy to end if war is born. From a young age, from Comrade Hun Sen to His Excellency Hun Sen to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, in order to preserve and protect the peace achievements that Samdech sacrificed and brought, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has strictly implemented a rule according to the French proverb. "If you want to keep the peace, be prepared for war," he said.
