This is according to the intervention of Mr. An Sok Khoeun in the continuation of the 43rd session of the Human Rights Council in the general discussion on the 10th agenda on technical assistance and capacity building on June 19, 2020 in Geneva.
Mr. An Sok Khoeun's intervention in continuing the 43rd session of the Human Rights Council has five contents:
2: Like many other delegations mentioned earlier, Cambodia maintains the view that technical cooperation must be determined and decided based on the needs of the relevant states and must be linked to the country's national goals and priorities, taking into account its characteristics. And state ownership. The importance of the state's role in implementing human rights obligations should be respected in this process.
4: In the context of the Kovid 19 epidemic, discussions on this topic should be conducted with caution, with an emphasis on sharing the best of life-saving efforts and avoiding politicalization on human rights issues if we Want to ensure the credibility and effectiveness of human rights mechanisms. Cambodia opposes unilateral measures by one state against another under the label of technical assistance.
Finally, Cambodia values multilateral partnership through constructive and mutually respectful dialogue to enhance the quality of technical cooperation and practical human rights standards.
