Nearly 10 years of land dispute in Ksem Ksan commune gives the authorities a headache, but the actual land occupants have lost the case, Kampong Speu provincial authorities still support and claim that the losers are still the owners
(Kampong Speu): A land dispute of more than 1 hectare in Talak village (formerly Trapeang Kanseng village), Ksem Ksan commune, Oudong district, Kampong Speu province, lasted for almost 10 years until it was filed in court from the provincial court until Supreme Court.
However, the Kampong Speu provincial authorities and relevant officials in the province still support the losing party in the three levels of court that they are still the real landowners who are actually occupying the land. The winner is not the landowner.
The above-mentioned 1-hectare agricultural land dispute occurred between Mr. Duong Choeun, a police officer in Kampong Speu province (the party lost the case in court but actually occupied the land) and Mr. Vong Chay (the party won the case in court but did not Yes, actually occupy the land) who is a resident of Phnom Penh.
Suddenly, during the same year, Mr. Vong Chay (land mortgagor from Mr. Chap Theary) filed a lawsuit in Kampong Speu Provincial Court and was sentenced by the court to be able to win and become the owner of this land, but then Mr. Duong Choeun did not run out. Chet also appealed to the Court of Appeal, but the Court of Appeal upheld the decision of the Provincial Court.
Undeterred, Mr. Duong Choeun appealed to the Supreme Court and was dismissed by the High Court on September 2, 2019. After the Supreme Court ruled in favor of Mr. Vong Chay, on June 16, 2020, he went down to lock the fence and use machinery to clear the land without the participation of provincial court officials. And professional officers to follow the procedure, which is completely illegal.
The purpose of going down to clear the land and wanting to occupy the actual land was because Mr. Vong Chay believed Mr. Mang Nan, a Udong district land officer, and had a conspiracy from a clerk officer to run a letter that means "storage". Equivalent to the protection order to lie to Mr. Vong Chay to use the machine to clear the land without notifying the authorities and the owner of the land by requesting to implement the verdict in accordance with this legal form.
On September 10, 2018, the Kampong Speu Provincial Administration issued a notification on the public posting of judgment documents or so-called systematic measurements to citizens, in which Mr. Duong Choeun has already registered the plot. There is plot number 296 with the approval of all relevant authorities.
On April 18, 2019, Mr. Tith Yan, Chief of Talak Village, with the approval of the Chief of Ksem Ksan Commune, wrote a letter to the President of the Supreme Court stating that the land belonged to Hong Muy Lang (wife of Mr. Duong Choeun) who managed to build a fence every season, never stopped reading.
Finally, Mr. Duong Choeun said that he was consulting with a lawyer to file a lawsuit in court in case of damage to his property.
