Please be informed that the Ministry of National Defense on June 20, 2020 organized a ceremony to commemorate the 43rd anniversary of the day Samdech Techo Hun Sen and his comrades left Cambodia in search of national liberation from the genocidal regime of Paul. Pot.
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Kun Kim expressed his gratitude and remembrance for the heroism of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and his comrades in the struggle to use life as a capital for the liberation of the nation and the people of Cambodia from the dead. The genocidal regime 43 years ago.
This senior official of the Royal Government of Cambodia said that every generation of Cambodians must be engraved in their hearts immortally the brave heroism of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and his comrades.
June 20, 1977 is the date of a new historical record for the Cambodian nation, in which five Cambodian patriotic warriors decide to use their lives as capital, risking tens of thousands of chapters and dangers to seek the liberation of the nation and the Cambodian people from the clutches. Death under the genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
The four brave warriors were Comrade Hun Sen and four other loyal comrades, including: Nuch Thorn, Nhek Huon, San Sanh, and Va Po Ean. The decision to leave Cambodia for Vietnam in search of the overthrow of the genocidal regime of Pol Pot left the five fighters in a state of mental immeasurability. Especially Hun Sen fighters.
Starting out, the great sacrifices of Hun Sen and his four comrades, as well as many other Cambodian patriots, saved the lives of the nation and the entire Cambodian people by overthrowing the genocidal regime. Pol Pot was completely overthrown on January 7, 1979.
For Kun Kim, without the dangerous decision and great sacrifice of Samdech Techo Hun Sen on June 20, 1977, it would continue to be under the control of the genocidal regime and suppress all freedoms. Yang of Pol Pot.
"Clearly, without the courage to rise up, fight and risk one's life for such dangers, the Pol Pot genocidal regime would never have collapsed," he said. "Without the overthrow, it is certain that the genocidal regime of Pol Pot is still present and the lives of millions of Cambodians will continue to die and never receive such a light of freedom."
Starting from the struggle of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and his comrades and patriots, just ended the regime of slaughter, starvation, and suppression of Pol Pot's brutal rights and freedoms. This struggle also brought an end to the war, unified the nation and provided an opportunity for nation-building to bring about the glorious national progress as it is today.
Senior Minister Kun Kim highlighted that the gift of saving lives from the abyss of hell is the greatest gift that can not be measured and priceless.
Senior Minister Kun Kim emphasized that the spirit of devotion and devotion to the nation and people of Samdech Techo Hun Sen is also a heroic example and a message to raise the memory of every Cambodian child to always remember for the cause of the nation and the people. Under any circumstances, even life dares to sacrifice.
The ceremony took place in the area of historical traces of the starting point of the struggle in Koh Thmor village, Tonlong commune, Memot district, Tbong Khmum province. The ceremony was presided over by Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Defense, and was attended by Vietnamese Ambassadors to Cambodia as well as military attachés of various countries in Cambodia.
Starting from the great sacrifice of Hun Sen and his comrades 43 years ago, which is the greatest cause to bring the nation and the people of Cambodia to the light of progress and beauty as today.
Many questions have been raised as to what the nation and the people of Cambodia would be like without all the sacrifices and the freedom to live and study as it is today. That both the United Nations and the United States supported Pol Pot's Democratic Kampuchea regime and did not see their brutal genocide?
Khmer historians see that without the start of the struggle of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and patriotic Khmer dignitaries to rise up to liberate the nation, the nation and the people of Cambodia have no chance of escaping the deadly regime of Pol Pot. No.
During the late 1970s, Cambodians across the country were waiting for a specific, strong leadership movement to overthrow the genocidal regime of Pol Pot. Without a locomotive and no real armed forces, the resistance movement would be ruthlessly destroyed by the genocide.
Location: Koh Thmor, Tonlong Commune, Memot District, Tbong Khmum Province, Area 21, 21:00, June 20, 1977 Four of them, Nuch Thorn, Nhek Huon, San Sanh, and Vapo Ian, began fleeing to Vietnam in search of support for national liberation from the Pol Pot genocidal regime.
After traveling through the forest in Vietnam for about 6 km, at 11:00 a.m., Comrade Hun Sen spotted a dirt road paved with red stones, decided to hide his weapons and prepare porridge with the remaining rice. In a small hand, then continue on the road to meet the army and the Vietnamese people.
Why did the comrades decide to travel without carrying weapons? This is a wise consideration, as long as there are people carrying weapons across the border, the Vietnamese Defense Forces or guerrillas can immediately explode their weapons, the lives of comrades and groups can not be guaranteed.
After beginning to believe some of Comrade Hun Sen's assertion that it was not Pol Pot's raid group, the Vietnamese side also cooked 10th grade rice and cooked for five people who had been eating porridge for more than a year. At 16:00 in June 1977, after eating, the five Cambodians were taken 4 km to Langjin village at 16:45.
The five Cambodians were again questioned there by a Vietnamese platoon commander. At 5:15 p.m., June 21, 1977, the five were transported in a GMC truck from Langjin Village to Lok Ninh District at 6:00 p.m.
After a hearty dinner of rice and vegetables, Comrade Hun Sen was separated from the four passengers who came with him and was again asked questions.
That was the most stressful time of all for the four people traveling with them, thinking that they could have killed Comrade Hun Sen or gone somewhere if they did not return. All four of them felt anxious, even though they were tired, could not sleep, could not breathe and waited until Comrade Hun Sen returned at more than midnight on June 22, 1977.
Due to the interrogation of information at all levels from the village, commune to district, the Vietnamese side clearly saw the strong will and decisive position of Comrade Hun Sen in the sharp aim is to mobilize forces. For the liberation of the motherland from the genocidal regime.
