Long-running land dispute between company and more than 500 families by Preah Vihear authorities could end soon
(Preah Vihear): A long-standing land dispute between the Economic Land Concession Company (Friendship Company) and more than 500 families that has lasted for many years has been resolved by the Preah Vihear Provincial Authority based on the principles of The Royal Government will be able to say that this solution will be completed soon.
An official from Preah Vihear Provincial Hall said on June 18, 2020 that the land dispute was started by migrants who illegally encroached on state forest land until a dispute arose. With professional officials and economic land concessions that the Royal Government has provided to private companies to invest in agricultural and agro-industrial crops.
The official said that on June 16, 2020, out of 546 families, many families received a compromise and settled 2 hectares of land per family from the Royal Government through the Preah Vihear provincial authorities. But only a small group of people, believing in the lure of brokers, refused to accept and went up to protest in Phnom Penh.
The official further stated that under the coordination of Preah Vihear provincial authorities, 546 families, most of them living in Trapeang Prasat district, Oddar Meanchey province, encroached on the forest land of Kulen-Prohm Tep Wildlife Sanctuary and the land of Friendship Company. So far, out of 546 families, many families have agreed to accept 2 hectares of land per family in accordance with the Royal Government's policy through the Preah Vihear Provincial Authority.
He stated that the social land concessions provided by the Royal Government through the provincial authorities to the 546 families at this time will require people to come and fill out the form to get land from illegal occupation to land. Within one month, they will receive a title deed and live and cultivate without fear and have all the rights five years after cultivating the 2 hectares of land.
Please be informed that several days ago, a small group of people who refused to accept 2 hectares of land according to the allocation of Preah Vihear provincial authorities went to protest in Phnom Penh, but the protest did not achieve its purpose. The provincial authorities will try to mediate only if the people return to accept 2 hectares of land as resolved by the Preah Vihear provincial leadership.
Oknha Dr. Chea Ratana Provides Funds to Expand the Business of People with Disabilities and Warns Not to Use Disabilities as an Obstacle
(Phnom Penh): On the occasion of the 10th meeting and funding to expand the business of both disabled people at the office of Sun & Moon Hotel on June 18, 2020, the owners of the Oknha Dr. Chea Ratana and Tycoon Ly Hiek Ratana Encourage all people with disabilities not to take disability as an obstacle, we do not want to struggle to become weak.
Oknha Dr. Chea Ratana continued, "Our fitness is disabled and there is nothing to fix it. However, we must not let our minds be disabled anymore because fitness is something else. But if we become more disabled, that makes us lose our resilience.
He said that in order to have hope in life, do not take our disabilities as an obstacle to overcome independence without waiting for dependence on others to survive. In addition, the charity continues to support and support people with disabilities who are willing to change out of poverty.
In fact, "So far, our foundation has helped to improve the livelihoods of many families with disabilities, both of whom have been able to avoid starvation by controlling the way to create their own businesses. Lack of daily livelihoods, such as raising pigs, chickens, ducks, providing financial support to study specific skills until the end of the purchase of equipment, including giving them artificial hands.
Oknha Dr. Chea Ratana stated, "The Oknha Dr. Chea Ratana and Oknha Ly Hiek Ratana Foundation was born out of a humanitarian spirit. We want to help him get out of poverty as well as join the Royal Government of Cambodia in reducing poverty and migration." In the past, we have also seen the success of our two disabled people. ”
In addition, Oknha Dr. Chea Ratana also appealed to the people, especially those who are engaged in the business of marketing equipment, must be very careful, because these jobs are very dangerous, please do not neglect, as it can cause amputation and disability as the case. In the past by some people with disabilities due to electric shocks, in addition to birth defects, traffic accidents and landmines left over from the war.
At the same time, we call on the relevant authorities to help inspect each work place that is vulnerable, requiring proper clothing and standard equipment before entering the work so as not to cause the risk of amputation. Taking that opportunity, Mr. Oknha Dr. Chea Ratana also appealed to all philanthropists who have helped and are helping people with disabilities, please continue and support more.
Please be informed that so far, the Oknha Dr. Chea Ratana and Oknha Ly Hiek Ratana Foundation have provided funding to support the expansion of 237 people with disabilities from different provinces throughout the country. For the disabled people who came to receive the budget this morning, 28 people (2 of them are still in the hospital) received 1 million Riel allowance and 1 T-shirt. 26 escorts received 100,000 Riels.
