(Phnom Penh): The Royal Academy of Cambodia has composed a song entitled "Princess Indra Devi". This song that praises the vitality of Indra Devi has received a lot of attention from the Cambodian people.
The song, which is based on the original Prasna Preah Mohasoth, describes the merits of Indra Devi, the consort of Jayavarman VII, in fulfilling her royal duty to promote national education in the Mohanakor period, the glorious period of the Angkorian Empire.
The song "Princess Indra Devi" entices the new generation of young people to turn their attention to learn more about the merits and sublime works of Princess Indra Devi, a famous queen and a highly educated Khmer scholar, a trained scholar and senior scholar. Many to become a strong pillar of the nation.
This song, which shows the values of our Queen of Angkor, was composed by Sarithy, a 7th generation Master of Philosophy, Part 1 of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, edited by Dr. Yong Pov, Secretary General of the Royal Academy of Cambodia and Co-produced by 7th generation undergraduate students, part 1.
This song was made after the Royal Academy of Cambodia, the nation's top research institution, erected a statue of Indra Devi, which was sculpted on metal in 2019. To commemorate the merits of her outstanding achievements in the field of education, especially linguistics and in the field of Buddhism, as a national treasure, a unique national identity.
It should be noted that to commemorate the merits of Indra Devi in the field of national education, the Royal Academy of Cambodia not only erected a statue of her, but also named the school building that trains Khmer intellectual resources at the Royal Academy of Cambodia in her name. Indra Devi also.
