China declares: "We have no intention of interfering in US elections"
BEIJING, June 18 (Xinhua) - China on Thursday announced that it has no intention of interfering in the November US presidential election. According to a release by CNA.
Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesman Zhao Lijian made the remarks at a press conference in Beijing in response to questions from reporters regarding the claims of former National Security Adviser John. Bolton said President Donald Trump had asked for help from Chinese President Xi Jinping so he could be re-elected.
In a meeting with Xi, Trump stressed that tackling US farmers' issues and increasing purchases of agricultural products such as soybeans under trade agreements with China could affect the election results. In addition, when the Chinese president agreed to hold talks on increasing US agricultural purchases as a priority, Trump even called Xi one of the greatest leaders in Chinese history.
