The following is a brief biography of Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk:
Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, Queen Mother of Cambodia in Freedom, Dignity and Happiness, was born on June 18, 1936.
As a child, he attended Preah Norodom Primary School, Preah Sisowath High School and Lyce Descartes in Phnom Penh. Samdech Mey can speak in French and English. Samdech Mey married Her Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia in April 1952.
His Majesty the Queen has two sons, Samdech Preah Boromneath Norodom Sihamoni, the current King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, and Prince Norodom Norinpong. Prince Norodom Narinpong died in 2003 of a disease.
In the late 1960s, Samdech Mey served as the President of the Cambodian Red Cross and now he is the Honorary President of the Cambodian Red Cross. Samdech Mey is the beloved wife of King Norodom Sihanouk, the King Father, who has received great love and mercy from her husband for more than half a century ago.
His Majesty the Queen Mother of Cambodia has followed His Majesty the King almost everywhere in all circumstances, including during the post-coup period of March 18, 1970, during the Democratic Kampuchea era, during the tripartite struggle on the border. Western or the Kingdom of Cambodia II.
On October 29, 2004, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, promulgated the Law on the Arrangement of His Majesty the Queen Mother, with the title of Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk. Khmer Queen Mother in freedom, dignity and happiness.
