Mr. Pa Socheatvong chaired a meeting of the management to review the progress of the work, challenges and suggestions of the provincial council.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pa Socheatvong, President of Phnom Penh Capital Council and President of National Association of Capital-Provincial Councils, chaired a meeting of National Association leaders in order to review the first half action report of 2020 and approve the second half action plan for 2020.
At the meeting, the management also reviewed and discussed the progress report, challenges and suggestions that the provincial council sent to the National Association to seek support and solutions.
At the same time, the meeting also reviewed the study and revision of the "Code of Ethics for Capital-Provincial Councilors" which was prepared and implemented in 2014.
In this meeting, Mr. Mao Phirun, Chairman of Kandal Provincial Council, was elected as the Vice President of the National Association to replace Mr. Nuon Pha who took on new responsibilities. The National Association has one president and 12 vice presidents (two women) from three political parties: the Cambodian People's Party, FUNCINPEC and the Khmer United National Party.
The National Association of Capital and Provincial Councils was established in 2013 with the aim of enhancing the status and capacity building of the Capital and Provincial Councils, protecting the legitimate interests and interests of its members, and building partnerships with relevant ministries and institutions to develop a strong base. Rule of law and promote democracy in Cambodia.
The National Association of Capital and Provincial Councils is the legal entity representing the voice of the Phnom Penh Capital Council and the 24 provincial councils. It should be noted that the Capital Council of the third mandate has a total of 559 members (94 women) from 550 CPP, 3 FUNCINPEC and 6 Khmer United National Party.
