In 2014, all NATO member states agreed to increase the military budget by 2% of their gross domestic product by 2024. So far, only eight countries have increased their military budgets by 2 percent, and others plan to meet the target by 2024. Germany, on the other hand, has not achieved this goal, hoping that it can be achieved by 2031.
* Why did Donald Trump reduce his army from Germany?
Reducing or withdrawing troops is Trump's policy and promise to bring US troops home. In addition to Germany, Trump has also announced troop reductions from South Korea, Japan, Syria, Iraq and Afghanistan.
Do Germans care about reducing US troops?
According to a September 2019 survey by the Pew Research Center, 45 percent of Germans say US military bases are not important to their national security, while only 15 percent think US bases are important to them. German national security. In contrast, 56 percent of Americans say US military bases on German soil are important to US national security.
Does Germany really need US troops?
