This budget was handed over by Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, to Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, Minister of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Board of Trustees of the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia this morning, June 17, 2020.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth highly appreciated the initiative of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport under the leadership of Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, which improved public services for the people and increased revenue for the state.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth thanked the inter-ministerial members for their hard work in the past with good results and requested to continue the good cooperation to make this service better. More and more revenue for the state.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol emphasized that the sale of personal license plates is another new source of income. He said that the revenue from the sale of "Cambodia 5" special license plate, which received 800,480,000 riels, is a history that this type of personal license plate sells at a high price.
On January 7, 2020, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport (MPWT) launched its own special license plate to create more options for car owners to use the license plate and raise more revenue for the nation. This license plate is different from other license plates in that the car owner can set the letters and numbers as he wants and is a unique license plate.
According to Heang Sotheayut, spokesman for the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, in the five months from January 7, 2020 to the end of May 2020, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport sold special license plates. Own 1,432 labels, about 16 billion riels, equivalent to about 4 million US dollars.
