A statement from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, received by Fresh News this afternoon, said that the meeting was co-chaired by the Co-President of the Republic of Indonesia, the current coordinator of the ASEAN-Russia Dialogue Partnership and the Russian Federation.
The ASEAN Foreign Ministers and the Russian Foreign Ministers exchanged views on the best practices and lessons learned from the global pandemic and discussed ways to boost cooperation in all fields. Joint interests and to strengthen the ASEAN-Russia strategic partnership, especially in the field of public health.
The video conferencing was held at a difficult and busy time due to the unprecedented global challenges of 19 communicable diseases, which require a united struggle through unity. And solidarity based solely on effective multilateral foundations. The meeting is a further step in the ASEAN-Russia strategic partnership for long-term cooperation.
