The following is the Royal Decree of the King: The Governor of Phnom Penh presents the project to build a water treatment plant in Stung Meanchey canal area (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): So far, the construction of Stung Meanchey canal system from the base of Stung Meanchey bridge to The Deum Sleng canal is about 90 percent complete, which is scheduled to be completed soon to avoid flooding in Phnom Penh.
The Stung Meanchey Canal, an old canal in Phnom Penh that was previously almost completely abused by the people living along the canal, was later recaptured by Phnom Penh authorities led by Mr. Khuong Sreng and provided an appropriate solution. To the people to be developed on the spot.
Phnom Penh Governor Khuong Sreng on the morning of June 16, 2020, confirmed that the Stung Meanchey canal is scheduled to be completed in about half a month or another month, while the canal area is no longer as congested as before. That.
In a press conference on the progress and direction of the work of the Phnom Penh Capital Administration, organized by the spokesman of the Royal Government, Mr. Khuong Sreng confirmed that after the completion of this project, the authorities will continue the development project, with plans to build a treatment plant. Clean water in this area to turn that water into clean water that can be used to irrigate crops.
Mr. Khuong Sreng said, "In the past, riding through Stung Meanchey was difficult to breathe, short of breath, but now it has been relieved, and we will continue to consider this issue step by step is to think about the construction of the treatment tank to make "Stung Meanchey sewer becomes clean water that can be used to irrigate crops, which is the next step that we need to develop for the people."
According to Khuong Sreng, the biggest advantage of rehabilitating the Stung Meanchey canal from this abuse is the release of water from the Khmer Rouge tribunal, which flows into Phnom Penh, in the Stung Meanchey area.
The Phnom Penh Governor also claimed that the Stung Meanchey Canal, which the Phnom Penh Capital Administration has been developing, passes through two districts, Khan Meanchey and Khan Sen Sok, where more than 500 families live and are affected by the canal. This will get 4 x 6 meters of land legally owned on the spot.
The Stung Meanchey canal plays an important role in bringing runoff into Boeung Tumpun. The project of Stung Meanchey canal is 8 meters wide, 2 meters wide, 6 meters wide concrete road, 5 meters wide in front of the house, 1 and a half meters in front of the house and half a meter behind the house.
