Woman lying dead in a rented room on suspicion of beating her husband to death in Kambol district
The death of the woman is suspected to have been beaten to death by her ex-husband in a dispute because the family was not very harmonious in the past, there were always arguments and the husband used violence to beat his wife. Often not only just surprised to find his wife's body immediately, the late husband escaped immediately as well.
Heng Sok Kheun, 45, a former factory worker, was a widow with two children, an 18-year-old daughter who was already married and a son who lived at the scene in his hometown of Chroul village, Balang commune. Kampong Trabek District, Prey Veng Province. She married Pich Chantha, 43, a construction worker in Svay Rieng province.
The housewife said that before the incident, he walked past the first room, there was a strange smell, and with suspicion, he cut the door and immediately found the woman dead. The situation is already rotten, so report to the authorities to go down and check.
As for the villagers, they said that on the evening of Saturday, June 13, 2020, the step-husband rode a motorbike to take the victim to his birthday party and did not return until late at night. Later, the wife disappeared from the house until the body was found, while the husband escaped, and now the authorities are conducting an autopsy and searching for the perpetrator to be punished according to law.
