Cambodia, China accelerate mango exports and expand banana, cassava and other agricultural products to China
(Phnom Penh): Both Cambodia and China have agreed to expedite the implementation of the recently signed Cambodian Mango Export Protocol to China and to actively expand the export of bananas, cassava and Cambodian agricultural products. There are other qualities.
Protocol on "Hygienic requirements for the export of fresh mangoes from Cambodia to the People's Republic of China" was signed on June 9, 2019 at the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries. Through this protocol, Cambodia can export 500,000 tons of fresh mangoes a year to China.
According to the joint statement, the Chinese side will actively review funding for Cambodia's priority infrastructure development projects, including roads, bridges, electricity, dams and irrigation systems. In addition, the Chinese side will continue to support Cambodia in improving the living standards of its people.
The two sides signed a memorandum of understanding on enhancing the responsibilities of the Cambodia-China Intergovernmental Coordinating Committee after the meeting. The two sides agreed to hold the sixth meeting of the Intergovernmental Coordinating Committee in China in 2022.
