Former diplomat: China provides aid to Cambodia, does not demand political conditions like some countries
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong, the former head of the Cambodian diplomatic corps, confirmed that the Chinese government has provided assistance to Cambodia in participating in economic and infrastructure rehabilitation without imposing political conditions like some other countries.
The former Cambodian diplomat stated: "There is no monopoly on Cambodia's friendship with any country. We are all open. The Cambodian-Chinese relationship is good. Why? Because China provides a lot of grants and loans. "Building Cambodian society, a lot of investment in Cambodia has no political conditions."
The Deputy Prime Minister added that the Cambodian relationship is the most comprehensive and strong strategic relationship. However, Cambodia-China relations are not exclusive, Cambodia needs to strengthen all ties with countries around the world.
Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong added: "Cambodia's development over the past 20 years has reached 7%, and in recent years it has exceeded 7% due to the efforts of our people under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister. "But Chinese aid, Chinese support, such as grants, interest-free loans, low lending and technical assistance, have all helped Cambodia to develop our Cambodian economy."
At the same time, through this strategic all-round relationship, in the face of the crisis in China 19, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, was the first leader to enter China to encourage the Chinese government. In a lonely stage where no foreign leader dares to act like Samdech Techo.
