(Prey Veng): Many farmers in Chea Khlang commune, Svay Antor district, Prey Veng province have chosen to grow sugarcane as a strategic crop and have increased their cultivation on a regular basis, and in this commune there are almost no migrants.
Mr. Obsat, chief of Chea Khlang commune, said that due to the high sugarcane market in recent years, the farmers in Chea Khlang commune have increased their cultivation almost twice as much as last year. Only 300 hectares, but for this year they have increased to more than 500 hectares.
He said that for this year, there may be a slight market challenge because the problem of Kovid 19 has occurred to silence traders, however, he is not a big issue.
As for the sugarcane farmers, they said that this year, the farmers have expanded their sugarcane cultivation a lot, there are almost no vacant fields, because in previous years, they can sell about 30 to more than 30 million riel per year. Hectares, but for this year, farmers may decrease slightly, but at least from 25 million to 30 million riels.
Separately, Mr. Boy Lot, Director of Administration Office of Prey Veng Provincial Department of Agriculture, said that in relation to the sugarcane crop here, as well as other crops, the Provincial Department of Agriculture always comes to advise farmers every year on how to grow and use seeds. And the use of fertilizers to prevent crop diseases and obtain high yields.
He added that in recent years, sugarcane in the commune has also experienced diseases and pests, but we can prevent and get as much fruit as today.
In addition, he also called on farmers to grow good quality crops and get high yields, please grow according to the techniques recommended by officials.
