(Kandal): Mr. Hing Sothy, Deputy Director of the Department of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction and Cadastral Affairs of Kandal Province, said that in order to reduce land disputes and achieve the complete elimination of land disputes in the districts in Kandal province, commune chiefs, commune chiefs and chiefs All villages need to understand the procedures of cadastral expertise and laws to make it easier to explain to the people in their locality.
Mr. Khon Serey Ratha, Governor of Ang Snoul District and Chairman of the District Cadastral Commission, praised the District Cadastral Commission, Commune / Sangkat Chief, Commune / Sangkat Clerks and Village Elders for their hard work in all activities. Land registration and coordination of land tenure and use procedures for citizens at their local level.
He said that in the past, a small number of procedures were implemented according to the habits and procedures of the commune, but today we have the opportunity to meet with instructors who have expertise in both technical and legal procedures that can be a mirror. A beacon for clear and accurate guidance on legal and technical procedures.
