Ministry of Commerce spokesman Seang Thai recalled that Minister of Commerce Pan Sosak and South Korean Minister of Commerce Yoo Myung-Hee had signed a joint statement on the start of the feasibility study. In establishing the Cambodia-South Korea Free Trade Agreement in November 2019 in Busan, South Korea.
Seang Thai added that after the signing ceremony, the two countries' working groups held regular talks and saw that free trade led to trade and investment benefits between the two countries. Two.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Commerce said that the working group of the two countries had already submitted a request for talks on the establishment of a free trade agreement to the leaders of the two countries. The spokesman stressed that if there is a blue rain from the leaders of the two countries, the talks could start in July.
Mr. Seang Thai emphasized that the free trade agreement not only agreed to the exemption of tariff barriers, but also covered many other areas, such as services, investment, trade facilitation, elimination of non-tariff barriers and so on.
Trade volume between Cambodia and South Korea has been steadily increasing, especially in recent years. In 2019, the trade volume between Cambodia and South Korea was nearly 9 million US dollars, an increase of more than 14 percent compared to 2018.
Cambodia's main exports to South Korea include: T-shirts, men's clothing, electronics, shoes, suitcases, aluminum foil, beverages, medical supplies (surgical cushions), tents and natural rubber. Reports from South Korea include trucks, natural mineral water blankets, blankets, electronics, bulldozers, nickel-plated panels or sheets, processed fabrics, dyes and beauty products.
Seang Thai expressed the hope that free trade with South Korea would further strengthen ties and expand trade between the two countries, as well as create domestic jobs, export services and expand investment. Contribute to the development of the national economy and benefit the people of both countries.
