During the Cold War, the KGB was responsible for overseas espionage and domestic security. In addition, the KGB was responsible for protecting Soviet political leaders, controlling troops at the border, and conducting general surveillance of the Soviet people.
A year later, the GPU was renamed the "OGPU" and took on additional responsibilities, such as managing labor camps and monitoring population activity. During the early 1930s, the OGPU began conducting covert operations on foreign territory to curb the activities of groups opposed to the Soviet Union from the outside. Some of them were kidnapped and murdered.
During World War II, the MGB carried out various espionage operations and also focused on countering enemy espionage, as well as controlling the concentration camps of war prisoners and ensuring loyalty among the military. After the war, the MGB helped the Soviet Union suppress opposition movements, whether true or false, in Eastern Europe and within the Soviet Union itself.
(Preah Vihear): Currently, a large number of rare birds are living in the Kulen Prom Tep National Park, Preah Vihear Province, which covers an area of 402,500 hectares, covering Choam Ksan, Kulen, Tbeng Meanchey and Preah Vihear and is also being conserved. From park rangers and community members, including the Thmat Bei Thoeun Krasang community, also actively participated in this work.
Travel from Preah Vihear City on National Road No. 62 to Choam Ksan District. From National Road No. 62, turn right along the red gravel road for a while, then you will reach the village in Pring Thom commune, where one side is the people's farmland and the other is full of large community forest The tail of the eye provides a pleasant natural shade.
Thmat Bei Thoeun Krasang Community was first established in 2003 with a total area of 214,000 hectares in Kulen Prom Tep National Park with the support of the Wildlife Conservation Society (WCS). It was not until 2005 that the community introduced ecotourism services to serve tourists.
There are 61 family members in this community who have been participating in tourism services in various fields, some of them are truck drivers, some of them are chefs, some of them are nest guards, some of them are Sellers of agricultural products, non-timber forest products, materials and many other indirect beneficiaries.
He added that in the past, wildlife was hunted for a small fee, but the devastation was so great that when it was relocated to a tourism service like today, the livelihood of the ecotourism community of Thmat Bei Thoeun Krasang has increased. So much progress.
Mr. Dip Kim On claimed that in the past, most of the villagers were hunters and he was the same, but he always felt sorry for the animals and regretted their actions. Until he got a new job in the tourism industry, he and his family were very happy because they earned more than hunting and built a righteous life by contributing to the conservation of the remaining wildlife.
He vowed that despite the difficulties, he persevered so that the natural resources in the community as well as in the national park would remain stable for the next generation to continue to provide tourism services to the guests, earning money to help the family, so that the children could go to school. They will use the money from the sale of tourism services to help build schools, wells, roads, and other infrastructure in the village.
(Kampong Cham): After a sudden gust of wind caused damage to the houses of 6 families living in Damnak Ampil village, Steng Chey commune, Cheung Prey district, Kampong Cham province, this morning, June 15, 2020, Dr. Ma Chhoeun, Member of Parliament for Kampong Cham and As the head of the middle level working group to help Cheung Prey district, he visited and gave gifts to alleviate the difficulties immediately.
"This natural disaster is not only in Cambodia, but all over the world, where we do not know the natural wind and wind, which requires our brothers to be very careful not to be dangerous," he said. Life. Due to this concern, the Royal Government of Cambodia, as well as officials of the working group, paid high attention to visit and find out the difficulties to alleviate the suffering immediately like now.
Apparently, as in the above case, our local officials immediately provided information to the upper level to continue to manage the team officials to find out the impact to provide food, budget and necessary materials to the families of the victims.
At the same time, the deputies of Kampong Cham also advised people to be careful if there is rain, thunder or strong winds, so please leave the risk area to a safe place to prevent any accident.
Dr. also reminded the authorities and authorities at all localities to monitor the weather closely, to rush to intervene in time while people are affected by natural phenomena.
On that occasion, the six families expressed their gratitude to Dr. Ma Chhoeun, a member of the National Assembly, who has always been associated with the people in all circumstances, especially when people are in trouble. Visit and help solve people's difficulties.
Especially today, Dr. Ma Chhoeun came to the place to inquire about the situation of this disaster and helped to provide food, budget and some necessary materials, which alleviated the suffering of the people after receiving the news. The typhoon destroyed homes on the afternoon of June 13, and he sent local officials to visit to find out the need for timely assistance.
Arrested after Clash with Military in Prey Nup District, Preah Sihanouk Province While Preventing Land Violation
(Preah Sihanouk): There was a clash between the military officers of Prey Nob district, Preah Sihanouk province, with a group of anarchists who violated the land of the people and built a fence to take their land anarchically and cause fear to Innocent people.
Brigadier General Heng Bunty, Commander of the Sihanoukville Provincial Gendarmerie, told Fresh News on the afternoon of June 15, 2020, that in the clash, the Gendarmerie was injured by an unknown person. Authorities also arrested a suspect.
According to the Commander-in-Chief, Prey Nup District Administration has received reports from residents that land has been encroached upon by anarchists, who have encircled the people's fences and are rebuilding their new fences. This fence belongs to everyone.
Therefore, the Prey Nup District Administration ordered the Prey Nup District Gendarmerie to intervene, but the intervention of the Gendarmerie was stopped by the anarchist group and used violence against the force with knives, sticks and rubber. Cruelly, a 25-year-old male soldier named Khoeun Sokret was injured by a knife.
However, in this incident, the police arrested the assailant named Su Eap, alias Pheap Sak, male, 37 years old, his hometown is Trapeang Roth village, Khnar commune, Samrong Tong district, Kampong Speu province. Serious hand injuries.
However, other sources claim that these people have always caused a great deal of anarchy by burning car tires and destroying the property of people living in the area of Koki village, Bit Trang commune, Prey Nob district.
Brigadier General Heng Bunty confirmed that on the morning of June 16, 2020, the arrested suspects will be sent to court for further proceedings while the other perpetrators are being carefully investigated by the specialized military forces. Put.
