A young man who stole a video while taking a bath was handcuffed by Saang district police in Kandal province
(Kandal): A young man was arrested by Saang district police after receiving a complaint about the use of a mobile phone to steal a picture of a woman taking a bath in a bathroom through a galvanized iron wall this morning, June 15, 2020, at a shared bathroom Located in Kbal Chroy village, Prek Koy commune, Saang district, Kandal province.
Sources from the Royal Forces said that the victim was a 14-year-old Cambodian student living in Kbal Chroy village, Prek Koy commune, Saang district, Kandal province. The suspect, En Theara, male, 26 years old, Khmer, car mechanic, resides in Kbal Chroy village, Prek Koy commune, Saang district, Kandal province.
According to the source, while the victim was taking a bath in the bathroom, the suspect, who was staying at a nearby car repair garage, stole a video phone through a hole in the corrugated iron roof. The victim was seen screaming and startling the family.
Then, the victim's mother came to ask for the phone from the suspect, but the suspect refused to hand it over, and the victim's mother reported to the Prek Koy police.
Police said that immediately after receiving the information, Prek Koy police arrived to interrogate and confiscated the suspect's phone and checked the naked video of the victim and sent the suspect and the evidence to the district police inspectorate. Saang to handle the procedure.
With a congratulatory message on Facebook, Samdech Techo stated, "His Majesty the King, His Majesty the King, His Majesty the King, His Majesty the King, His Majesty the King, His Majesty the King, His Majesty the King, His Majesty the King, His Majesty the King, His Majesty the King, His Majesty the King, His Majesty the King, His Majesty the King, His Majesty the King." World July 7, 2008. "
His Majesty the King of Cambodia, His Majesty the King, His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, carried out the Royal Crusade to demand the Temple of Preah Vihear and expel the Thai Armed Forces from the Temple of Preah Vihear.
After a failed diplomatic process, Cambodia filed a complaint with the International Court of Justice in The Hague on October 6, 1959, requesting the court to hand over territorial sovereignty over the Temple of Preah Vihear to Cambodia and demand that Thailand withdraw its armed forces. All from the temple of Preah Vihear.
During the trial, Cambodia and Thailand presented their respective arguments for ownership of the Preah Vihear temple. Cambodia has adopted the Dangrek map (Appendix 1 map), a map derived from the Franco-Siamese Treaty of 1904, as its legal basis. The boundary line in the Appendix 1 map shows that the Temple of Preah Vihear is in Cambodian territory.
Despite the Thai side's objections, the 1962 International Court of Justice in The Hague ultimately rejected the Thai side's claim. According to the Hague Tribunal, Article 1 of the 1904 Treaty stipulates the demarcation line of the waterway, but Article 3 of the treaty states that the actual demarcation line will be determined by the Commission. French-Siamese mix.
In the case of the Dangrek area, the border line arising from the work of the Franco-Siamese Joint Commission is unique, the border line in the Appendix I map cited by Cambodia as a reference. So there is no need to find the location of the waterway divider.
