Po Sen Chey District Governor Inspects Rehabilitation of Toul Pong Canal and Calls on People Not to Throw Garbage or Other Waste Into the Canal
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Hem Darith, Governor of Por Senchey District, together with many other district officials, this morning, June 15, 2020, inspected the rehabilitation activities of Toul Pong Canal at the construction site of Borey Chip Mong next to the factory. EDC East of Toul Pong Village, Sangkat Choam Chao I, Khan Por Sen Chey, where the condition of the canal is narrow and the land is shallow with grass and gravel, which needs to be ferryed in order to operate.
Mr. Kang Vong, Chief of Choam Chao I Commune, said that the two Tuol Pong canals have a western border with Prey Lvea Village, Sangkat Choam Chao II East and a border with Khan Dangkor and Khan Meanchey with a length of more than 2,000 meters. The restoration process started three weeks ago, achieving more than 90%, only the end of the canal remains.
These two Tuol Pong canals are very important in relieving the flood and rain water of daily use in the southern area of Khan Kampol and Khan Por Sen Chey. For many years, these two Tuol Pong canals have never been restored, leaving the entire body of the canal shallow with mud, grass and mud.
In addition, in some places, people have stolen land, flooded canals, taken ownership of roads, replaced them with small drains, and in some places, people have dumped rubbish or construction debris in this situation. The canal is getting narrower and the land is shallow, blocking the flow of water, causing the houses of the people above to flood every year.
During the inspection of the canal rehabilitation activities, Mr. Hem Darith called on the people not to violate the canal drainage and not to throw garbage or other waste into the canal, leading to shallow land canals, blocking the flow of water and causing flooding of houses.
Taking this opportunity, the Governor of Po Sen Chey District also called on all people to continue to be careful about the transmission of Kovid 19, by following the guidelines of the Ministry of Health.
