Since 2014, the Asian Development Bank (ADB) has partnered with the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training to take TVET systems and programs in Cambodia to a new level, with an investment of nearly $ 175 million.
This work includes sharpening the skills and competitiveness of Cambodia's industrial workforce, as well as developing human resources for the four priority sectors, including manufacturing, construction, electricity and electronics.
Selected technical training institutes have been transformed into leading national technical and vocational education and training institutes to develop high-quality technicians for priority sectors and respond to changing industrial and technical needs.
