Authorities inspected a timber storage site in Ponhea Leu district after it was reported that there were irregularities
(Kandal): Mr. Ly Socheat, Deputy Provincial Police Commissioner in charge of Economic Crimes under the direct command of Brigadier General Chhoeun Socheat, Kandal Provincial Police Commissioner, visited a timber storage site in Ta Chey Village, Chrey Las Commune, Ponhea Leu District, Kandal Province. .
The operation took place on June 13, 2020 in collaboration with the Ang Snuol Sangkat Forestry Administration, Chrey Las Commune Police Post to inspect the non-timber forest products processing handicraft owned by Men Makara, male, 25 years old, in Ta Chey village. Chrey Las commune, Ponhea Leu district, Kandal province.
Ly Socheat told Fresh News in Kandal province that after an anonymous person posted a slander in connection with a $ 15,000 corruption case, he denied that he had any money. Involved in this case, and he did not even know the location of this wood storage until the Forestry Administration led to the new location.
He said that after visiting the site, the force found that the owner of the site has the correct legal documents, including:
First, the permit to establish a small-scale wood processing non-timber handicraft factory No. 08KLP, dated March 4, 2020, issued by the Director of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries.
Third: There is a book to monitor the traffic of non-timber forest products. The team then inspected and measured the actual amount of wood in the craft as in the legal documents.
It should be informed that after an anonymous person posted false information on social media related to this case, then Brigadier General Chhoeun Socheat, Kandal Provincial Police Commissioner, came out to reject a news that was spread on Facebook that the Kandal Provincial Economic Police opened Green light takes $ 15,000 to bring timber to be stored at a warehouse in Ponhea Leu district.
The Brigadier General of the Provincial Commissioner said that in this case, the owner of the small-scale non-timber forest products processing handicraft has the right permit from the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, which has the owner of the handicraft named Men Makara and the permit to set up the non-timber processing handicraft factory. Small type forest No. 08 KHP / K / SFH / P is located in Ta Chey village, Chrey Las commune, Ponhea Leu district, Kandal province.
