Drunk man angry at wife for not sleeping, set fire to his own house
(Stung Treng): On the night of June 12, 2020, there was a house fire in Keng Nhay village, Sekong commune, Siem Pang district, Stung Treng province, caused by the man who owns the house. According to the authorities, the fire occurred because the man was angry with his wife not to sleep when he was drunk and decided to set fire to his house.
According to the Sekong Post authorities, the case of self-destruction caused by a 58-year-old man named Lot Tan, living in Ke Nhay village, Sekong commune, Siem Pang district, Stung Treng province.
Sekong police said that on the day of the incident, the man was drunk when he returned home to sleep with his wife, but his wife chased him not to sleep nearby, so he was angry and set fire to his house. The villagers all night.
The Sekong commune administrative police station added that the house that her husband set on fire was 5 meters long and 6 meters long, made of thatch, bamboo, and bamboo.
After the incident, the villagers helped to put out the fire, but could not put it out because the fire was too strong and completely destroyed. Meanwhile, the man who set fire to his property was also summoned by the Sekong Post Police for questioning.
