Overall, farmers have decided to grow about 80% of the early season rice on 1,221 hectares using fragrant rice and weed. So far, the rice is growing well, but the water condition in the canal is lacking for pumping rice.
From Maung Russey district, Minister Veng Sakhon, Deputy Governor and colleagues traveled to Banan district to inspect the Tvea Kanghat dam, a source of water flowing down the rice fields in Prey Touch commune.
In the above area, Kantea 1 commune has an area of 6,848 hectares of rice cultivation, up to now it has achieved more than 90% and generally uses fragrant rice varieties, romduol, jasmine and jasmine rice.
The rice crop is growing well, but in recent weeks, insufficient rainfall has made the main canal lacking water for farmers to pump their rice.
Most of the farmers asked Minister Veng Sakhon and the Deputy Governor to help solve the problem of having water in the canals to pump rice, and if there is no rain in the next few days, many hectares of farmland may face water shortage.
On behalf of Minister Veng Sakhon, he instructed the director of the department to cooperate with the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology and district authorities to monitor this issue closely and be ready to intervene to farmers in a timely manner.
