But unlike the KGB, the CIA is banned by US national security law from spying on US territory, meaning that CIA operations must take place abroad. In contrast, most KGB operations took place in the Soviet Union and directly against the Soviet people. The KGB was disbanded in 1991 after the collapse of the Soviet Union.
The CIA is divided into four major departments. The Department of Intelligence is responsible for analyzing critical information collected through open means, such as from the media, and through non-open means, such as from CIA agents, from satellite imagery, and from eavesdropping on conversations. Phones as well as other means of communication.
The last is the administration department, which is responsible for the finances and issues related to the CIA staff directly. The department also has a security office, which is responsible for ensuring the security of personnel as well as protecting CIA intelligence and secrecy within the CIA.
During the Cold War, CIA technical operations included the installation of hearing aids on Soviet military communications lines in East Germany and the development of reconnaissance aircraft such as U-2s and reconnaissance satellites. Good pictures and so on. Aerial and space reconnaissance by aircraft and satellites helped the United States anticipate plans for a Soviet missile deployment in Cuba and the development of new missiles in the Soviet Union.
The CIA has also been criticized for conducting covert operations that are immoral or illegal under international law, for maintaining close ties with human rights abusers and other criminals, for failing to do so. Ensuring the protection of its operations, and since 2001 due to kidnapping, torture and illegal detention of foreigners.
