(Kandal): Mr. Keo Remy, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Chairman of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, on June 13, 2020, led the working group and philanthropists to continue to visit and bring food and study materials. Some items are provided to children at "Cambodian Child Development" in Prek Treng village, Sitbo commune, Saang district, Kandal province.
This is the fifth time that the Human Rights Committee has taken a child with his mother in prison for humanitarian intervention. The Cambodian Human Rights Committee has been in contact with Various partner organizations that are qualified to adopt the 3-year-old son of the detainee Pich Soneth to raise, care for, educate and live in a better environment.
