Minister Veng Sakhon Inspects Rice Cultivation of Pursat Residents and Calls for Participation in Defending Peace "Peace, Only Development"
(Pursat): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on June 13, 2020, inspected the progress of the agricultural community "Rasmei Kakkar" in Kampong Sambo village, Sya commune, Kandieng district, Pursat province.
During the meeting with community members, most of whom are rice producers, said that the community now has 61 members with 234 shares and a total capital of more than 50 million riels.
In 2019, community members produced fragrant rice seeds using 3 hectares of seeds on an average yield of 3.50 tons per hectare, twice a year for self-consumption and distribution to members and Other farmers, both inside and outside the village.
In order to improve the quality of rice seeds for 2020, the community has piloted the production of certified fragrant rice seeds using 40 kg of foundation seeds on 3 hectares of land obtained from the General Department of Agriculture.
As for the production of fodder rice, the community uses fragrant seeds on an area of 65 hectares, with an average yield of more than 4 tons per hectare, applied two to three times a year, and the price of wet rice from 900 to 1,200 riels per kilogram. .
Mr. Chea Sokun, a member of the community, said that he was also involved in the production of rice seeds and fodder on an area of 5 hectares, with an average yield of 4 tons per hectare. The community generally uses an inscription system that originates from the Pursat River.
In addition to rice, some community members raise chickens for meat, eggs, hatchlings, and pigs for family consumption, and are connecting to prefabricated power grids for irrigation of agricultural crops.
Clearly recognizing all the important achievements that the community has achieved, both rice (seed and fodder) and animal husbandry, Minister Veng Sakhon appreciated the efforts of all members to raise the standard of living well. Better.
Minister Veng Sakhon continued that this is what the Royal Government wants and wants to see the people who have been sheltering under the shadow of peace, live in peace, rich life, happy family.
Therefore, Minister Veng Sakhon requested that all of our people must participate in defending peace to have development.
Regarding the production of both seed and fodder rice, Minister Veng Sakhon requested the community to implement contract agricultural production to ensure the value and sustainability of supply.
Regarding technical work, Mr. Veng Sakhon suggested that the community cooperate with the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to use drumseeder equipment in conjunction with bulldozers to save labor time, easy to control weeds and get high yields.
In particular, it is necessary to improve the irrigation canal better than at present, which is to pump water once into the rice field, avoid pumping two or three times before entering the rice field, which costs a lot of money.
