Authorities thank authorities and philanthropists for bringing water to the Bakong temple
(Siem Reap): The team of APSARA Authority in cooperation with Prasat Bakong District Unity Command has been diligently digging water wells to pump mud from Bakong temple pond to deep water and transport water from outside area into this pond from June 10-11, 2020.
This work was done to save the big fish in the pond to continue to live in the pond water of Bakong temple. Lim Sambath, police inspector of Prasat Bakong district, said that after the incident, the district governor and he released more than 100 police officers to intervene by putting a pump head and transporting water to fill the tank. .
Another main reason is that the waterfall of Bakong temple is only related to the groundwater layer and also has no direct connection with any other river. Please be informed that a few days ago, due to the water in Kasinthu, Bakong temple was dry in some places, causing the death of some big fish and some big fish.
The District Inspector and the authorities would like to thank the Phnom Penh University students, the Trang Village Assistance Team, and Mr. Tan Sopheaktra, as well as the people who donated diesel, pure water, soft drinks, packaged rice, canned noodles and cooking. To the team that is carrying out fish rescue operations in the pond of Sinthu, Bakong temple.
