(Phnom Penh): The Governor of Chamkarmon District, Mr. Theng Sothol, called on people to be very careful about their personal and family safety, as this season there is rain mixed with wind, wind and thunder, which can be dangerous in any event.
Mr. Theng Sothol made this call during the distribution ceremony of the CRC Sub-Branch of Chamkar Mon District to the needy people living in the 5 Sangkats of Chamkar Mon District.
He added that as the rainy season approaches, people need to take care of their young children with the proper electrical connection to avoid electric shock when it rains. Or the wind can cause the trees to collapse, affecting the lives of small children who do not know, and so on.
Mr. Theng Sothol also reminded the people when any problems should be reported to the local authorities who are close to you so that the team can intervene to you quickly and in time.
In connection with the rainy season, Mr. Theng Sothol also called on people to store garbage properly, especially to release garbage according to the time when the truck came to collect garbage to avoid leaving in front of the house when it may rain. Let it flow into the drain, causing the drain to clog.
