Mr. Ith Sam Heng urges people to continue to protect themselves and listen to the instructions of the Ministry of Health
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Member of the Central Committee, Deputy Chairman of the Phnom Penh Municipal Assistance Team and Chairman of the Chamkar Mon and Boeung Keng Kang District Assistance Task Force, urged people to continue to protect themselves and follow the instructions of the Ministry of Health. Avoid the global Kovid-19 epidemic.
This announcement was made by Mr. Ith Sam Heng during a meeting and distribution of gifts to 192 poor families in Boeung Keng Kang district on the morning of June 13, 2020 at Chea Sim Boeung Keng Kang High School.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng said that people must continue to maintain hygiene measures to be safe, must wear a mask every time they go out and wash their hands often with soap and alcohol. He reminded that Kovid-19 is a disease that the world is very concerned about because it is contagious, whether rich or poor, old or young, can face infection if not prevented.
On this occasion, he also called on all people to continue to maintain hygiene rules in accordance with the instructions of the Ministry of Health not to infect other diseases, especially Kovid 19, which is spreading to keep people healthy.
