Another main goal is to continue to strengthen and expand the new achievements of the party youth to join the CPP in the cause of serving the nation and the people better.
Please note that Mr. Hun Manet on Saturday, June 13, 2020 was officially announced by the Cambodian People's Party as the youth leader of the Cambodian People's Party at the middle level.
The announcement of the appointment of Mr. HUN Manet as the youth leader of the Cambodian People's Party in the middle to replace Mr. Ke Bun Khieng was presided over by Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, Vice President of the Cambodian People's Party.
According to the decision of the Cambodian People's Party, the appointment was made based on the capacity and request of the Central Committee Organizing Committee as well as the opinion of the Standing Committee of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party.
Please note that Mr. HUN Manet currently has a position in the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces as Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the Army. Mr. Hun Manet is also a permanent member of the Cambodian People's Party.
Separately, Mr. Ke Bun Kheang, who is over 60 years old, has been transferred to his previous position as Deputy Chairman of the Education Propaganda Committee of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party. This is according to the confirmation of the Cambodian People's Party.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that despite the small number of infected people in Cambodia, the disease is still the most deadly epidemic and there is no cure.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that people should not be short-sighted, negligent or risk themselves with the Kovid-19 epidemic, whether living in the city or in the countryside of Sre Chamkar district, all must always be careful.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen wrote completely like this: "How are you, compatriots? Please continue to take care to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 throughout the country, even if the number of infected people in our country is small. Kovid-19 is still the deadliest pandemic, with so far the number of infected people in the world has risen alarmingly, and there is no cure.
Please, people, do not think short, neglect or risk yourself with the Kovid-19 epidemic, whether living in the city or in the countryside, we must always be careful.
As of this morning, June 13, 2020, a total of 126 people (39 females and 87 males) have been infected with the Kovid-19 virus throughout Cambodia. Of the 125 people being treated at the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital, only one was a Cambodian man who had just returned from the Philippines.
On this issue, the Director of Emergency Management of the WHO also continued to call on the world to work together to overcome this global crisis. He also stressed the importance of learning to live with the virus and finding a balanced approach to managing it. For some countries it is very difficult to take action to close the country in front of COVID-19.
Minister of Agriculture urges Kampong Chhnang Provincial Department of Agriculture to diligently inspect all farming activities of farmers, if any problems are solved in time
(Phnom Penh): On June 13, 2020, Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and Mr. Chhour Chandoeun, Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province, inspected Mr. Hoeung Seng Hay's 6-hectare corn crop in Anlong An area, Sangkat Kampong Chhnang. Kampong Chhnang. After that, they continued to inspect 500 hectares of early season rice crops (using fragrant seeds, cassava flowers and 5154 varieties) in Kampong Os village, Kampong Os commune, Chulkiri district.
Meeting with the owner of the corn field, Mr. Seng Hay described happily that this area has the potential to grow corn, soybeans and sweet potatoes, he can grow corn twice a season after harvesting beans and can earn 10 million Riel does not include income from soybeans and rice noodles mixed with corn, a day sells 50,000 riel.
Regarding rice, Ms. Chrek Kimchhean, on behalf of the farmers, described the production chain of rice from seed to care and harvest. In general, farmers in this area use fragrant seeds and cardamom, both of which yield more than 6 tons per hectare and sell for 1,000 riel per kilogram.
She said that the ER 5154 varieties yield 8 tons per hectare, the selling price of 800 riel per kilogram. Sowing and harvesting uses all the machinery, especially to sell rice in the field, and in some cases, traders come down to the price of rice since the rice began to sow.
She added that in addition to rice, farmers also have a combination of peppers and beans. Each year, each family earns not less than 10 million riels, but it depends on the land that each family has.
The Minister and the Provincial Governor joined in congratulating the achievements of the corn and rice farmers now, the increase in yields, the market for good products and the sustainability of household income. The Minister, on behalf of the Ministry leadership as well as the Provincial Governor, expressed their support and encouragement for them to make more efforts to contribute to the success of the Royal Government's vision for 2030 and 2050.
Regarding technical work, the Minister instructed the Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to diligently monitor all crop production activities so that farmers do not encounter problems and must cooperate to solve in time. On this occasion, the Minister donated 1 million Riels to the community of Kampong Os Ponleu Chan and 800,000 Riels to the provincial governor.
