Minister of Justice defends draft law on anti-financing of weapons of mass destruction to Senate Interior Committee
(Phnom Penh): In the afternoon of June 12, 2020, Mr. Keut Rith, Minister of Justice, accompanied by leaders and senior officials of the Ministry of Interior and the National Bank of Cambodia, attended a meeting to defend the draft law on anti-financing. The proliferation of weapons of mass destruction to the Committee on Interior, National Defense, National Assembly-Senate Relations, Inspection and Public Function of the Senate.
The commission is chaired by Mr. Sok Isan and is attended by Mr. Yang Sem, Chairman of the Second Commission and representatives of the relevant commissions.
According to the Ministry of Justice, the defense of the draft law on anti-financing for the spread of weapons of mass destruction to the Internal Committee on Defense, National Assembly-Senate Relations, Senate Inspection and Public Works of the Senate has been approved. Assignment from the Royal Government.
It should be noted that the draft law on anti-financing for the spread of weapons of mass destruction aims to guarantee against money laundering and terrorist financing by defining measures to prevent, prevent, suppress and eliminate money laundering and terrorist financing.
This draft law has the following contents:
* From 2011-2015, the Royal Government of Cambodia has made great efforts to meet the recommendations of the Finance Working Group. As a result, the General Assembly of the Finance Working Group expressed its appreciation for the efforts and unanimously decided to remove Cambodia from the gray list on 26 February 2015.
* In 2016, the Asia-Pacific Group on Money Laundering conducted a second round of anti-money laundering and anti-terrorism financing and found that Cambodia still lacks some strategic shortcomings, such as lack of legal basis or measures to implement them. UN Resolution on Targeted Financial Sanctions for the Financing of the Holocaust
Objective: This law aims to ensure the prevention of money laundering and terrorist financing by defining measures to control, prevent, suppress and eliminate money laundering and terrorist financing.
(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police, on behalf of General Dr. Neth Savoeun, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police, presided over the handover ceremony on the afternoon of June 12, 2020. The rank of senior police chief of the National Police General Commission.
