(Foreign): Coffee is a beverage made from the seeds of a tropical green plant that originated in Africa. Coffee is one of the three most popular beverages in the world, including pure drinking water, and it is also one of the most lucrative international commodities.
Nowadays, there are many types of coffee, but this drink is especially popular because of the effect of its taste, which makes us drink and feel full of energy and bright spirit. This effect is caused by caffeine, an alkaline substance found in coffee drinks.
* The historical story of coffee
The coffee plant, probably from Ethiopia, was taken to southern Arabia and cultivated there in the 15th century. As coffee began to be grown in Arabia, Islamic authorities declared coffee to be an alcoholic beverage and therefore banned by the Qur'an. However, many Muslims became interested in the new beverage and drank it. Instead of alcohol.
Coffee was then introduced to European countries in the 16th and 17th centuries. By the end of the 17th century, "cafes" had spread throughout the United Kingdom and throughout the colonies in the Americas and throughout Europe.
Until the end of the 17th century, the world's coffee supply came almost entirely from Yemen, the only southern Arab country. But as coffee grew in popularity, the plant spread to other parts of the world, including Java and other islands in the Indonesian archipelago in the 17th century and to the Americas in the 18th century. Coffee cultivation began on the American island of Hawaii in 1825.
