Cambodian Red Cross Donates 1,313 Membership Certificates to Calmette Hospital
(Phnom Penh): Mrs. Pum Chantyny, Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross, received a hearing and handed over the 2020 Membership Certificate to Calmette Hospital.
The handover ceremony took place on June 11, 2020 at the Cambodian Red Cross Headquarters, with the participation of Prof. Koy Vanny, Chief of Technical Office of Calmette Hospital, Mr. Mao Rasey, Chief of Administration and participants. Some more.
In addition, she also thanked the management and staff of Calmette Hospital, in addition to providing excellent health services to the people, as well as participating as a member of the Cambodian Red Cross.
At the same time, Prof. Koy Vanny also expressed his deepest gratitude to His Excellency Dr. Bun Rany Hun Sen for giving the opportunity to the officials and staff of Calmette Hospital to participate in humanitarian activities to help the victims. Accident. In particular, he was very happy to contribute to reducing poverty and improving the well-being of Cambodians.
Please be informed that the Cambodian Red Cross has handed over the 2020 Membership Certificates to a total of 1,313 Calmette Hospitals. The total contribution of all members is 13,723,000 Riels and $ 155.
The members of the Cambodian Red Cross are: Supporting, active, supportive and honorary members. The membership budget of the annual membership is determined by categories such as: Honorary members from 2 million Riels and up, Assistant members from 800,000 Riels and Support members from 3,000 Riels to 200,000 Riels.
Donating one meal at a time can help a victim improve his or her life. Police seize 6 kinds of vegetables containing pesticide waste imported from Vietnam through Chrey Thom
(Kandal): On the morning of June 12, 2020, the authorities of Chrey Thom International Gate inspected the quality and safety of all kinds of fruits and vegetables brought by Cambodian traders from Vietnam to Cambodia through the Chrey Thom International Gate. In Chrey Thom village, Sampov Poun commune, Koh Thom district, Kandal province, six kinds of vegetables were found containing pesticide waste.
The operation was led by Mr. Muong Dara, Director of the Customs and Excise Office at Chrey Thom International Gate, and Mr. Ou Manrin, Head of the Consumer Protection Branch of the Anti-Fraud Competition (CPPCC) in collaboration with Mr. Se Chuntry, Head of the Gate Control Office. International Chrey Thom, Kandal Province to promote attention to the health of the people.
During the inspection, the police found 6 kinds of vegetables, including: Cabbage, Cauliflower, Corn, Small Lemon (for pickle tea), Pumpkin and Pomegranate, which contain unsafe pesticide residues. Use and do not allow temporary import. Apart from this, there are no toxic or deteriorating chemicals that can affect health, that is, good quality and safe to eat.
