White-tailed monkey, a rare animal in Stung Treng province, was shot dead, the suspect was arrested by the provincial military
(Stung Treng): A white-tailed monkey, a rare animal in Stung Treng province, was shot in the head and died on June 12, 2020 at the split point of Svay Rieng village, Talat commune, Sesan district, Stung Treng province.
Authorities confirmed that the suspect who shot and killed the white-tailed monkey was Nam Yon, 35, a farmer living in Svay Rieng village, Talat commune, Sesan district. The police confiscated 1 monkey (white-tailed monkey) and 1 recycled weapon (air rifle). After interrogation, the criminal experts of the Provincial Armed Forces handed over the suspects and exhibits to the environmental officer to continue the procedure.
According to the report, this white-tailed monkey is a rare species and in Stung Treng province, there are only five species.
Minister of Justice Defends Draft Law on Mutual Legal Assistance in Criminal Matters with Senate Legislative and Justice Committee
A meeting to clarify and defend the draft law on legal mutual assistance in the criminal field was held at the Senate.
It should be noted that the "Draft Law on Mutual Legal Aid in the Criminal Sector" was approved by the National Assembly by a vote of 108 to 111 in the 4th session of the 6th National Assembly, chaired by Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin. National Assembly on June 5, 2020. This draft law has 6 chapters and 44 articles, with the following contents:
Within the framework of legal cooperation in the field of criminal law, Cambodia has signed bilateral and multilateral treaties with many countries, especially treaties related to extradition, transfer of prisoners and mutual legal assistance in the field. Criminal.
At the same time, Cambodia has received requests for legal assistance in the field of criminal justice from many countries that have a treaty or agreement with Cambodia, but based on the principle of refusal, Cambodia has agreed to provide assistance in accordance with all these requests, because this is Important cooperation to contribute to the fight against crime, especially transnational crime, terrorism, as well as money laundering and terrorist financing.
Although Cambodia has provided legal assistance in the field of criminal law to many countries, including countries that have treaties with Cambodia and countries that have not had treaties with Cambodia in the past, Cambodia does not yet have a clear internal law to ensure The implementation of the request for mutual legal assistance in the field of criminal yet.
The purpose of this law is to provide legal assistance in the field of criminal affairs between Cambodia and foreign states in relation to criminal proceedings, as well as to freeze, seize, and confiscate property in order to strengthen and expand International cooperation.
