The victim was a child who jumped to his death on the Stung Meanchey flyover named Chan Meas Pisal, working for a private company. Currently living in Stung Meanchey, Sangkat Stung Meanchey II, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh. The victim is currently receiving emergency treatment at Lok Sang Hospital.
Information from the scene said that before the incident, they did not know what the victim was riding, suddenly saw the victim jump from the Stung Meanchey flyover and fall to the underground road, causing head injuries. He was taken to hospital by ambulance. Delegation of the Ministry of Health and the President of the World Health Organization in Cambodia visit a group of doctors and patients in Sambo district, Kratie province
(Kratie): Ms. O Vandin, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Health, and Ms. Li Ailan, President of the World Health Organization (WHO) in Cambodia on the evening of June 11, 2020, visited a group of doctors and patients. Who is being treated and giving birth in the health center of O'Kreang commune, Sambo district.
At the same time, the delegation also continued to meet with malaria program volunteers and to examine the actual situation in Kratie province related to the situation of COVID-19 for the second time, as well as malaria prevention measures. Will arrive soon in the rainy season.
Speaking on the occasion, Ms. O Vandin said that Kratie is an important tourist destination in the northeast of Cambodia, which today has been a large influx of national and international tourists and many tourists. Who are rushing to visit this province are negligent by not wearing the mask properly.
She called on Cambodians as well as national and international tourists not to forget proper hygiene by washing their hands with soap, alcohol or gel, wearing a mask properly, and applying better personal and social gaps. She instructed the authorities and professional officers to advise restaurant owners in resorts, guesthouses, hotels to clean regularly according to the instructions of health officials and authorities.
Where does the name Alaska come from? What is the history of this Alaska territory or state? Why did Russia foolishly sell Alaska to the United States? And how does Alaska bring prosperity to the United States? Please find out the following brief story.
During the colonization of North America, Russia also benefited from trade for some time, during 1812 the Russians also settled near the shores of Bodega, now in Also in California to profit from trade, but was pushed back to the north by British and US troops.
After the end of the civil war, talks between the United States and Russia on the sale of Alaska territory resumed, but seemed slow. It was not until April 1867 that the Senate ratified the Alaska Treaty by a one-vote majority.
Why Russia decided to sell Alaska to the United States: At that time, probably no Russians knew that "Alaska is a peninsula of gold and rich in oil resources under the sea." Alaska is just an Arctic ice cap, so they decided to sell it to the United States.
New breakthrough in Alaska: After being bought from the Russian Empire, Alaska is like a street child who was adopted by a rich man and hated by the children of the landlord because there are not many Americans living there. Far from the original homeland of the United States, the climate is very cold, unfavorable to longevity, and the government is not yet fully classified as a state.
Alaska State and Tourism Potential: With its growth to become the world's number one economic and arms power, Alaska has emerged as one of the most attractive ecotourism potentials as the 49th state is full of natural landscapes such as natural lakes. Beaches, Midnight of Sun, rivers, rivers, glaciers, wildlife and many other tourist attractions.
(Phnom Penh): The media and human rights organizations that receive money from the United States are now worthless because they do not dare to tell the truth about the crackdown on protesters in the United States and around the protests in Cambodia in the past. They spoke out in support of the US government and supported a brutal crackdown on protesters.
In contrast to the United States, China has taken this opportunity to show solidarity with the international community by announcing additional assistance to the WHO, as well as sending aid, including its experts, to many countries to help them fight COVID-19. In addition, as Donald Trump cuts US aid to countries around the world, Beijing is increasingly lending money to countries through "ring and road initiatives."
Belt and road initiatives have been claimed by China to benefit other countries, but critics, especially the United States, have often accused China of being a debt trap, despite repeated denials by Beijing.
So is it time for China to take over as world leader from the United States? Of course, a country that wants to be the number one power in the world does not just say one word and wants to become a leader immediately, that is, it needs to develop itself to be truly strong in all areas. First.
If China wants to be a world leader, it must have these five big points:
1: Economic power
A country with a strong economy but a weak military is usually threatened and persecuted by other military powers. Historical studies, for example, have already shown that the supremacy or power of an empire cannot exist without a strong military.
3: Ideology and values
Ideology and values are soft and necessary power for world leaders alike. Throughout history, many superpowers have collapsed because their values are not worthy of the world. Ideology and values are the fuel that burns leadership because it can persuade people to accept a system of leadership, not just in their own country or in the world.
4: Public-International Services
The capacity to provide public services here is meant to protect the international system and order, as well as universal law. Today, the United States is the world leader, not only leading the Allies to victory in World War II, but also leading the establishment of international institutions such as the United Nations to maintain order. Global.
Allies are also the most important factor. The reason the United States was able to defeat the Soviet Union in the Cold War was because of the alliance. In particular, the last important factor is opportunity and luck, as the Chinese proverb always says, "Opportunity to win, even if we want to lose, it is difficult." But as leaders, if they do not seize the opportunity in front of them, they will have to wait a long time for the second opportunity.
