(Banteay Meanchey): On June 11, 2020, Mr. Keat Hul, Governor of Poipet City, Colonel Thin Sindeth, Poipet City Police Inspector, Mr. San Vichea Saravuth, Chief of Banteay Meanchey Provincial Branch of Consumer Protection, Competition and Fraud, led the officers. Under the advice and authority of the police, they inspected the liquor store under the brand name "Tang Kuoy" after a dead person poisoned and confiscated 3999 bottles of wine.
Authorities and professional officers have been educating and preventing traffic and requesting traders to temporarily stop selling "Tang Kui" Chinese liquor and similar types of wine to customers in Phsar Thmey Fish Market, Poipet City and at wine depots around the market. Sangkat Poipet, Poipet City.
As a result, the authorities banned this type of alcohol and poisoned seven people in Mongkul Borei district, Malai district and Poipet city, Banteay Meanchey province.
Poipet Sangkat authorities have appealed to traders to cooperate with the authorities to temporarily stop selling the above brands and ask people who used to drink this type of wine to stop immediately because it could endanger their lives and families by waiting. Wait for professional officials from ministries and institutions to do the proper testing before selling or buying to drink.
Please note that this terrible incident happened on the evening of June 9, 2020. After the inspection, the officers confiscated a total of 3,999 bottles of Chinese wine, equivalent to 1,995 liters.
The Department of Infectious Diseases of the Ministry of Health has once again warned alcoholics to be careful when buying alcohol and to buy clear-sourced wine with proper supervision by experts and drink to a minimum.
The Department of Infectious Diseases requested the relevant institutions and local authorities to strengthen inspections of handicrafts and wineries. In particular, eliminate unlicensed wineries from professional institutions. To help prevent alcohol poisoning, the Department of Infectious Diseases claims that the Ministry of Health has worked with the relevant ministries to organize public awareness campaigns to understand the risks posed by alcohol consumption.
In the past, cases of alcohol poisoning were claimed by officials to be caused by the use of high levels of methanol. New Beijing airport launches first freight flight
BEIJING, June 11 (Xinhua) - The new Daxing International Airport in Beijing, China, will receive its first cargo flight on Thursday, June 11, 2020, since its official opening in September last year. 2019. This is according to the release by the Chinese news agency Xinhua.
Daxing International Airport, shaped like a starfish, was built in 2008 and officially opened in 2019 (after five years of construction at a cost of more than $ 11 billion). In addition to regular pick-up and drop-off, Daxing also has 24 berths for cargo planes. Vietnam Airlines to resume flights to Cambodia in July
In a statement issued by Vietnam Airlines on June 11, 2020, the resumption of flights is scheduled to begin on July 2.
A representative of Vietnam Airlines told Vietnam News Agency that the company is in detailed discussions with the Vietnamese Civil Aviation Secretariat, the Ministry of Transport and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and the Ministry of Health to find ways to reopen flights in accordance with the instructions of the Vietnamese Prime Minister.
A representative of Vietnam Airlines said the company would issue an official announcement to the public after a final agreement was reached with the parties.
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of June 11, 2020, under the assignment of the Royal Government, Mr. Keut Rith, Minister of Justice, accompanied by leaders and senior officials of the National Bank of Cambodia and the Ministry of Interior, attended a meeting to clarify and protect Draft Law on Anti-Money Laundering and Terrorist Financing with the Senate Economic, Financial, Banking and Audit Committee headed by Chea Cheth.
According to the Ministry of Justice, a meeting to clarify and defend the draft law on anti-money laundering and terrorist financing took place in the Senate.
It should be noted that in the plenary session chaired by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on Friday morning, May 15, 2020, the Council of Ministers decided to approve the draft law on anti-sanitation. "Money and terrorist financing."
This draft law is based on the Law on Anti-Money Laundering and Terrorist Financing of 2007 and the Law on the Amendment of Articles 3, 29 and 30 of the Law on Anti-Money Laundering and Terrorist Financing 2013 as a basis. Including the National Anti-Money Laundering Strategy and Terrorist Financing 2019-2023 and the FATF 2012 Standards Recommendations of strategic importance.
Minister of Labor requests Swiss Agency for Development and Cooperation to establish distance education system for technical and vocational education and training
The meeting has two main objectives:
Mr. Ith Sam Heng requested development partners and stakeholders, especially the Swiss Agency for Development and Cooperation, to continue to support the process of drafting the law on technical and vocational education and training, both technically and financially, until it is approved. For official use.
In order to achieve quality and efficient human resources or skilled labor to meet the needs of the labor market, especially to support the development goals of 2030 in line with the Industrial Revolution 4.0, Minister Ith Sam Heng recommended the meeting, including:
1: Continue to strengthen the quality of education, technical and vocational training to meet the needs of the labor market.
2: Continue to expand technical and vocational education and training to support economic and social development through online or offline curriculum. 3. Continue to strengthen public-private partnerships and partners to ensure the sustainability of technical and vocational education and training.
4: Continue to improve the governance system of education, technical and vocational training.
5: Continue to promote research and technology implementation in the field of technical and vocational education and training.
