Minister of Commerce: Safe food market process helps increase productivity and profitability of farmers in natural vegetables and meat
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, stated that in order to promote the production of safe vegetables, poultry and agro-trade, safe vegetables for farmers and the market, the Ministry of Commerce has led the implementation of the market promotion project for scale agriculture. Small and facilitated public-private partnerships to enhance productivity and profitability of farmers.
He said that the opening of a safe food market, which supports the field of vegetables and natural meat of farmers now will help increase productivity and profitability for farmers as well.
Mr. Pan Sosak stated that the project to promote the market for small-scale agriculture and food safety market will improve the value chain and agro-commercial products, safe vegetables and chicken, especially to facilitate farmers to support the plan. Vegetable production, chicken, meat and agro-trade, vegetable trade and marketing.
He added that the vegetable and chicken market is one of the key players in the agribusiness value chain, and not just the food safety market, but all markets, please focus. Pay attention to the quality of vegetables and chicken products in its market, because quality plays a very important role for competitiveness and long-term strategy.
Taking the opportunity to launch this food safety market, Mr. Pan Sosak recommended the market promotion project for small-scale agriculture and the food safety market to work well together to accelerate the development of agro-trade value chain, vegetables and chickens. To promote the prosperity of smallholder farmers by increasing their profits by connecting agribusiness, vegetable and poultry trade and markets.
Mr. Pan Sosak strongly hopes that the cooperation in strengthening the development of agro-commercial value chain, vegetables and poultry will contribute to the increase of agro-commercial products in both quantity and quality in the market for service. Need safe vegetables and broilers for the people, taking into account the welfare of the people and reduce the consumption of vegetables and broilers without a clear source.
Please be informed that KCCV Plantation has established this food safety market with the vision of how to contribute to society to make farmers have regular income, reduce migration, especially health. The people of Cambodia and to help the people and youth of Cambodia to have jobs and help Cambodian farmers to expand their business of growing vegetables, fish, meat and rice.
This safe food market brings vegetables, fish, meat from pure farming communities, all of which have received proper technical training from the Ministry of Commerce and are accredited by the World Health Organization to help. People can create a small market for selling natural vegetables, fish, meat without chemicals banned.
Ms. Mithona Phuthong shows the progress of Koh Kong province through the press conference of the Royal Government Spokesperson's Office (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Ms. Mithona Phouthong, Governor of Koh Kong Province, this morning, June 11, 2020 Achievements and progress of the province through a press conference organized by the Spokesperson of the Royal Government on "Progress and direction of the work of the administration of Koh Kong."
Koh Kong province is divided into 1 city, 6 districts, 29 communes, sangkats and 119 villages with a total area of 10,045.58 square kilometers, a total of 30,385 families, a total population of 136,320 people, 67,984 females. 13 people per square kilometer. About 57.5% of the population are farmers, relying on agriculture as the main source of livelihood for the people in the province.
Apart from agriculture, which is the core sector, there are other sectors such as industry 0.2% and service sector about 42.3%, which is the basis for creating jobs for people. The three main economic sectors: agriculture, industry and services have boosted the province's economy, with significant growth rates.
In particular, for the progress of work and achievements in 2019, Ms. Mithona Phu Thong presented as follows:
* Mineral Resources and Energy: Koh Kong Province has 3 large hydropower plants with a total power of 602 MW and solar panels in some areas. The three hydropower sites are Kirirom 3 with 18 MW in Dong Peng commune, Sre Ambel district, Russey Chrum Krom with 338 MW and Tatai with 246 MW.
* Tourism: Due to the peaceful factors and the rich potential of natural resources, Koh Kong province has developed a lot in tourism, including vacation areas, ecotourism areas, mangrove forests, waterfalls, coastal areas, coral reefs and some islands and services. Tourism such as: hotels, guesthouses, restaurants, entertainment centers.
* Land administration work: Registered and issued certificates of identification of real estate owners to the people, including: 7,759 separate land registrations, 53 state land registrations, and land registration in the form of The system under Regulation No. 1 issued 5,334 cards and the systematic land registration system issued 7,272 cards.
