Phnom Penh Authority Plans to Relocate Landfill Site from Dangkor District to New Location Along Street 51 in Ang Snoul District, Kandal Province
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Municipal Authority plans to move the landfill site along Street 51 in Kandal province's Ang Snoul district, and the current landfill site in Dangkor district will be retained as a landfill transfer site. This was confirmed by the Phnom Penh Municipal Authority in the 13th Ordinary Meeting of the Phnom Penh Capital Council this morning, June 11 at Phnom Penh Capital Hall.
Mr. Khuong Sreng said that when we transfer to the new landfill, the old landfill in Dangkor district will be used as a landfill. In addition, we have selected three other waste transfer locations on the outskirts of Phnom Penh, including two in Prey Pnov, one in Sen Sok and one in Por Sen Chey.
Mr. Khuong Sreng also confirmed that the Phnom Penh Capital Administration has already bid for three garbage transport companies, and after the three companies have carried out their work, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration will take strict measures against those who do not pay. Garbage will also have measures against squatters.
It should be noted that the above meeting of Phnom Penh Capital Council was held in the presence of Mr. Pa Socheatvong, Chairman of Phnom Penh Capital Council and Mr. Khuong Sreng, accompanied by Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, as well as the participation of some relevant officials to urge the Phnom Penh Capital Administration to allow Better jobs, both in terms of building infrastructure and providing public services to the people.
The confirmation of the Prime Minister of India was made during a telephone conversation with Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the afternoon of June 10, 2020. This is according to a press release from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation.
A statement issued by Fresh News on June 11, 2020 stated: "The two leaders are also committed to further strengthening and deepening bilateral cooperation by the Prime Minister. "India considers Cambodia an important part of India's eastward policy."
According to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, the two leaders also pledged to further strengthen regional cooperation, including the ASEAN-India and Mekong-Ganges frameworks. Regarding cultural and archeological cooperation, Prime Minister Modi expressed his satisfaction with India's trust in co-chairs the International Coordinating Committee for the Restoration and Development of Cambodia's Preah Vihear Temple.
It should be noted that the Act East Polocy policy is implemented through four areas: protection of Indian Ocean security, integration with Southeast Asia, deepening of strategic partnership with implementation. The balance between the great powers and the management of the conflict with China.
Sihanoukville needs more than $ 1.5 million to end landmine and mine impact
(Preah Sihanouk): Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Deputy Chairman of the Mines Authority, said that Sihanoukville province has more than 5.5 square kilometers of land affected by mines and munitions and needs about 1.5 million dollars. US to end landmine and mine casualties.
This statement was made on the occasion of Senior Minister Ly Thuch presiding over the closing ceremony of a commemorative training course on the use of tablets to collect data on mine / cluster mine survey data for Mapu officials in 19 provinces on June 11, 2020.
The training was attended by Mr. Kong Vithanak, Deputy Governor of Sihanoukville and Chairman of the Provincial Mine Action Committee, leaders, staff, staff of the Mine Authority, DFID project officers and officials of the Mine Action Project (CFR).
On behalf of Samdech Techo Prime Minister and Chairman of the Mine Authority, Senior Minister Ly Thuch commended and thanked the 25 officials of the Mine Action Planning Working Group (MAPO) for their active participation in coordinating mine activities in the provincial capitals. Each to meet the real needs of the community, work to develop and contribute to reducing the risk of landmines and explosive remnants of war.
At the same time, Senior Minister Ly Thuch requested all Mapu officials to continue to pay close attention and cooperate more closely with all stakeholders on mine action and be ready to address any challenges related to landmines and Explosive remnants of war in their jurisdiction, in particular, must join the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Prime Minister in achieving the goal of Cambodia no 2025.
Before concluding the session, the Senior Minister made six recommendations to strengthen leadership and achieve high efficiency, including:
* 1: Understand the goals, strategies, policies and procedures of the organization * 2: Ensure the quality of work efficiency by spending time and budget in accordance with the goals * 3: Increase awareness of the environment and their duties. * 4: Prepare goals and plans on a regular basis * 5: To maintain well-being and harmony in the unit * 6: To solve small problems first before preparing to solve strategic problems.
