Beijing recently issued a warning message advising Chinese people to avoid traveling to Australia due to concerns about racism and violence against Chinese people during the COVID-19 outbreak. However, in a national radio interview on Thursday, Australian Prime Minister Scott Morrison dismissed China's claim that it was ridiculous.
Tensions between China and Australia have been heating up in recent years as Australia has joined the United States in criticizing and blocking China's expansion of influence in the Pacific. Tensions escalated after Australia rejoined Washington, calling for an investigation into the origins and resolution of China's COVID-19 crisis when the disease first broke out.
BEIJING: A new study released on Tuesday shows that the northern end of the Great Wall of China was built not to resist the invasion of the Mongol Empire, but to monitor population movements. On the contrary.
The findings come after Israeli, Mongolian and US researchers spent time researching a detailed map of the 740-kilometer-long Northern Line of the Great Wall of China, most of which stretches across Mongolia.
(Phnom Penh): The trend of car use in Cambodia today seems to have changed to some extent due to changes in living standards and safety in travel. According to a report by the Automobile Association of Cambodia, affluent people are now turning to new cars instead of used cars.
The reasons why they started using new cars are:
As the rainy season approaches, there will be heavy rain mixed with slippery, muddy road conditions and difficulty driving when it is raining, which can cause you to blur long distances, which can lead to accidents. Travel of Cambodians.
With all these reasons, it is easy to consider that you should use a new car to get many benefits for your family and loved ones. Banteay Meanchey, Battambang Provincial Leaders and Tycoon Leng Navattra Launch $ 4.6 Million Road from Malai to Sampov Loun District
(Banteay Meanchey): A 22-kilometer road connecting Malai district, Banteay Meanchey province to Sampov Loun district, Battambang province, worth up to 4.6 million USD, was opened for construction on June 10, 2020. Contributing to greater economic strength, especially faster transportation and travel between the two border provinces.
The groundbreaking ceremony was held in the presence of Mr. Kheng Su, Chairman of Banteay Meanchey Provincial Council, Mr. Ou Rathrey, Provincial Governor, Mr. Hoeung Sokun, Deputy Governor of Battambang Province and Mr. Oknha Leng Navattra, as well as leaders and officers of the People's Armed Forces. Many others.
Brigadier General Tek Bunthoeun, a representative of Western Steel Company, said that a road that is currently under construction is 22 kilometers long and 30 meters wide, connecting O'Ampil village, Tuol Pong commune, Malai district, Banteay Meanchey province to Banteay Sam, Trao Chou village, commune. Serey Meanchey, Sampov Loun District, Battambang Province.
Taking this opportunity, he also apologized to the people who were affected by the development of the company, but this development is to make the people have easy access to the road, and in addition to the 30-meter road above, there is a 20-meter road. More that the company plans to develop for future use.
Mr. Ou Rathrey said, "This is a source of pride for Banteay Meanchey and Battambang provinces, we have received the development of this new road for people to use to travel according to their needs and would like to thank the West Steele Company. Contributed to the development of Banteay Meanchey as well as Cambodia.
At the same time, he also instructed the authorities and the working group to continue to help people who are suffering and affected by the effects of Kovid-19 and asked the people themselves to be very careful about Kovid-19. And please continue to follow the instructions of the Ministry of Health to keep clean by washing your hands with alcohol, gel, alcohol or soap and to wear a mask every time you go out, especially to fight against Kovid-19.
In response to the opening of the road construction site, the people applauded and expressed their happiness that the company has taken into account the people, and this road has really benefited them a lot, both for travel and transport of agricultural products. They. At the end of the program, souvenirs were distributed to 1,200 people participating in the program.
France pledges continued training of Cambodian Blue Hat troops and military police
In addition to helping to continue training the Blue Hat Army and helping to train the Cambodian Gendarmerie, the two sides also continue to examine the possibility of signing a third Memorandum of Understanding in the future. The ambassador also highlighted the importance of relations, strengthening cooperation between the two countries and better armies.
The White Paper, after its publication, received rave reviews from the public. Some people have suggested that the White Paper is a kind of statement because it reflects the idea of preventing the virus in China, which has a large population. Some people also mentioned it as a timely help book because it shared China's experience and knowledge in preventing the virus to the world without any secret.
Some people say it is a battle order because it encourages people to be ready to fight the virus for a long time. Some say it is a military signal to Chongfeng because it calls on the international community to unite in the face of this century's catastrophe. Taking this opportunity, I would like to share some of my personal feelings and personal opinions with you all.
China has quickly dealt with the country's resources and strength, and has taken precise and comprehensive measures to prevent any valuable sacrifices in order to preserve the lives of its people.
In the face of an outbreak of the virus, control the spread of the virus until the number of virus-carrying cases is reduced to the number achieved in the Wuhan War and the Hubei War. To achieve the normalization of viral diseases across the country, the effectiveness of the prevention of viral diseases in China has been remarkable.
As of 24 May 30, the cure rate for COVID-19 was 94.3%. In order to preserve the health and life of the Chinese people, these greatest sacrifices in spirit and life have been recorded in the most exciting history ever.
The fight against the virus in China is documented in the White Paper, showing the great strength of the people. From Chinese New Year (Chuxi) to March 8, 346 national medical teams, more than 40,000 doctors and more than 900 public health teams traveled to Hubei to help.
During the outbreak, more than 4 million local teams worked at the first gate of 650,000 villages, communes and cities across the country to prevent the spread of the disease. This one virus. Freight forwarders, environmental protection workers, road transport workers, journalists, loyalists and team members from all walks of life have worked tirelessly and without hesitation.
As of May 31, more than 8.81 million people have registered to participate in virus prevention activities across China. Over 460,000 projects, recording the number of hours of service of loyalists, more than 290 million hours.
"The difficult journey in the fight against the virus in China is a shared memory engraved in the hearts of more than one Chinese people," a spokesman for the State Council Information Office said at a news conference. .4 billion. The people are the biggest confidence and source of strength for China in the fight against the virus.
China conducts surveys on epidemics using big data, smart AI and other technologies. China is currently deploying special forces across the country to develop key components of viral disease control technology to accelerate research and rapid deployment, and has launched 83 emergency research projects.
It is believed that through research, vaccines will be found more and more, people's livelihoods will be restored to normal soon. The fight against the virus in China is recorded in the book. White represents the core idea of building a community of common destiny.
In the aftermath of the virus outbreak, China has maintained the idea of a common destiny, a responsible and high-performing community, showing the responsibility of the superpowers to stand shoulder to shoulder with the countries involved.
By: Wang Winthean, Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia June 11, 2020
(Rattanakiri): Ms. O Vandin, Spokesperson and Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, and Ms. Ailian Li, President of the World Health Organization (WHO) in Cambodia, on 11 June 2020, continued their mission to inspect the Level 1 and Level 2 Centers in Kon Mom District. And check out Hang Anh Banana Farm Company as well.
Attending the event were the Director, Deputy Director of the Department of Health, Director of the Provincial Department of Labor and Vocational Training, the Governor of Kon Mom District and other relevant officials.
Dr. Ung Ratana, Director of the Ratanakkiri Provincial Health Department, informed the working group that under the leadership of Mr. Thong Savun, Provincial Governor and Chairman of the Ratanakkiri Kovid-19 Commission for the Prevention of Epidemic, the medical team responded immediately. (RRT) Collaborate with relevant units and authorities at all levels, partner organizations to prepare back-up equipment and response plans in case of Kovid-19 outbreak.
Meanwhile, Mr. Duch Chanto, Director of the Department of Labor and Vocational Training, also informed the working group about the situation of workers working in Hang Anh banana plantation by keeping them clean, such as washing their hands with soap or alcohol, working at a distance. Separately, they must be checked in and out of the plantation regularly, if there is any suspicion, they should be kept separately for 14 days for health check.
Speaking on the occasion, Ms. O Vandin and Ms. Ailan Li praised and appreciated the efforts of Ratanakkiri Province to prevent this epidemic, especially the frontline public health workers who are actively fighting Kovid-19. .
However, the Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health urged the provincial authorities to be more vigilant as the disease has not yet decreased worldwide, with the participation of all circles in the province to prevent the spread of the tidal wave. 2 of this disease. Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth will officially launch an online business registration system early next week.
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, will officially launch the "Online Business Registration System" on Monday next week.
This is according to the invitation letter of the Deputy Prime Minister sent to the ministers of some ministries and institutions to participate in this important program.
Please be informed that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has just issued a new sub-decree on business registration through information technology. This sub-decree aims to facilitate and create a good environment for business creation through business registration through information technology to contribute to improving the business environment and attracting investment in Cambodia.
* Business registration by the Ministry of Commerce * Tax registration by the General Department of Taxation of the Ministry of Economy and Finance * Examination and receipt of enterprise opening announcement by the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training Qualifications by Council for the Development of Cambodia.
Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Secretary General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, considered the launch of the online business registration system to be a major step that will enable investors to register only once. One technology nursery means that when registration is required, it can be done remotely without having to spend time in person at the ministry.
Nearly 1,000 luxury saplings are planted on the grounds of the Cambodian Buddhist Cultural Center in Suramarit Kosamak Kirirom National Park.
(Kampong Speu): Nearly 1,000 luxury saplings were planted on the grounds of the Cambodian Buddhist Cultural Center in Preah Suramarit Kosamak Kirirom National Park, Phnom Sruoch District, Kampong Speu Province in the presence of Dr. Mok Mareth, Member of National Assembly and Constituency MP. Takeo Neak Oknha Thombandit Moha Upasika Nhek Buntha, President of the Cambodian Buddhist Cultural Center, Mrs. Hun Sinath and many nearby Buddhists.
Oknha Thombandit Moha Upasika Nhek Buntha said that the planting of trees now to celebrate the Royal Tree Day in July and the contribution of the Royal Government to maintain and preserve the forest for a long time. Long, in particular, wants to show all Cambodian children to know and recognize the different types of rare trees, as well as inspire people to love and protect the natural environment.
Neak Oknha Thombandit also mentioned the construction process of the Cambodian Buddhist Cultural Center, which is currently under construction, despite the 19 epidemics of Kovid, and all the construction on this 100-hectare area is Preserved all kinds of forests, which are suitable as a storehouse of Buddhist festivals and as a storehouse of national art and culture.
Speaking at a press conference on the progress and direction of the Koh Kong Provincial Administration, organized by the spokesperson of the Royal Government, Ms. Mithona Phu Thong, denied that the airport serves the military, claiming that the new airport aims to serve For tourism and business.
