With the advent of the ARPAnet, US military scientists and experts were particularly concerned about the possibility of an attack on the US telephone network by the Soviet Union. They fear that a single missile can destroy all the telephone lines that are so important for long-distance communication.
(Phnom Penh): According to the results of the census of vultures across Cambodia, there are 3 species present in the protected area, a total of 119, including 11 fire vultures, 71 gray vultures and 37 brown vultures.
This is the announcement of a senior official of the Ministry of Environment on June 11, 2020, after the census of vultures across Cambodia was conducted at four different locations on June 10, 2020.
First: Cheb Wildlife Sanctuary in Preah Vihear Province has a total of 34 vultures: 3 fire vultures, 22 gray vultures and 9 brown vultures. Second: Siem Pang Wildlife Sanctuary in Stung Treng Province has a total of 81 vultures. 4 fire vultures, 49 gray vultures and 28 brown vultures Third: Sre Pok Wildlife Sanctuary, Mondulkiri Province There are 4 fire vultures and no vultures are present in Sre Pok Wildlife Sanctuary, Kratie Province.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that the results of the vulture census in 2019 showed that Cambodia has 137 species of vultures, and the area with the most vultures is in the Siem Pang Wildlife Sanctuary in Stung Treng and Den. Cheb Wildlife Sanctuary in Preah Vihear Province.
He also said that the current census of vultures is important to know the true number of vultures in Cambodia and the development situation around the number of vultures in Cambodia.
Vultures are a rare species and are at high risk of extinction globally as the number of vultures continues to decline each year and to a worrying extent, despite the Royal Government through the Ministry of Environment in collaboration with NGOs. Partners strive to protect and conserve.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that the reasons why vultures in Cambodia are declining due to the greatest threat from human pollution, loss of habitat, lack of food, hunting through traps.
He said that communities in some areas have used poisons in or around ponds to catch birds and mammals, and that pollution is also a major cause of vulture deaths. Eat the carcasses of dead animals due to poison.
Because vultures are endangered in the world and Cambodia is known to have the largest number of vultures left, the Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment said that the Ministry of Environment has partnered with the Wildlife Conservation Society (WCS). Implemented conservation activities in protected areas through supplementary feeding and protection of nesting nests, increasing in-depth understanding of vulture risk factors.
Cambodia promotes conservation of whispers or peacocks as this bird has very little in the world
(Kampong Thom): Whistleblowers in Cambodia promote the conservation of Whistle Peacocks or turtles to increase biodiversity and serve ecotourism, while the presence of this bird remains minimal in the world.
The Northern Tonle Sap Lowland Protected Area is an area located in the seasonal floodplain grasslands and is located in Kampong Thom and Siem Reap provinces. According to a study by wildlife scientists, this area is important for hummingbirds to live and reproduce.
According to Sum Phearun, Technical Advisor of the Wildlife Conservation Project of the Cambodian Wildlife Conservation Society (WCS), the conservation of this rare bird can be done by maintaining a grassland sanctuary in the lowlands of the Tonle Sap Basin. As a source of food and they lay eggs in the dry season.
He said the estimated number of whispers in Cambodia in 2018 was about 104 after the 2007 census, which was about 370, accounting for 57.14 percent of the world's total. Cambodia is one of the countries in India, Nepal and Bangladesh where the species is present in the world.
According to Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment, most of the whispers in Cambodia live in the Tonle Sap Lake area and can only lay two eggs at a time, which requires conservation and protection from various threats. .
It should be noted that the Ministry of Environment and the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, together with the Forest and Wildlife Conservation Organization, have cooperated to support people living in the Tonle Sap North Plains Protected Area to participate in protecting and conserving whispers through habitat protection. And stop hunting all kinds of animals.
Nhep Nheun, community coordinator of the WCS Whistle Conservation Project, said that in this protected area, people can earn $ 40 from the whistle nests per nest.
According to the Ministry of Environment, the Northern Tonle Sap Lowland Protected Area covers more than 30,000 hectares (31,159 hectares) in Kampong Thom and Siem Reap provinces and is the last habitat for the Whistle in Cambodia.
In 2016, the Royal Government of Cambodia transferred 18 protected areas and conservation areas from the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to the Ministry of Environment. To strengthen the management and conservation work, the Ministry of Environment has requested the Royal Government of Cambodia to organize the Whistle Conservation Areas in Kampong Thom and Siem Reap Provinces by sub-decree dated May 9, 2016 on an area of 31,159 hectares.
It should also be noted that the Northern Tonle Sap Lowland Protected Area is part of the Tonle Sap Lake Biosphere Reserve by Royal Decree No. NS / RKOT / 0401/070, dated April 10, 2001. On the other hand, the Tonle Sap Lake Biosphere Reserve is receiving a lot of attention from UNESCO. Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth inaugurates the construction site of rural infrastructure and supports farmers.
The event was attended by senior representatives of ministries and agencies implementing the project, including: Ministry of Rural Development, Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, Electricite du Cambodge, Kampong Thom Provincial Governor, and representatives of relevant departments of the target provinces. June 11, 2020.
2: Development of agricultural and rural infrastructure, including: roads, canals for irrigation, and low-cost electricity connection to agricultural pumping stations.
The first phase of the labor cash project was implemented for three years from 2017 to 2019 with a total budget of 215.4 billion riels and covers 12 target provinces, including: Kampong Chhnang, Kampong Thom, Kampong Speu, Takeo, Battambang, Pursat, Prey Veng, Siem Reap, Svay Rieng, Oddar Meanchey, Kandal and Banteay Meanchey.
The project has been successfully implemented so far, the project to build 688 km of rural roads, rehabilitate and build canals to drain water to farmers through a total cash program of 1,140 km. The total number of beneficiaries from the project is about 937,335, of which 254,129 workers participated in the cash program, each receiving between 300,000 and more than 1,000,000. Riel.
Taking the opportunity to meet with workers, farmers and people who are the beneficiaries of the project, the General Doctor appreciated and appreciated the efforts of the Ministry-Institution as a project implementation agency and the active participation of the people. All beneficiaries who have contributed to the implementation of the first phase of the cash flow project to achieve the planned success.
In addition, the Royal Government recently decided to implement the fourth round of measures to continue to manage the impact on key sectors of the national economy in the context of the crisis and the rehabilitation and promotion of Cambodia's economic growth after the Kovid crisis. 19 In that measure, Samdech Techo Prime Minister decided to increase the budget for the implementation of the labor cash project in 2020 from 150 billion riels to 410 billion riels.
According to the new plan, by 2020, the project will be able to absorb 890,000 short-term lost workers, build 2,255 km of roads, 2,384 km of canals and connect the network. Electricity to 45 agricultural pumping stations. The population benefiting from these infrastructures is 957,000 households.
He emphasized that the cash flow program, which is being implemented under the direct consideration and leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, is very important for Cambodia's current socio-economic situation, especially in an environment where the world Moul is in crisis of Kovid 19 disease.
He also brought greetings and greetings from Samdech Techo Prime Minister and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, both of whom always pay attention to the lives of the people.
(Preah Vihear): Speaking from the north of Cambodia in Preah Vihear province, Mr. Net Pheaktra, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Environment, confirmed that vultures, giant trout, white-tailed deer and other rare species have contributed to attracting national tourists. And more and more internationals are visiting Cambodia to contribute to boosting the community economy.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra made this statement on the occasion of leading a delegation of the Ministry of Environment and a group of nearly 20 national journalists, the institution to review the implementation of the Wildlife Conservation and Conservation Project of the Wildlife Association of Cambodia (WCS) last June 9-10, 2020 in Kulen-Prohm Tep Wildlife Sanctuary and Chep Wildlife Sanctuary in Preah Vihear Province.
He said that in addition to growing organic rice, people in the community have established a community of vultures Bei Thoeun Deum Krasang, which in one year they can earn more than 30,000 dollars to support the operation in their community. He and so on.
He added that the participation in the conservation of natural resources, the participation in the conservation of wildlife, the tourism community of Thmat Bei Thoeun Deum Krasang made them all earn income from organic rice cultivation, bringing national and international visitors to see wildlife and selling things. Memories of these tourists have contributed to boosting the local economy by cutting down deforestation and hunting.
Dip Kim On, president of the 50-year-old Blair tourism community, said that in order to protect the forest and wildlife for future generations, he had been actively involved in the Thmat Bei ecotourism community from the beginning as a committee member. He led community members on forest patrols and organized meetings to educate villagers about the importance of forests and wildlife.
"At first I thought it was very difficult to change my mind and make the villagers understand the importance of forests and wildlife because they depend on all those natural resources to survive," he said. Live for many years. "But I am determined to solve this problem in order to protect the natural resources around the village for the next generation of children."
In 2006, Mr. Dib Kim On was elected by community members to be the president of the Thmat Bei ecotourism community. In this role, he led community members to protect the forest and wildlife and expand the ecotourism project in Thmat Bei to help community members find additional income to feed their families.
This ecotourism project is progressing well, with the number of tourists coming to Thmat Bei increasing every year. In 2019, many international and national tourists came to Thmat Bei, which helped the tourism community earn more than 30,000 USD for the village development project.
The Prime Minister of India praised Samdech Techo Hun Sen in a telephone conversation on June 10, 2020 yesterday.
According to the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs, during the telephone conversation, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Madi focused on the fight against Kovid 19. The Prime Minister paid tribute to the efforts of Madi and the Government of India in the fight against Kovid 19 and also offered condolences for the loss of life of Indians due to Kovid 19.
Kovid 19 is an infectious disease that has spread rapidly around the world. As of June 11, 2020, more than 7 million people have been infected and nearly 420,000 people have died from the disease.
For Cambodia, 126 cases were found. Of those, 125 were cured and only one was treated and no one was killed.
According to this data, it is estimated that the management of the 19 cases of Kovid in Cambodia is better and more effective, leading to the transmission is not as strong as in other countries.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen is considered the Supreme Commander in the Battle of Kovid 19. Since the first case of Kovid 19 in Cambodia in January, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has been paying close attention to the most realistic and precise measures and measures.
Measures and measures that are timely and clear response to prevent the spread of disease from outside, prevent the spread and treatment efforts of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, accompanied by the careful implementation of the army and officials Involved only to improve the management of Kovid 19 disease situation like this.
The excellent results of the management of the 19 cases of Kovid have been praised by the World Health Organization and some other countries.
On June 12, a plane will transport 60 Cambodian citizens and students from India to Cambodia. And on June 11, Indians will return to the country and the other leg will transport 280 Indians back home on June 19, 2020.
At the same time, the two leaders agreed that moving forward to restore the socio-economic situation in the aftermath of the Kovid 19 crisis requires greater international cooperation and coordination.
The figure is the highest ever, with new infections and daily deaths in the South Asian country. Adding to the above figures, it brings the total number of cases across India to 2,286,579, with 8,102 deaths and 141,029 recovering. This brings the total number of active or inpatient patients in the hospital to 137,448.
A telephone conversation between the Prime Ministers of the two friendly countries was held on June 10, 2020, during which the two leaders discussed the COVID-19 pandemic and agreed to continue cooperation. To help its people abroad and facilitate their evacuation.
According to the Indian Embassy, Narendra Modi has expressed India's commitment to strengthening its relationship with Cambodia, a key member of ASEAN and a friendly country with similar civilization and cultural ties with India.
The two leaders reviewed the strong development partnerships between the two countries, including capacity building programs under the Indian Economic Technical Cooperation (ITEC) and Rapid Revenue Projects under the Mekong-Ganges Cooperation Framework.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stressed the importance of Cambodia paying attention to its relations with India. At the same time, the Prime Minister also responded with emotion and emphasized Cambodia's valuable role in India's Eastern law policy.
In this telephone conversation, the Prime Minister of India praised Samdech Techo and the Royal Government of Cambodia for the good management of Kovid 19, which can be a model for the world.
The following is a press release from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs:
Senior Minister Cham Prasidh hands over Royal Decree, sub-decree and proclamation to 42 senior officials and civil servants in the Ministry
(Phnom Penh): After the Ministry of Industry and Handicraft was renamed by the Royal Government to the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation recently, the re-appointment of officials of the former Ministry was repeated.
In fact, on the morning of June 11, 2020, a ceremony was held to hand over the Royal Decree, Sub-Decree and Proclamation to 42 senior officials and civil servants of the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation from the level of Director General to the Heads of Departments and Heads of 25 Departments in Phnom Penh. The province is chaired by Mr. Kittisetha Dr. Cham Prasidh, Senior Minister, Minister of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation at the Ministry.
This ceremony is to re-appoint old officials and facilitate duties and appoint civil servants under the General Department of Science, Technology and Innovation and the National Institute of Science, Technology and Innovation, which is the General Department and the National Institute was established in line with the establishment of the new Ministry. This. Separately, Mr. Chhem Keat Rithy, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, also participated in the honor of presiding over the occasion.
Mr. Son Sotha, Delegate of the Royal Government of Cambodia in charge of the Director General of General Affairs, confirmed that the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation was formally established by the Royal Government's decision through Royal Decree No. NS / RKAM / 0320/009 dated. March 26, 2020, accompanied by Sub-Decree No. 48 of the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation, dated April 6, 2020.
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Forestry Administration has brought all kinds of trees to plant in the campus of Boeung Trabek High School to make Phnom Penh a green city, especially for the whole campus to have a fresh environment to improve the environment for students. Take in the fresh air of the trees.
The planting of all kinds of trees took place this morning, June 11, 2020, at Boeung Trabek High School, with the participation of students, teachers and many forestry administration officials.
Mr. Koam Seiha continued that every year, the Phnom Penh Forestry Administration always planted more trees in the high school area of Wat Aram Hospital.
"Planting trees on campus will not only provide shade for students, it will help reduce climate change on the planet and help eliminate toxins on campus as well as Phnom Penh," he said. .
At the same time, the Director of Phnom Penh Forestry Administration also asked all students and people to plant trees and take care of the trees that have been planted to grow well, because trees are important for human life, animals and biodiversity of all kinds, especially as a barrier. The flood barrier will also bring rainwater to increase human livelihoods.
Ministry of Education Allows Higher Education Institutions for Online Admissions and Graduation Exams during Kovid 19
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has sent a letter to the Rector of the Institute under the auspices of the Ministry of Education regarding the permission of higher education institutions to accept students for the online graduation exam during the epidemic. Of Kovid 19.
According to a letter from the Ministry of Education, received by Fresh News on June 11, 2020, to ensure quality and sustainable teaching and learning during the communicable disease period. 19 Kovid Outbreaks The Ministry allows higher education institutions, both public and private, to:
* First, organize the entrance examination and graduation exam of students online, each higher education institution must prepare the application documents to the Ministry of Education for the Ministry to review and prepare a letter of introduction to the committee to inspect the examination process.
* Second: Organize training for students through distance learning system through electronic system with interaction between professors and students.
* Third: Establish a clear management structure to ensure that the process of teaching and learning through the electronic distance learning system, as well as the evaluation of students to be quality.
