Mr. Neth Pheaktra: Cambodia is the only large sanctuary in the world for the giant and white-tailed trout, which are endangered species on earth.
(Preah Vihear): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Environment, said that Cambodia is the only large sanctuary in the world for the giant and white-tailed trout, which are endangered species. Earth. "Cambodia is proud to have this rare animal and we all need to work together to protect and conserve this rare species for generations to come for the benefit of the world's biodiversity."
Mr. Net Pheaktra made this statement during a delegation led by the Ministry of Environment and nearly 20 national journalists to review the implementation of the Wildlife Conservation Society of Cambodia (WCS) Wildlife Protection and Conservation Project (WCS) on June 9-10, 2020 in the Kulen-Prohm Tep Wildlife Sanctuary and Chep Wildlife Sanctuary in Preah Vihear Province.
The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment said that according to the census of the Ministry of Environment, the world's largest endangered species, 300 giant trout, representing 99% of the world's giant trout. There are less than 200 adult giants. There are nearly 600 white-tailed deer, accounting for about 95% of the world's white-tailed deer.
"In 2005, the giant trout was designated by Royal Decree as the national symbol bird of Cambodia," he said. The giant trout is an endangered species and is protected by the laws of the Kingdom of Cambodia. That is why the Royal Government of Cambodia pays great attention to the protection and conservation of the white-tailed deer and the white-tailed deer.
According to WCS, the fast-growing rice program from two villages is currently being implemented in 11 villages in the Northern Landscape Protected Areas of Cambodia (Kulen Promtep Wildlife Sanctuary, Svay Chep Wildlife Sanctuary and Wildlife Sanctuary). Preah Rokar Wildlife) 5 villages bordering the western area of Siem Pang Wildlife Sanctuary, 3 villages within the Keo Seima Wildlife Sanctuary and 3 villages within the Prey Lang Wildlife Sanctuary in Stung Treng Province.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that the Ministry of Environment would like to highly appreciate the project on rice, which is designed to encourage farmers to reduce and achieve the elimination of poaching and illegal logging and forest encroachment. .
Mr. Neth Pheaktra stressed that at the same time, the authorities will enforce the strictest laws to protect and conserve giant trout and white-tailed trout for the benefit of biodiversity and for attracting tourists.
