According to the Department of Communicable Diseases, 27 people in Banteay Meanchey province were poisoned by alcohol and drugs, resulting in the death of six people. Alcohol poisoning cases occurred in four districts in Malai and three in Poipet.
Alcohol poisoning in Banteay Meanchey is not a new case for Cambodia. According to the Department of Combating Infectious Diseases, such cases of alcohol poisoning have also occurred in 2015, 2016, 2017 and 2018 in Tbong Khmum, Kratie, Mondulkiri, Kampong Chhnang, Kratie and Kampot provinces.
In the past four years, there have been nearly 600 cases of alcohol poisoning, killing 59 people.
The Department of Infectious Diseases has once again warned alcoholics to be careful when buying alcohol and to buy clear-sourced wine with proper supervision by experts and drink to a minimum.
The Department of Infectious Diseases requested the relevant institutions and local authorities to strengthen inspections of handicrafts and wineries. In particular, eliminate unlicensed wineries from professional institutions.
To help prevent alcohol poisoning, the Department of Infectious Diseases claims that the Ministry of Health has worked with the relevant ministries to organize public awareness campaigns to understand the risks posed by alcohol consumption.
