During the meeting, Minister Veng Sakhon expressed his congratulations to the new Ambassador who has just been appointed to fulfill his diplomatic mission in Cambodia.
Taking this opportunity, the Minister also informed the guests about the potential and progress of Cambodia's agricultural sector, especially in recent years under the leadership of the Royal Government, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the Prime Minister of Cambodia has expanded productivity. Agricultural production and export market for many agricultural products to international markets such as: rice, mango, banana, cashew, fresh cassava, dried vegetables, fish and animals, etc.
Through the Ambassador, Minister Veng Sakhon requested for cooperation between the two countries in the field of agriculture through research, training, human resources and exchange of experiences between leaders, researchers and experts.
The Ambassador praised and appreciated the progress made in all areas, including the interesting agricultural sector, which has helped support Cambodia's economic growth and reduce poverty.
During his tenure in Cambodia, the Ambassador said that he would work hard to promote and review better agricultural cooperation between the two countries and review and prepare a memorandum of understanding on exports. Agriculture and human resource training soon.
Regarding rice exports to East Timor, the Ambassador said that he would like to encourage East Timorese traders to study and learn more about the procedures, laws, techniques and procedures of Cambodia's exports in depth and hope that Cambodian rice will be available in the East Timor market in the near future.
The meeting ended in the spirit of solidarity, friendship and cooperation as ASEAN member countries. Minister Veng Sakhon wished his diplomatic mission in Cambodia a success.
