Mr. Teang Sokun sent a message of greetings from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross with great remembrance and sympathy. He urged all the families of the victims to cut off their emotions, because all these incidents have already passed, but what we need to continue to consider is the work to earn money according to their ability to support life. Family recovery for the better.
He added that Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen always thinks about the well-being of the general population without any discrimination on the basis of race, religion, caste or political affiliation. In that, the director also disseminated the history of the Red Cross movement and the seven basic principles to the people.
Mr. Khon Serey Ratha, Chairman of the Cambodian Red Cross Sub-Branch Committee, said that 14 families were affected by the strong wind, houses collapsed and the roof was opened on June 5, 2020, of which 4 families were seriously affected. And an average of 10 families were affected. He urged people to pay attention to good health care, especially to participate in the implementation of measures to prevent and prevent the global epidemic of Kovid-19 in the community.
