(Siem Reap): Vendors in front of Angkor Wat continue to join the APSARA Authority by voluntarily dismantling two large souvenir stalls and restaurants next to the floating bridge and near the restrooms of the Angkor temple complex. Wat this morning, June 10.
The dismantling of the souvenir shop and restaurant took place after the vendors who rented the stalls and the restaurant owners volunteered to hand over the location to the officials of APSARA Authority to prepare it as a hospitality area, a garden, and to improve the beauty and environment. Organize order in front of Angkor Wat to be more orderly.
Mr. Yit Chanda, Deputy Director General of APSARA Authority, who is leading the force to dismantle the stalls, said that the authorities plan to dismantle all the stalls and restaurants from the Angkor Wat area by the end of August. Upcoming 2020.
The Deputy Director General of the APSARA Authority stated that although the demolition of the stalls did not force the traders who own the stalls, the APSARA Authority will try to explain to the traders to agree to voluntarily dismantle. .
With the dismantling of these stalls and restaurants, the APSARA Authority is also building new shops to replace the traders to make a living not far from the old place.
Souvenir vendors and restaurant owners have repeatedly expressed their willingness to dismantle their stalls and accept new ones.
This is the fifth time that vendors in front of Angkor Wat continue to volunteer with the APSARA Authority to dismantle two more souvenir stalls and restaurants in front of Angkor Wat.
