(Kratie): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, said that the Ministry of Public Works will not issue a certificate of absolute recognition for any construction contractor who builds roads that do not meet the technical standards.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol made this statement this morning, June 10, 2020, on the occasion that he led a delegation and the technical team of the Ministry to inspect the quality and technical characteristics of the construction of National Road 7. Participation from representatives of construction companies, technical consultants and officials of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Kratie and Tbong Khmum Provinces.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol continued that if the road is not inspected in accordance with the technical specifications, the Ministry will not accept the road because the Ministry is based on the principle of "building a strong quality road for a long time" and the Ministry will inspect At all construction sites under the jurisdiction of the Ministry in Cambodia.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also instructed the freight forwarders to respect the traffic law, not to carry overweight according to the law, not to modify the vehicle in a technical way and called on the people to take the car to check if it is time to check. To change the driver's license if it expires and wear a seat belt when driving a car wearing a helmet, do not drive under the influence of drugs and alcohol for the safety of all and to avoid fines.
Please be informed that National Road No. 7 is a project to manage the property of the second road with a total length of 164 km, improving the quality of the road from DBST to AC, and this project is divided into three major construction sites using a construction period of 18 months. And a 36-month maintenance period, built by a Chinese company, technically inspected by a Korean company and costing a total of 36,456,064.75 US dollars. Until now, this section of road is about 80% completed.
