(Phnom Penh): Minister of Commerce Pan Sosak has asked East Timor to examine the possibility of exporting Cambodian rice to its market as Cambodia prepares about 30,000 tonnes of rice for the Southeast Asian country.
East Timor is another new market for Cambodian rice, which Cambodia has been trying to negotiate with the East Timorese government. The East Timorese ambassador claimed that his country was currently in political trouble. Once this political issue is resolved, it will examine the possibility of importing Cambodian rice to its market.
Mr. Pan Sosak claimed that about 30,000 tons of Cambodian rice was ready for East Timor. He asked East Timor to examine the possibility and inform Cambodia when the problem is resolved.
During the meeting, the Minister mentioned the Memorandum of Understanding on Trade between the two countries which has already been signed and requested to expedite the implementation of this Memorandum of Understanding for the benefit of both countries.
Mr. Pan Sosak also welcomed the private sector of East Timor to open a rice mill in Cambodia to export rice to East Timor.
