(Banteay Meanchey): On the morning of June 10, 2020, the police continued the procedure by visiting a Chinese liquor store in Malai district, Banteay Meanchey province, after an incident of alcohol poisoning that caused 3 deaths and some others. Is being treated at the hospital.
The incident of alcohol poisoning caused a surprise at noon on June 9, 2020 in Sangkat Poipet, Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province.
According to the initial explanation from the victims, on the evening of June 8, after taking a break from construction work, five of them went to buy a bottle of Tang Kui wine for 12,000 Riel to drink. Fake food such as dog meat, salted fish, papaya mixed with crab together, drink out of alcohol. On June 9, at 11 noon, they suddenly felt unwell, drowsy, and knew that they were poisoned, so they went to their respective doctors.
Cambodian Civil Aviation: Airlines flying to Cambodia must comply with the Royal Government's conditions in case any passengers do not meet the conditions to be transported back to their original place (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation of Cambodia has issued a new announcement. Specifying some principles for all airlines flying into Cambodia to be implemented to prevent Kovid 19 disease.
Chea Aun, Permanent Secretary of State and Spokesman for Civil Aviation, told Fresh News on the afternoon of June 10, 2020 that the purpose of the Civil Aviation Authority of Cambodia is to inform all airlines that fly. Come to Cambodia to respect the conditions required by the Ministry of Health and some new conditions that Cambodia Civil Aviation requires companies to implement correctly and responsibly.
In addition to the conditions required by the Ministry of Health for civil aviation, all airlines must not allow the transport of passengers with Kovi 19 on their aircraft to enter Cambodia and must not transport passengers. Which lacks the documents required by the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Mr. Chea Oun emphasized, "In this letter of Civil Aviation, there is a point that requires all airlines to comply: if the passengers that the airline brought to Cambodia, but lack the documents required by the government. The airline is responsible for transporting the passengers back to their original places.
The Permanent Secretary of State further stated that all airlines are required to send a specific list of nationalities of passengers before flying to Cambodia with the required documents.
Please be informed that the Royal Government of Cambodia has set out some important measures for travelers entering Cambodia, including:
* All passengers, both Cambodians and foreigners arriving in Cambodia, must be sent to a waiting center for testing for Kovid 19 virus and awaiting results from the Pasteur Laboratory.
* In the case of one or more passengers with a positive Kovid 19, all passengers, along with all others, are required to undergo a 14-day cataract at a location designated by the Intergovernmental Commission for the Prevention of Kovid 19.
* In the event that all passengers have a laboratory test result of Kovid 19 negative, they are allowed to undergo a 14-day catheterization in their respective homes under the supervision of local authorities and health officials. Repeat the test on the 13th day of the test.
Authorities transport water to the site of Bakong temple to save the remaining trout after several trout died due to lack of water
(Phnom Penh): On June 10, 2020, Prasat Bakong District Authority cooperated with APSARA Authority to transport water to Kasin Prasat Bakong to save some of the remaining trout after many trout died due to lack of Water. This is according to Mr. Leng Kosal, the spokesman of Apsara Authority, told Fresh News this afternoon.
Mr. Leng Kosal said that the APSARA Authority has always considered this issue, but because of the Bakong temple, it is just a pond waiting for the rain, like a pond, there is no water source nearby that can be drained immediately. No. He said that at present, at the site of Bakong temple, it is not dry yet, only the water is shallow, narrow, and the day is very hot, which causes some fish to die.
It should be noted that many fish in the pond of Prasat Bakong in Prasat Bakong district, Siem Reap province, many of them have died, while many others have died due to the dry water from this pond. This is according to the Facebook post of Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information.
Residents and monks living near Bakong temple said on the evening of June 9, 2020 that the fish had been dead since the afternoon of June 8. They say that some of them live here 50 to 60 years ago and have never seen the temple dry and see such big fish, this is the first time they have seen the fish in Bakong Ring. See a lot of big fish like this.
The dead and living fish in this farm are a species of trout, and they are thought to have been released by the authorities or monks when there was a lot of water. Some of these fish have died and been buried, while some have been taken by locals to other ponds and some have been living in shallow water in the lake.
Cambodia-Switzerland continue to jointly develop skills and vocational education system in the second phase
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and the Swiss Agency for Development and Cooperation (SDC) have pledged to jointly develop the Technical and Vocational Training System (TVET) in the second phase, while the first project Affected by Kovid-19 respiratory disease.
The second project is a skills training for poor youth in the communities of five target provinces in northeastern Cambodia, including Preah Vihear, Stung Treng, Kratie, Mondulkiri and Ratanakkiri.
The remarks were made during a meeting between Minister of Labor and Vocational Training Ith Sam Heng and a delegation from the Swiss Agency for Development and Cooperation (SDC) led by Nadia Ottiger, Deputy Director of the Swiss Agency for Development and Cooperation. Cambodia Cooperation at the Ministry of Labor on the morning of June 10, 2020.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng expressed his deep gratitude to the Swiss Government for always supporting all activities in promoting human resources in the field of employment and vocational training in Cambodia.
He said that this skills development project is a good initiative to integrate skills in the northeast to build human resources for Cambodia in this area.
He stated that the goal of this project is to attract poor youth in the community to receive skills training to increase human resources as well as increase income for the people of Cambodia.
She stated that all project activities are closely supported by the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training as well as other partners to develop skills to reduce migration. The Cambodian government is also responding to the needs of the labor market and what employers want today.
It should be noted that the second phase of this project will start from July 1, 2020 to June 2024, with a total budget of about 9 million US dollars. As a result of the project, 1. TVET Cambodia will be more effective in the target provinces, regions and enterprises, and 2. Young people, men, women and low-skilled workers will have increased access to employment.
Blood screams, skin calls! Gasoline Murder in Kandal Province, Authorities Arrested in Prey Speu Forest
(Kampong Speu): A case of premeditated murder of a husband who set fire to his wife and killed her while living in Ponhea Leu district, Kandal province, was arrested by the police on June 10, 2020, while the suspect was hiding Fugitive in Oral district, Kampong Speu province.
The operation was carried out by the Criminal Police Department in collaboration with the Kandal Provincial Police and Kampong Speu Provincial Police. The suspect was arrested at Chamkar Ampov Sugar Company in Peam Sor village, Raksmey Samaki commune, Oral district, Kampong Speu province.
Please be informed that on June 6, 2020, the suspect named Nguon alias Toeur, 51 years old, a construction worker, set fire to his wife Sar Chan, 47 years old, a factory worker at Prey Phchech village, Chhwang commune, Ponhea Leu district, Kandal province. .
Authorities confirmed that the victim and the suspect had a love affair and lived together as a couple since 2018. In May 2020, the suspect got drunk and came to the victim jealous of the victim and accused the victim of stealing a new boyfriend and not talking to each other for more than a month.
On the day of the incident, the suspect asked the victim to reconcile, but the victim refused. The suspect then went to bed alone in the house, while the victim slept on the front bed with his daughter Chan Srey Nich, 19 years old, then the suspect took 4 bottles of gasoline, half a liter of water equal to 2 liters Already purchased, poured on the victim, burned, and the suspect crawled out of the wall of the house to escape.
Suddenly, the victim's daughter woke up to see the fire, the mother shouted for help to extinguish and took the mother to the Calmette Hospital in Phnom Penh until 11 o'clock the same day, the victim died at Calmette Hospital transported the victim's body home.
