(Preah Vihear): Mr. Net Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Environment, on June 10, 2020, participated in the opening of the annual vulture census in Cambodia, which took place in the community of Dang Phlit, the vulture restaurant in the geographical area of Chep Wildlife Sanctuary. In Cheb district, Preah Vihear province, with the participation of provincial authorities, Prey Lang Baitong project officials and officials from the Ministry of Environment.
The Vulture Report Census, co-organized by the Wildlife Conservation Society of Cambodia (WCS) and the Ministry of Environment, was conducted in five areas where vultures live.
Ministry of Environment spokesman Net Pheaktra said the vulture census was conducted at five different locations, including: at the Siem Pang Wildlife Sanctuary in Stung Treng province at the vulture restaurant at Boeung Toal field in Prey Andong Dang Plit community. Chep Wildlife Sanctuary in Preah Vihear Province, Sre Pok Wildlife Sanctuary, Mondulkiri Province, Sre Angrang in the Sesan area of Stung Treng, and Lumphat Wildlife Sanctuary in Ratanakkiri Province.
As vultures are endangered in the world and Cambodia is known to have the largest number of vultures left, the Ministry of Environment has partnered with the Wildlife Rescue Association (WCS) to carry out conservation activities in protected areas. Through supplemental feeding and protection of nesting nests, increase in-depth understanding of vulture risk factors.
At the same time, on behalf of the Ministry of Environment, Mr. Net Pheaktra called on all people to participate in the conservation and protection of vultures by stopping hunting or wildlife trade.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra stated that vultures are gentle and clean people of the environment by eating other animal carcasses as food and protecting and conserving vultures, it is a preservation of valuable natural heritage for Cambodia and the world. The whole world is the value for biodiversity conservation and attracting tourists for eco-tourism, creating jobs, providing income to the people.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng: Action Plan is an Important Part of Public Administration Reform
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Interior, stated that the action plan is an important part of the efforts in the reform of public administration, which is a central institution that plays an important role.
On the occasion of chairing the meeting of the General Department of Administration on the morning of June 10, 2020, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng emphasized that if the administration is strong, it means that all activities and services to the people Better.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng continued that the first planning does not require perfection, but to collect various issues to discuss and continue to divide the work.
Also in this meeting, Mr. Prak Sam Oeun, Director General of the General Department of Administration, Ministry of Interior, stated that this action plan was prepared and submitted to two meetings with the leadership of the General Department of Administration and submitted to the following meeting: The leadership of Mr. Sak Setha, Permanent Secretary of State on May 19, 2020.
He added that the action plan is a specific map of the implementation of the activities of the General Department of Administration and focuses on supporting sub-national administrations in the implementation of the functions assigned to economic, social and local development and the promotion of services. Effective, transparent and accountable citizens in accordance with established laws and regulations.
It should be informed that the Action Plan for 2020 is a tool for implementing the five-year strategic plan (2019-2023) and as a measure as well as a solution to meet the challenges. This action plan is designed to enhance the efficiency of the General Department of Administration, the Ministry of Interior and the sub-national administration in providing services and socio-economic development at the local level in a sustainable manner and responding to the real needs of the people.
