Kampot Provincial Administration Inspects Canals Rehabilitated for Irrigation of Agricultural Land in Angkor Chey District
(Kampot): Mr. Chheng Phalla, Chairman of Kampot Provincial Council and Mr. Chiao Tai, Provincial Governor, on June 10, 2020, led officials of relevant departments to visit Trapeang Run village, Tani commune, Angkor Chey district to investigate and mediate the case. A canal that involves the people living on the back of the canal.
During the inspection of the canal, Mr. Chiao Tai stated that the poverty reduction policy is one of the priority policies of the Royal Government of Cambodia, the development of infrastructure at the local level, especially the irrigation system for agricultural crops is an important and necessary work.
The provincial governor also stated that the development of any development always has more or less impact, so people should cooperate with the authorities and professional officials so that the development work can achieve good results. He also asked the officials to set up a clear demarcation post before starting the restoration of the canal so that the people can understand and cooperate.
The implementation is divided into four phases, and the implementation for the fourth phase in 2021, with a length of 563 meters, will be completed, which will involve the houses of 18 families on the back of the canal. As a result, after the mediation, the people congratulated and agreed to push for the restoration of this canal in the near future.
