(Phnom Penh): To contribute to improving the health of the people by eating comfortable and safe food that does not use banned chemicals, a food market with a high quality standard called "Safe Food Market" will start Open for sale from June 11, 2020 tomorrow, located next to the Bayon roundabout, Khan Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh.
This safe food market brings vegetables, fish, meat from pure farming communities, all of which have received proper technical training from the Ministry of Commerce and are accredited by the World Health Organization to help. To enable people to create a small market for selling natural vegetables, fish, meat without chemicals banned.
This safe food market not only sells high quality vegetables, fruits, fish, meat without chemicals, but also sells seafood, fish, meat imported from the country, as well as many other goods to Serve to meet all customer needs. In addition, in addition to selling safe food, there is also a restaurant with standard food quality with reasonable prices.
(Phnom Penh): The General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries has issued a press release dismissing allegations that restrictions on pig imports and the closure of illegal importers have pushed up the price of pork in the market. This is according to the press release received by Fresh News on June 10, 2020.
The dismissal came after the afternoon of June 8, 2020, the Cambodian Pig Supply Association held a meeting on the topic of "abnormal pig prices."
The General Department of Animal Health confirmed that the management of the import of live pigs to supply the Cambodian market is not related to corruption. Expand animal husbandry and family farming.
The sale of pork in the market at between 18,000 and 22,000 riel / kg is due to the fact that during the 19 outbreak of Kovid, large gatherings and events were not organized and restaurants were not operated, making traders sell Pure pork is on the market, while leg bones and offal are not used to their full potential. Therefore, the price that traders can sell to make a profit is to include all the prices on the meat.
