He said that in Cambodia, the Yangtze Rice Project, implemented by the Wildlife Conservation Association under the auspices of the Ministry of Environment, has been working with local communities in protected areas for more than 10 years to develop sustainable livelihoods programs. Associated with conservation, which is a cash benefit for the local population.
