Read the full text of the Joint Statement: Department of Public Works and Daun Penh District Disseminate Drainage Project to Residents, Businesses and Representatives of Public Institutions Residing along Sisowath Quay
(Phnom Penh): On June 10, 2020, a meeting was held to disseminate the sewer project to the people, business people and representatives of various public institutions with residences and locations along Preah Sisowath Quay from Street 88 to Street 90.
Mr. Sam Piseth, Director of the Capital Department of Public Works, said that the project will be dug to install a network of 2 meters by 2 meters. This is the plan in the project to prevent floods and improve the drainage system in Phnom Penh, Phase 4 within the framework of the Japanese grant.
Mr. Sok Penhvuth explained to the people that the Capital Administration wants to publicly present the strategic plan and master plan to improve the sewer and sewage system in Phnom Penh to escape from the flooding. On the other hand, we want to gather as many input consultations as possible so that we are able to set out a set of directional principles to harmonize.
It should be noted that since 2001, Japan has provided grants through JICA to help improve the flood protection of Phnom Penh from the first to the fourth phase, which is currently underway through the improvement of the system. Subsequently, the Phnom Penh Municipal Authority inspected that many areas in the city that used to be flooded were reduced to flooding, especially in the four districts in the city center.
Authorities hope that after 2021, the geography of central Phnom Penh will no longer be flooded by rain.
