(Phnom Penh): On June 9, 2020, Mr. Sok Penh Vuth, Governor of Daun Penh District, ordered the forces of Daun Penh District Unity Command to organize order on the streets and disseminate measures to protect Kovid 19 to local people.
The campaign was attended by Mr. Yos Yuthy, Deputy District Governor, Mr. Ny Samith, Director of Public Works, Transport, Sanitation, Environment and Public Order, Daun Penh District, Mr. Muth Bunthorn, Deputy Chief of Office, Mr. Chuon Chit, Deputy District Inspector, Mr. Kim Vutha, Chief of Khan People's Defense, Mr. Mao Po. Mr. Kem Heng, Deputy Chief of Division.
On the occasion of meeting with the people, the Cambodian Red Cross delegation brought the speech of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen and the Royal Message of Her Majesty Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, the Queen Mother of Cambodia, the Honorary President of the Cambodian Red Cross. Nostalgia and sympathy, especially concern for the lives of people everywhere who face unforeseen natural disasters.
At the same time, all citizens should pay attention to traffic safety, must adhere to traffic laws to prevent the tragedy of traffic accidents that occur every day and to maintain peace and live together in harmony. And strive to grow crops to improve family life.
Please also note that each victim's family received a humanitarian donation from the Cambodian Red Cross, including: 30 kg of rice, 1 box of noodles, 10 cans of fish and 1 kit (mosquito net, blanket, sarong, scarf, T-shirt) as well. Separately, the families affected by the complete collapse of their house received an additional tent and a budget of 200,000 riels.
According to the Ministry of Commerce, on June 9, 2020, the Working Group on Free Trade Negotiations between Cambodia and China met again via video. This is the third meeting between the two working groups.
In a statement, the ministry noted that the Cambodian side, chaired by Sok Sopheak, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce of Cambodia, and the Chinese side, led by Yang Zhengvy, Deputy Director General of the Ministry of Commerce, focused on opening up markets for goods and services. Invest in economic, technical and legal cooperation that will boost the export of goods from Cambodia and attract more foreign investment.
During the talks, the 10 technical working groups also reported on the progress achieved and requested recommendations on technical, legal and policy challenges from the two countries' chief negotiators.
During the video conference, the negotiating team resolved the remaining issues of the text of the agreement and also agreed on key principles regarding the opening of markets for goods and services.
According to the press release, the working group will request the principles from both governments to approve the text of the agreement and the proposal to open the market and other chapters to make a decision to close the negotiations and sign the agreement. Bilateral free trade agreement by the end of 2020
Negotiations on a Cambodia-China Bilateral Free Trade Agreement were initiated by Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Chinese Prime Minister Li Keqiang at a bilateral meeting on January 20-23, 2019 in Phnom Penh. Beijing. The initiative aims to deepen trade, investment, services and cooperation for the benefit of the two peoples.
If successful, it will be the first free trade agreement for Cambodia. The Ministry of Commerce claims that based on the joint principles agreed by the negotiating team, if the two governments agree on the text of the proposed agreement and market opening, Cambodia's export growth is expected to increase. Up about 20 percent.
At the same time, the growth of foreign investment is also expected to increase significantly, which is a source of income and jobs for Cambodians in the near future. The Royal Government determines the services of foreigners for testing for HIV 19
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to charge a fee from foreigners for testing for 19 Kovid virus, screening and treating 19 Kovid patients at public hospitals. This is according to the letter from the Minister of Economy and Finance to the Minister of Health, which was received by Fresh News on the night of June 9, 2020.
The Ministry of Economy has outlined the implementation procedures as follows:
* For the treatment of 19 Kovid patients at public hospitals, the Ministry of Health should require passengers to purchase local insurance to facilitate payment. At the same time, insurers should be allowed to sell insurance policies with bank issues at international gates in the passenger terminal upon arrival.
* The introduction of an online system to improve operational efficiency should be made as soon as possible so that passengers can make deposits and withdrawals, as well as purchase Kovid-19 insurance products for the convenience of To travelers in and out of Cambodia.
(Stung Treng): More than 300 workers of Angkor Banana Company in O'Svay Commune, Borey O'Svay Senchey District on June 9, 2020 protested in front of Angkor Banana Company and requested the Provincial Department of Labor and Vocational Training to inspect And help solve the work of workers at the banana plantation as well, because the new boss uses workers do not comply with the employment contract.
Mr. Chhean Samnang, representing the workers, was equal to the director of the Provincial Department of Labor and Vocational Training to inspect the workers' work activities because they were oppressed by the Vietnamese boss by using workers with contemptuous behavior towards workers, using abusive words against workers. And non-compliance with the contract.
He said that this is a new boss who came to work less than 2 months, dared to insult and remove the workers not to pay irregular wages and dare to recruit new workers to work and suspend old workers. To work day in and day out makes them lose income to make ends meet.
Mr. Bou Phirun, Director of the Provincial Department of Labor and Vocational Training, urged the workers to be patient and to disperse the crowd from the front of the company headquarters to give the opportunity to the competent officials on June 10, 2020 tomorrow because Today he is busy meeting in the province.
Mr. Hor Wang Dung, head of Angkor Banana banana plantation, came forward to coordinate with the workers but did not solve the problems that the workers wanted.
Please note that the workers in this banana plantation want to get enough jobs and pay their salaries regularly and do not have to fire them as old workers, because they come from the provinces to sell their labor here for Take money to solve livelihood.
