General Chhorn Sarane chaired a meeting with the leadership of the Department of Construction and Engineering to focus on strengthening the work more effectively.
(Phnom Penh): General Chhorn Sarane, Deputy Director General of the General Department of Logistics and Finance, Ministry of Interior, chaired a meeting with the leadership of the Department of Construction and Engineering to strengthen the work of the Department to be more effective.
The meeting was held on June 9, 2020 by General Chhorn Sarane and set out a number of strategic principles to further guide the direction of the Department in line with the Royal Government's Rectangular Strategy.
The General also reminded the Department of Construction and Engineering to carefully inspect the vehicles and machinery that are registered as state property and continue to validate to be used carefully and correctly, not to be used differently from the original form (such as labels Vehicle number "A" but used on vehicle "B") will also help maintain the department's vehicles and machinery better.
General Chhorn Sarane confirmed that he recently mobilized philanthropists to get 3 land trucks to use in the department.
The general also instructed that in the event that any engineering unit in the department uses this vehicle, the director of the department should charge the engineering department to use the money to support the officials in the department who have a shortage, as well as Use on other services of the department as well.
Ministry of Water Resources: From today to June 16, there may be light to moderate rain in Cambodia, people continue to be careful of thunderstorms and gusts of wind
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has issued a notification on the weather situation in Cambodia from today to June 16, 2020.
According to the Ministry, through the continuous change of weather conditions, Cambodia is experiencing moderate southwest monsoon. But by June 12-16, there will be a low pressure system extending through southern Laos.
The ministry also called on people to be careful of thunder, lightning and strong winds.
