Kampong Cham Provincial Governor Decides to Continue Construction of Provincial Hall Administration Building to Increase Officials' Workplaces
(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, on June 9, 2020, after the 13th Ordinary Meeting of the Provincial Council of the third mandate and after inspecting the construction of the new administrative building of Kampong Cham Provincial Hall, decided to work. Construction of the building resumed after a hiatus.
During the inspection, Mr. Un Chanda said that due to seeing the difficulties of officials who are working at the provincial hall and to provide a suitable place for officials to perform daily work for public services to the people and The public who came to receive public services at the provincial hall, the Board of Governors has agreed and allowed to continue the construction of this new administrative building, the construction site is scheduled to start on June 18, 2020.
It is pointed out that the construction project of the Provincial Hall is made of concrete frame, brick wall and tiled roof, 53.25 meters long, 24 meters wide and 24.57 meters high, located in the Provincial Hall in Village 7, Sangkat Kampong Cham. Kampong Cham city.
Spokesman for the General Commission: On June 9, another 1708 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, within 40 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to June 9, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected And fined a total of 57,024 vehicles, including 41,988 motorcycles and 15036 vehicles of all types.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that during the 39 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine the offending vehicles went well.
