(Stung Treng): Mr. Kao Thach, Director General of the Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture and his colleagues, on June 9, 2020, continued to disseminate the loan policy and procedure for obtaining a loan under the Royal Government's special financing project of 50 million US dollars. To the people who are engaged in agriculture, handicrafts, aquaculture, a total of 300 agricultural community production groups in Stung Treng Provincial Administration.
The occasion was also presided over by Mr. Mom Saroeun, Governor of the Provincial Board of Governors, Chheang Lak, Chairman of the Provincial Council, members of the Provincial Council, Governor of the District Board of Governors and directors of relevant departments around the province.
He requested and requested farmers, fish farmers, animal husbandry, vegetable growers to develop a clear planting plan, feeding plan to supply the market to meet demand and sustain the market and to help reduce imports from neighboring countries. This will contribute to solving the market problem that is the concern of farmers as well.
Mr. Kao Thach allowed you to ask questions related to the procedure to get credit on marketing issues, cultivation techniques, etc., and he answered and explained your questions in a friendly manner.
