(Kandal): Senior Minister Kun Kim, Vice President and Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, reminded the leadership of the Kandal Provincial Veterans Association to pay more attention and take responsibility for the well-being and lives of veterans in Kandal Province.
In this meeting, the Senior Minister reminded of the merits of Cambodian veterans to the society, stating that the veterans are all those who have sacrificed and sacrificed a lot for the motherland and the people of Cambodia.
Mr. Kun Kim stated that due to this invaluable merit, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia and the President of the Cambodian Veterans Association, has always kept the well-being of veterans high and always addressed the needs of Cambodian veterans.
In order to repay the veterans and fulfill the order of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, in this conversation, the Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association instructed the leadership of the Kandal Provincial Veterans Association to monitor the lives of veterans. And diligently visit their backyards to be aware of adversity and other needs and to respond in a timely manner.
Mr. Kun Kim also instructed to educate and guide veterans to follow the guidelines of the Ministry of Health to prevent health from Kovid 19.
However, Senior Minister Kun Kim praised the efforts of the provincial commissioners, deputy commissioners and district inspectors who have worked together to complete all tasks and resolve local challenges in a timely manner.
It should be noted that in this meeting, Brigadier General Chhoeun Sochet also brought the budget of Kandal Provincial Police about 5,000 dollars to help build infrastructure at the headquarters of the Veterans Association. Experts found 3 points that caused more than 70 workers to faint at the lamp factory in Svay Rieng province
Mr. Touch Poliva, Deputy Governor of Svay Rieng Province, told Fresh News Agency in Svay Rieng Province on the afternoon of June 9, 2020 that the team investigated the case of workers fainting at the lamp factory in Doeum Po village, Kandeang Reay commune, Svay Teap district. Inspected and measured both inside and outside the factory.
* First: There is a hustle and bustle in the production building * Second: Workers 'personal health problems * Third: Workers' fears and panic.
He said that the measures for the enterprise, the team for the director of the factory to improve, open all windows while working in the production building in accordance with Prakas No. 125 S.K.P.Y. and education about food. Get proper rest and adequate rest for 8 hours a day to ensure the good health of workers.
Workers who did not faint to return to work on Tuesday, June 9, 2020, and the factory director failed to implement the above measures are also responsible before the law in force.
