(Kampong Chhnang): Two girls, siblings, were abandoned by their parents when they were young and were raised by their grandmother as a widow without a bright field and a house to live in. They asked for their land to build a small hut to live temporarily with their two grandchildren in Teuk Hout village, Teuk Hout commune, Rolea Bier district, Kampong Chhnang province.
They were both orphaned by her parents when she was a child, when the eldest granddaughter was only 4 years old and the youngest granddaughter was only 2 years old. The grandmother, who has been raising her two granddaughters from then until today.
To this day, she has not given up on all of these businesses, but she is no longer able to work as a hired laborer because she is very old. Physical illness can no longer do this.
