The coastal areas in Sihanoukville, including Ochheuteal Beach and Otres Beach, were liberated by Mr. Kouch Chamroeun under the control of the provincial administration after falling into the control of the people, causing disorder and use as Individual interests, such as anarchic trade on the coast.
The Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province has confirmed that the beach liberation campaign has so far rehabilitated more than 9 kilometers of coastal infrastructure from Ochheuteal Beach to the tip of Chumteav Mao Beach. A concrete road to make it convenient for tourists as well.
According to Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, this 9 km coastal area is open to tourists to sit and bathe for free without any barriers and no obstruction from any group, which in the past was required. There is a seating area and buy food to get a place to sit or take a shower.
The provincial governor emphasized that after the liberation of the beach, the provincial administration has been gradually improving the aesthetics by pouring concrete roads and cleaning the beach area, while the provincial administration is also studying to build a public bathroom. Also, according to the plan, 20 locations will be built.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun said, "The public toilets along this beach, because of the financial procedures, we can not think of doing now, so be prepared in our financial plan. In the future, we can only build a sewer system to prevent dirty water from flowing into the beach in the future, and now we plan to build more than 20 bathrooms and septic tanks from Ochheuteal beach.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun added that the provincial administration will start testing the construction of a public toilet near Ochheuteal pumping station, and how this toilet will be built to ensure long-term use and prevent dirty water from flowing in. Seawater is like a bitter experience in the past.
In addition to the issue of public rooms and bathrooms after bathing in the sea, the Governor of Sihanoukville also presented plans for a car park for tourists. The parking lot is planned to be located in a large coastal area, but not to affect the trees stored on the beach.
It should be informed that Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, led the relevant officials of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration to maintain order at Ochheuteal 2 Beach (formerly Ariston Beach) and Otres Beach, which are the common property of all Cambodians. From now on, national and international tourists can come and visit for free.
Most of the stalls built by the people on Otres Beach are mostly solid structures that have been poured concrete on the beach directly, and some are built right next to the waterfront, after dismantling those stalls. 136 sewers and kitchen waste were found embedded in the beach.
