Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said this on June 9, 2020, when he presided over a meeting and visited government officials, staff and workers of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Ratanakkiri Province with the participation of leaders. Ministry, Ratanakkiri provincial governor, civil servants, staff and workers around Ratanakkiri in large numbers.
He also highlighted the important role of Ratanakkiri in contributing to the sustainable development of the motherland and the master plan and policy to reduce competitive transportation costs, adding that Ratanakkiri has become a tourist destination. One of the main potentials for the rapid development of the province.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also reminded that the factors of peace and political stability under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia are indispensable factors in attracting foreign investors to create jobs for the people. Attracting tourists to find markets for agricultural products contributes to the national economic growth of around 7% per year and puts people below the poverty line.
On that occasion, the Senior Minister also instructed all civil servants, staff and workers of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Ratanakkiri Province to implement the measures of the Royal Government as well as the Ministry of Health that have recently been issued, such as hand washing. Wash frequently, keep gaps, and wear masks properly to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 more effectively.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also instructed all civil servants, workers of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Ratanakkiri Province with two slogans: "Please do not ask what Cambodia does for us, ask what we do for Cambodia." And another phrase that "useless words harm the nation, effective work brings prosperity."
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol agrees to build a paved road from Rattanakiri to Vern Sai
Ratanakkiri: Ratanakkiri provincial governor Thong Savun has asked Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, to help build a paved road from the provincial town to Vern Sai district and install traffic lights on a busy Banlung road. In response, the Senior Minister agreed in principle to build this paved road in 2022.
Mr. Thong Savun's request was made on the occasion of Senior Minister Sun Chanthol's participation in a meeting with government officials, staff and workers of the Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport on the morning of June 9, 2020 at the Provincial Hall.
In addition to the above request, the Governor of Ratanakkiri also requested the Senior Minister to provide technical training on road work to professional officers in the province.
On this occasion, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol praised and appreciated the progress in Ratanakkiri province, especially the progress in the field of road and bridge infrastructure, which has contributed to the provincial economy in building the province and reducing poverty for the people. The fourth phase of the Royal Government's Rectangular Strategic Policy, headed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
On this occasion, he also reminded public officials in Ratanakkiri to provide good public services to the people, that is, to make it faster, more efficient and transparent, because the roles and responsibilities of sub-national administrative officers are very important. In contributing to the building of a sustainable homeland.
He also informed the ceremony about the project to build, repair and maintain the road infrastructure, especially to improve the quality of important national roads to contribute to the facilitation of the transportation of goods and products of the people throughout the country.
The Senior Minister also mentioned the roles and responsibilities of public officials in providing services to the people well, that is, speed, efficiency and transparency, and outlined some strategies related to the provision of public services, such as: Information technology systems to bring public services closer to the people, the use of mobile vehicles and other mechanisms to improve the quality of public services.
Mr. Sun Chanthol expressed his deep appreciation to the leaders, civil servants, workers of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Ratanakkiri Province who worked hard to achieve good results and requested to continue to cooperate and contribute new ideas. Refers to modernization of public services.
