At the same time, Colonel Prohm Yot, Director of the Fire Prevention and Rescue Office of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, called on all citizens to be careful in case of fire before traveling, please turn off the electricity system completely. Avoid causing a fire eventually. Ministry of Labor announces the opening of allowances for garment and tourism workers whose contracts have been suspended
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has notified 17052 workers of 50 factories in the garment and tourism sectors who have received permission to suspend employment contracts in accordance with the spirit of the third round of the Royal Government's package of measures. That Wing Specialized Bank will send a message about the payment of government subsidies to the phone number that the workers provided to the Ministry through the factory administration in the past.
The announcement of the Ministry of Labor, received by Fresh News on the afternoon of June 9, 2020, stated that this allowance will be paid in KHR and depends on the number of days of suspension of the employment contract. :
In order to avoid the difficulty of reimbursing the Royal Government, in case the factory applies to work before the end of the contract period, the allowance will be divided in two times for those who have suspended the contract from 21 days to 1 Monthly, and will be divided into 4 times for those who suspend the employment contract for 2 months, each time equal to the budget of 82,000 Riels (US $ 20).
The Ministry reminded that Wing Specialized Bank will return this subsidy to the Royal Government if you fail to pay this allowance within 10 days after receiving the phone message from Wing Specialized Bank. To pay this allowance, you need to bring your Cambodian ID card and the phone number that received the message to the nearest Wing agent. Please note that you are not required to pay the service fee to Wing Agent when paying this allowance.
In case the workers working in these 50 factories do not receive a phone message from Wing Specialized Bank, please contact for more information or update their phone number to their factory administration immediately based on the content of Instruction No. 045/20 of the Ministry.
The Ministry will continue to inform other factory workers about the opening of this allowance. As mentioned above, the public, especially workers, should be informed and please contact the nearest Wing agency to pay this allowance in a timely manner. Samdech Techo Hun Sen Congratulates and Appreciates the Ministry of Agriculture's Efforts to Open the Cambodian Fresh Mango Market to China
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the afternoon of June 9, 2020, posted a message congratulating and appreciating the efforts of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to open the Cambodian fresh mango market to the country. China through the signing of the official protocol on "Hygienic requirements for the export of fresh mangoes from Cambodia to China" this morning.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also thanked the Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia and all relevant officials who participated in promoting this work until a formal agreement was reached.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen considers the signing of this protocol to be good news for farmers, plantation owners and traders who are investing in mango crops and are concerned because there are many plantations where ripe mangoes are falling while the price of mangoes has dropped dramatically. A lot.
The Prime Minister also said that by exporting mangoes to China, it will provide more jobs and income for the people, especially at a time when our country is facing Kovid 19.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen wrote on Facebook, "I congratulate and appreciate the Ministry of Agriculture's efforts to open the Cambodian fresh mango market to China, which on June 9, 2020, Cambodia and Chinese friends. Signed an official agreement on phytosanitary requirements for the export of fresh mangoes from Cambodia to China.
By exporting mangoes to China, it will provide more jobs and income for the people, especially at a time when our country is facing Kovid 19.
Let farmers and traders strengthen the cultivation techniques to a higher quality and set up a proper packaging factory so that we can be able to process mangoes to get more benefits. "The most important thing in exporting Cambodian mangoes to China is to have good hygiene and phytosanitary (SPS) that is acceptable abroad."
After signing the protocol to export Cambodian mangoes to China, Cambodia can export 500,000 tons of high quality mangoes to the Chinese market every year.
This is the second success in the negotiations to export fresh fruits from Cambodia directly to China, the first success in the export of fresh bananas to China.
In addition to mangoes, Cambodia is also negotiating with China to export mangoes, dragon fruit and oyster saliva directly to China. Currently, five Cambodian agricultural products are allowed to be exported directly by the Chinese side: rice, cassava chips, cashews and bananas.
