Tbong Khmum Provincial Officials Continue to Inspect Food Safety at Chi Paing Market in Ponhea Krek District to Ensure Safety for Citizens
(Tbong Khmum): Mr. Meas Mora, Branch Manager of Consumer Protection, Competition and Fraud Suppression in Tbong Khmum Province (PPR) on June 9, 2020, assigned PAC officials. Continue to inspect, inspect and test food as food and beverages that are being displayed for sale in Chi Paing Market in Ponhea Krek District, Tbong Khmum Province to check the safety of food items to ensure the health of consumers.
Mr. Meas Mora confirmed that in that activity, the professional officers tested the samples of products including: dried fish, samyong, prahok and fish meat products. As a result, no banned chemicals were found.
Mr. Meas Mora said that after that, the professional officers continued to inspect the packaging labels on the food, such as the expiration date of the source of production and other requirements, and found and confiscated the defective goods beyond the expiration date. Some include: 14 cans of orange juice and fruit juice, 10 bottles of yogurt and 100 packets of cakes.
In addition, experts have taken samples of fresh water produced in some provinces to check for non-compliance with the requirements for labels on fresh water packaging and corrective measures for local producers in collaboration with relevant departments.
