Mr. Kouch Chamroeun talks about the progress of Sihanoukville in the press conference of the Royal Government Spokesperson's Unit (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Preah Sihanouk Provincial Governor Mr. Kouch Chamroeun on the morning of June 9, 2020 Progress and direction of the work of the administration of Sihanoukville through a press conference organized by the Spokesperson of the Royal Government at the Office of the Council of Ministers.
Sihanoukville is a coastal province in the southwestern part of Cambodia, 230 km from Phnom Penh on National Road 4 and 260 km on National Road 3, and has a railway connecting Phnom Penh through the province. Kandal, Takeo and Kampot provinces.
Sihanoukville is a province with important economic sectors, including industry, trade, tourism and agriculture, which are priority sectors for the development of the national economy of the Royal Government. Potential includes: Deep Sea Port, SEZ with 10 locations (4 in operation and 6 in operation), Sihanoukville International Airport and beautiful beaches named "Southwestern Star".
* Water Resources and Meteorology: Irrigation potential: 88.32 km of saltwater dams, 36 sluice gates, 133 km of canals, divided into 06 planes or so-called (polder), which protects 9 rice fields. 772 hectares in 9 communes in Prey Nup district and another salt water protection system in Ream and Bit Trang communes with a total length of 7,670 meters, 6,470 meters of canals, 4 sluice gates and 3 sewers.
* Provision of public services: The provincial administration has strengthened and restricted the provision of all types of public services to the people, as well as expanded the dissemination of information about public services to the grassroots. At the provincial level, there is a one-stop-shop unit, at the municipal and district level, there is a one-stop-shop office that is serving the people.
The OWSO of Sihanoukville Provincial Administration provides public services in 14 areas, equal to 484 services, fast, efficient, transparent, and accountable, in accordance with the recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
