Minister of Rural Development led a delegation to inspect the construction site of two paved rural roads in Kampong Thom province.
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Ouk Rabun, Minister of Rural Development, on June 9, 2020, led a delegation of the Ministry of Rural Development to inspect the construction site of two double-story paved roads (DBST) with a total length of 41.5 km. Located in Kampong Thom province.
The first road from Ta Ok to Ngon with a total length of 21.10 km is located in Prasat Sambo and Sandan districts and the second road from Trach to Smanh with a total length of 20.4 km. In Kampong Svay and Prasat Balang districts of Kampong Thom province, the project is funded by the Royal Government of Cambodia, funded by the Asian Development Bank (ADB), the French Agency for Development (AFD) and the Australian Government Grant (GOA).
As a result, the first line reached 95% and the second line reached 55% and is scheduled to be completed in November 2020. Cambodia-East Timor pledges to jointly develop better jobs after Kovid-19
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Labor of Cambodia and the Ambassador of the Democratic Republic of East Timor have pledged to further develop the employment sector between the two countries after the end of Kovid-19.
The meeting focused on cooperation in the field of labor, which Cambodia and East Timor have cooperated well in the past and have been further strengthening.
Minister Ith Sam Heng warmly welcomed the Ambassador of the Democratic Republic of East Timor and emphasized the good relations between our two countries and peoples with beautiful nature and similar history.
The Ambassador praised the Prime Minister's win-win policy of national unification, peace and development in all areas, allowing Cambodians of all political persuasions to live in harmony with each other. Each.
The ambassador pledged to work hard for a successful diplomatic mission in strengthening the two countries' relations. He considered Cambodia as his second home and was very warm. Although the world now has the Kovid-19 problem, Cambodia has managed the disease situation effectively.
It should be noted that the past cooperation between the two countries signed an agreement on cooperation in the field of labor on August 19, 2016, including:
Changes in the system of specialized study programs, research studies and information related to various fields, including comparative studies on employment, vocational training and labor administration, such as collective bargaining, law enforcement and implementation, and resolving labor disputes. Social security, labor protection, freedom of association, occupational safety and health, management of foreign labor, and exchange of information on labor productivity enhancement.
* Encouraging the exchange of visits between officials in charge and professional officers.
* Management of labor migration between the two countries.
Exchange of information to prevent the recruitment and use of illegal workers, as well as to prevent and combat labor exploitation and human trafficking.
