For this tax concession, Mr. Din Somethearith, a well-known businessman in the hotel industry, thanked the Royal Government of Cambodia for supporting the tourism business at a time when Cambodia and the world are facing the crisis of 19 communicable diseases. .
He added, "I would like to thank the Royal Government of Cambodia for its continued support for the business community, especially the tax incentives for the hotel industry, while Cambodia and the world are facing a crisis of 19 communicable diseases, including "I also call on the government to intervene in the financing package for the hotel sector to cope with the devastating effects of the Kovid 19 crisis and to keep it afloat."
He said that from mid-February until now, the situation has not been good, which has affected all hotel sectors, with many hotels closing because it is more profitable to close. But for himself, he continues to open both hotels at his location, despite the monthly payment of about $ 80,000.
Please be informed that the Royal Government of Cambodia on May 26, 2020, announced the extension of tax incentives for tourism and aviation for two more months.
These measures are designed to maintain business balance and workers' livelihoods by stating that:
1: Measures to continue to help the tourism sector:
* Continue to exempt all types of monthly taxes for hotels, guesthouses, restaurants and travel agencies registered with the General Department of Taxation and have business activities in Phnom Penh, Siem Reap, Sihanoukville, Kep, Kampot Bavet and Poipet for two more months from June to July 2020.
* Continue to allow the non-payment of insurance premiums on occupational risk and health care during the suspension of business, except for the renewal of all types of tourism licenses in the tourism sector for 2021.
2: Measures to help the aviation sector:
* Minimum tax exemption for a further two months from June to July 2020 to airlines registered in Cambodia. The King issues a Royal Decree appointing three Secretaries of State and Undersecretaries of State. 4 people of the Ministry of Posts
