(Phnom Penh): The Governor of Phnom Penh, Mr. Khuong Sreng, has ordered all district and commune governors to collect garbage at the mouth of the sewer in their locality to open the waterway to the sewer canal. Floods have not yet flowed as the rainy season has arrived in recent days, after a few heavy rains in the past, some areas have been clogged with rubbish.
In a meeting on measures to solve the problem of drainage on the morning of June 8, 2020, Mr. Khuong Sreng said that some areas affected by floods due to heavy rains these days to 105. Millimeters, which inundated some areas.
The governor of Phnom Penh claimed that the flood was caused by a number of reasons, such as the violation of the canal, the poor storage of garbage, causing garbage to flow into the canal. Regarding this issue, he told the district governor to go directly to the location when it rains, to collect garbage from the sewer to make the water flow faster.
Mr. Khuong Sreng also stated that in connection with the poor storage of garbage, causing it to flow into the sewer canal, this is a measure in front of the Phnom Penh Municipal Authority and fines for people who do not store garbage properly. However, the Governor of Phnom Penh confirmed that before implementing this fine measure, we, as the authorities, must first clean our bodies as an example to the people.
According to Mr. Khuong Sreng, the problem of garbage, the problem of flooding is all about the people and the authorities, so we must work together to do this work, without the participation of the people, we can not carry out this work successfully. Also.
