Legal Awareness: Contracts
(Phnom Penh): In recent years, the number of construction projects has increased in Cambodia, such as: villas, villas, apartments, condominiums, hotels, casinos and supermarkets. In the construction of such large structures, a contract is often created between the owner and the contractor to bind the obligations of the parties to the contract, which is called a "contract contract".
In order to better understand the contract contract, the legal awareness program of FRESH NEWS, in collaboration with the Cambodian Bar Association for International Cooperation, would like to make the following interpretations related to the topic of "contract contract" to the people:
In this case, the contractor can repair the defect of the work or can repeat the work based on the selection. If the performance of this work is complete, it is necessary to incur excessive costs compared to the loss of benefits due to the defect, then the contractor can refuse. If the contractor resumes the work, the contractor may demand that the employer repay the defective work.
When the work is defective, the owner can repair the defect himself / herself and may claim the necessary expenses for the repair of the defect from the contractor if the appropriate period of time to complete the work has elapsed or in the event that Failure to complete the work or in the event that it is assessed that the full performance of the work by the contractor will cause improper harm to the owner.
However, even if the parties have agreed to make a special contract, they are not responsible for the guarantees for the known incidents but have not been reported, the contractor can not be exempt from liability or No liability level. On the other hand, the owner can terminate the contract at any time by compensating for the damage until the contractor completes the work.
In summary, a contract is a contract that requires that it be properly written, clearly defining the rights and obligations of each party. If not specified in the contract, the parties must comply with the provisions of the Civil Code or in special law, if any.
