(Phnom Penh): On the morning of June 7, 2020, the Ministry of Health issued a new reminder to all citizens to continue to implement the social safety gap and personal safety gap to prevent and prevent the second transmission of the coronavirus. 19 in Cambodia.
The Ministry of Health said that restaurant and canteen owners must adhere to the previously published guidelines of the Ministry of Health to ensure that there is no transmission of Kovid-19 virus in their stores. In particular, to maintain the safety gap, the Minister of Health would like to introduce the following reminders:
1: Maintaining the social security gap
Maintaining a social security gap means breaking the chain of transmission of the Kovid-19 virus through more than two gatherings.
* Avoid or, if possible, reduce the maximum of social gatherings in crowded societies such as weddings, festivals, such as national festivals, religious ceremonies, traditional festivals or ceremonies. Other concerts, outings, dinners with friends, birthday parties or large-scale housewarming parties, outings and more.
2: Maintaining personal safety gaps
Keeping a personal safety distance means keeping a safe distance from one person to another, such as sitting, standing or standing, waiting or standing, talking for at least 1.5 meters, as the Kovid-19 virus can be transmitted through droplets. When we talk or cough, sneeze, and through contact with the mucus, respiratory tract of the human body, or contact with animals. So we all need to:
When meeting, avoid hugging, kissing, shaking hands, instead of saluting or raising your hand as a signal or nodding your head at a distance of at least 1.5 meters.
* Keep a distance of at least 1.5 meters from one to another, use a mask (if necessary) or use a scarf or towel, and always practice good hand hygiene in places such as work, public places, restaurants, restaurants Recreation or tourist attractions and transportation.
* In the event of meetings, training and workshops (as needed), the organizers must ensure that the large, well-ventilated rooms are kept at a distance of at least 1.50 meters above the individual heaters. All participants must wear masks and practice regular hand washing. Individuals with health problems should not attend.
The Ministry of Health calls on all members of the public to follow the instructions of the above Ministry for everyone to be effective for personal health, family health and community health without infection and to prevent There is a second wave of Kovid-19 virus transmission in Cambodia.
