3 museums of APSARA Authority reopen
(Siem Reap): The three museums, which are under the control of the APSARA Authority, will reopen to welcome visitors from June 2, after being closed for a while during the Kovid 19 outbreak. The reopening of the doors is highly concerned with the safety of visitors.
Mr. Seng Sotheara, Deputy Director of Cultural Development, Museums and Heritage Standards of the APSARA Authority, said that the three museums, the Norodom Sihanouk-Angkor Museum, the Museum of Asian Traditional Textiles and the Latani Porcelain Museum, are equipped with alcohol thermometers for monitoring and Safety considerations against Kovid 19 infection.
He added that all visitors will be required to be at a distance of 2 meters from each other if the number of visits during the visit to the museum.
APSARA Authority will continue to open for free to celebrate the 25th anniversary of the establishment of APSARA Authority, which is announced from the beginning of March 2020 until the end of January 2021 in order to promote the history, culture, civilization and traditions. Tradition to tourists of all nationalities knows about Cambodia.
The Deputy Director of the Department of Cultural Development, Museums and Heritage Standards has called on the public as well as national and international tourists to visit the three museums of the APSARA Authority. 19 This. This protection is to ensure the safety of both tourists and the staff of the museum to ensure the safety of Kovid 19 infection.
