He added that with the consideration of the head of the Royal Government, especially General Ke Kim Yan, she provided the wells to the community to irrigate crops in both the dry and wet seasons, where the 12 wells can supply surface water. 23 hectares of land throughout the community is easy for people to cultivate.
The provincial governor also promoted the fund of General Ke Kim Yan and her to help those who want to expand their cultivation but do not have the money to borrow from the fund as well as the Rural Development Bank with the lowest interest rate.
He added that in the past, there was false information that General Ke Kim Yan's fund charged higher interest rates than banks and other microfinance institutions, which caused confusion. In relation to this information, please do not believe in the dissemination of this information is not true, that is, the fund of General Ke Kim Yan and she charge the lowest interest rate to help farmers different from banks and other microfinance institutions.
According to Mr. Chea Yuthearun, Director of the Provincial Department of Rural Development, the water wells provided were 16 wells, 12 of which were provided to the community, 2 wells provided to the Phnom Kang Va tank, and 2 wells provided. Air Force and Kang Wa Pagoda. The well was donated by General Ke Kim Yan and Mrs. under the supervision of the Ministry and the Provincial Department of Rural Development.
The director of the department also confirmed that the 12 wells in the community can irrigate 23 hectares, and each well has a depth of 14 to 52 meters, water flow (drainage force) from 2.5 to 10 cubic meters. One hour can irrigate throughout the dry season and the dry season.
