General knowledge: Panama Canal benefits humanity and Sino-US influence struggle
It is about 77 kilometers long, but the excavations have faced many problems, such as infectious diseases, malaria, yellow fever and landslides. When the project was completed in 1914, an estimated 27,500 workers were killed in the effort from start to finish.
Since the Panama Canal opened in 1914, it has been a resounding success in international shipping. Humans around the world consider the Panama Canal to be one of the Seven Wonders of the Modern World and a representative of the trade revolution.
Ships carrying goods from New York to San Francisco are much easier and faster to cross the canal, with more than 8,000 miles to travel through the Horn Valley. 20,000 kilometers.
Every year, more than 14,000 ships pass through the canal, transporting more than 205 million tons of cargo a year. In 2017, it was noted that the Panama Canal had 13,548 small and large ships passing through, carrying a total of 403.8 million tons of cargo. The journey across the canal takes an average of nine hours.
The expansion of the Panama Canal has enabled more ships to navigate, increasing Panama's revenue. At that time, the Panama Canal expansion project took nine years and a budget of about $ 5,000,000,000.
