Farmers in Kang Va village, Banteay Meanchey province are happy to grow palm because it is popular and sells well
(Banteay Meanchey): The palm plantation in Kang Va village, Sangkat Kampong Svay, Serey Sophorn city, Banteay Meanchey province, is attracting a lot of people to visit and buy it, making the plantation owners happy when they see the support of our Cambodian palm plantations. This.
The owner of a palm plantation in Kang Va village is very happy when the palm tree plant starts to bear fruit and attracts a lot of visitors every day. At the same time, the owner of the plantation sells from 150 to 170 kilograms per day, with a price of 50,000 riels per kilogram.
Yean Men, a 35-year-old plantation owner, said he initially worked as a mobile phone repairman but seized 165 palm trees on four acres. He said he started planting palm trees three years ago.
At first, he was a mobile phone repairer and did not have the techniques to grow palm trees, but what made him interested in growing this crop was because he watched the cultivation on Youtube and thought that growing palm trees was very profitable. This is why he decided to start buying seeds to grow.
For resale, he currently sells for only 50,000 riel per kilogram (previously he sold 60,000 riel per kilogram, if you buy from 2 kg up to 50,000 riel per kilogram). At the same time, he was happy to see many visitors to his farm every day, while some were from Siem Reap, Oddar Meanchey and also bought to take home.
However, Mr. Yean Men requested that people who visit his plantation be free to take pictures, but do not touch or pick unripe fruits. He also requested the department to help promote this palm crop to support our Cambodian products and asked the department to provide additional training related to their cultivation skills for this cultivation to be effective. Better yet.
In addition, Mr. Hul Raya, Governor of Serei Sophorn City, said that throughout Serei Sophorn City, about 60% of the people are engaged in agriculture, all kinds of crops, such as leafy vegetables, tubers and fruits. He said that in the city, there is also a community, the Kang Wa Safe Vegetable Community, which covers an area of 57 hectares and has 46 families involved in planting.
On behalf of the municipal authorities, he said:
* I want people who have vacant land should grab more palm plantations because it is profitable and has a long life. * People who are planting palm trees, he urges to grow more. If there is a lack of funds to expand the cultivation, General Ke Kim Yan has the funds to lend as well as the Rural Development Bank with the lowest interest rate.
