The following is the full text of the NEC Press Release: The Head of the Cambodian Diplomatic Corps: Due to Japan, Cambodia has successfully implemented the Rectangular Strategy.
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, said that due to the large part of Japan's official development assistance, Cambodia has successfully implemented its Rectangular Strategy and has now reached the stage of 4 and has boosted Cambodia's economic growth to more than 7% every year for the last 21 years.
Cambodian Foreign Ministry Spokeswoman Jiang Yu's Regular Press Conference on June 5, 2020, during a joint press conference with Japanese Ambassador to Cambodia Mikami Masahiro Ministry of Foreign Affairs.
The head of diplomacy was pleased to sign with Ambassador Mikami an exchange of letters on a Japanese grant of 4,501 million yen (US $ 41.4 million). Provided by the Government of Japan to the Royal Government of Cambodia for the implementation of three projects:
348 million yen (approximately 3.2 million US dollars) for human resource development projects through a scholarship program for talented young Cambodian officers to pursue master's and doctoral studies in Japan.
* 2,153 million yen (approximately 19.8 million US dollars) for the improvement of health centers, medical equipment and health care services in referral hospitals in Siem Reap.
* 2 billion yen (approximately US $ 18.4 million) for economic and social development programs through the provision of medical equipment for the fight against Kovid-19 in Cambodia.
Mr. Prak Sokhon reminded that on March 24, 2020, the Royal Government of Japan provided grants and concessional loans totaling 34,138 million yen (approximately 310 million US dollars) for three projects: 1: Expansion Water supply in Takhmao City 2: Demining and assistance for mine victims C: Economic and Social Development Program and D: Improvement of National Road 5.
He thanked Ambassador Mikami and his team in Cambodia for their active support and efforts in promoting friendship and cooperation in all fields between Japan and Cambodia.
On that occasion, Mikami said that the world is now facing an unprecedented threat of Kovid 19 and that international cooperation is indispensable. The virus is also a threat to human life and the dignity of the individual, which has a serious impact on the socio-economy.
According to the ambassador, to date, Japan has led international efforts to achieve global health insurance. Considering that Kovid 19 is affecting countries where the health system is still weak, he reiterated the importance of strengthening the health system in all countries, not just symptomatic measures. Japan's commitment is based on this idea and the needs of Cambodia.
"In today's globalization, the entire international community must work together against Kovid 19," he said. While deeply appreciating the efforts of the Royal Government of Cambodia to manage this difficult situation well, I sincerely hope that we will be able to continue to cooperate to overcome all our common obstacles in the future. I promise that Japan will continue to move forward in cooperation with Cambodia. ”
