(Phnom Penh): Dr. Sok Po, President of the National Blood Transfusion Center, said that the center is now reaching a difficult stage without blood storage to save the lives of patients who need blood while patients need blood every day. At least 270 blogs to save lives.
The President of the National Blood Transfusion Center said, "As of the first five months of 2020, the National Blood Transfusion Center received 27,000 units of blood from almost all of the patients' families for about 200 volunteers. Only. "Because of the Kovid 19 crisis, we are not holding big events to call for life-saving blood donations, and the number of blood donors has dropped significantly compared to previous years."
This statement was made by Dr. Sok Po on the occasion of the management and staff of Ariana Polyclinic and Maternity Hospital donating blood at the National Blood Transfusion Center, led by Ms. Koun Thida, Director General of Ariana Polyclinic and Maternity Hospital on June 05, 2020 This.
On that occasion, the President of the National Blood Transfusion Center expressed his deep gratitude to Ariana Polyclinic and Maternity Hospital for donating blood, which is one of the best gifts that can save the lives of patients in hospitals that need blood.
In addition, he also called on young volunteers who used to donate blood to the center, "Please continue to donate blood, our team is still waiting for the invitation to donate and urge the public to participate more to save "The lives of those who need blood are needed, especially for patients who do not have siblings and need blood every month to save lives."
Ms. Koun Thida said, "Blood donation is equal to saving lives, we are always actively involved, because this is a reward for society as well as the general public, that's why we set up a blood donation program. Today. ”
Donating blood can not only save the lives of patients and society, it also benefits those who donate. Blood transfusions automatically increase the production of red blood cells in the human body.
In addition, donating blood can reduce the risk of heart disease because all blood transfusions reduce some of the iron in the blood. In addition, regular blood transfusions every three to four months will help improve health by donating blood, which burns some of the energy during each blood transfusion and reduces the risk of cancer. Also.
She said that the blood donation program is part of the humanitarian program of Ariana Hospital and Obstetrics and Gynecology, which is born of true love and shows the utmost care for the people of Cambodia. This humanitarian activity is a contribution to the National Blood Transfusion Center to meet the urgent needs of the current blood supply.
