Samdech Techo, Head of the Royal Government, stated that the third ring road, which is an important road to help reduce congestion and facilitate traffic in Phnom Penh, this road is scheduled to be used for 42 months, which is scheduled to be completed in December 2021. .
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated on Facebook that "The construction of the third ring road was opened on January 14, 2019 under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and the Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia. So far, the construction of the third ring road has been completed 37 percent, and according to the plan, construction will take 42 months, scheduled to be completed in December 2021.
The Third Ring Road is an important road to reduce traffic congestion and facilitate traffic in Phnom Penh, and is also an internal connection and integration of special areas connecting ASEAN highways and major economic corridors. "The Greater Mekong Subregion contributes to the facilitation of cross-border transport, promotes international trade and turns the land on either side of the ring road into a development zone."
Please be informed that the third ring road, nearly 53 kilometers long, passing through Phnom Penh and Kandal province, with a construction budget of nearly 300 million US dollars, was opened for construction on January 14, 2019. The groundbreaking ceremony for the important transportation and travel of Cambodians was presided over by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Wang Wentian, Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia.
The construction of the Third Ring Road (National Road No. 4-National Road No. 1) is located in Phnom Penh and Kandal Province, with a total length of nearly 53 km, including more than 15 km through Phnom Penh and Kandal Province. Nearly 38 km, starting at km 14 + 105 of National Road 4 and ending at km 24 + 840 of National Road No. 1.
This road has a width of up to 27 meters for the city, for out of town, the width of the road is 25 meters. The road will have street lights for city streets and ornamental trees for suburban roads.
The third ring road will have four flyovers (crossing National Roads 4, 3, 2 and 21) with a total length of 1,000 meters. Construction of 2 bridges across the Bassac River at Anlong Chen Island with a total length of 996 meters (including the 630-meter-long East Bassac Bridge and the 366-meter-long West Bassac Bridge). Construction of 6 medium and short bridges and 113 sewers of all kinds.
The road project will cost a total of 273 million US dollars, which is a concessional financing from the Chinese government, and the Royal Government of Cambodia contributes to the impact of demining and unexploded ordnance, taxes and royalties.
