NBC will host the 7th Annual Macroeconomic Conference on "Discussing the Cambodian Economic Development Model"
(Phnom Penh): The National Bank of Cambodia (NBC) has issued a new announcement on the organization of the 7th Annual Macroeconomic Conference 2020 under the theme "Discussion on the Cambodian Economic Development Model" which is scheduled to take place. In December 2020.
According to the announcement of the National Bank of Cambodia, since the beginning of 2020, the outbreak of Kovid 19 has severely affected the world economy, especially in countries that rely on the external sector due to Declining international trade and investment.
The global health crisis, which is becoming the economic crisis, has changed the economic process, relating to the economic structure in and after the crisis. For Cambodia, due to the open economy and strong dependence on external sectors, including exports of textiles, tourism, construction and investment, economic growth in 2020 will face the same decline as other countries in the world.
In order to adapt to the new context of the global economy, what kind of economic model should Cambodia implement that can be resilient to crises and successfully achieve its planned goals? In this context, the NBC has selected the theme research topic on "Discussion on the Cambodian Economic Development Model" for the 7th Annual Macroeconomic Conference.
The conference aims to promote research on the above topics and provide a forum for discussion on a sustainable economic development model that can be an input into the formulation of economic policies to achieve a future vision.
