(Phnom Penh): Wing Specialized Bank (Cambodia) Limited and Aeon Mall (Cambodia) Co., Ltd., the leading and largest supermarkets in Cambodia, have signed a partnership to provide shopping and Convenient service without using banknotes to customers at both Aeon Mall locations.
Manura Chan, CEO of Wing Specialized Bank, said: “We believe that this partnership will give you more freedom to buy better products and services. "Payment using QR codes is becoming popular all over the world because of its convenience and security."
Through this new partnership, customers at Aeon Mall can shop for products and services without having to carry a banknote, just by tapping a finger on a smartphone with a Wing account to gain a shopping experience. Safe and up-to-date. Customers can scan the QR code at the counter for instant transactions.
Mr. Tsubuya Masayuki, CEO of AEON Mall (Cambodia) Co., Ltd., said: “We are delighted that Wing Specialized Bank and AEON Mall can work together to do this. "Together we use financial technology to provide more choices and better shopping to our customers in Cambodia."
Both Wing Specialized Bank and Aeon Mall (Cambodia) Co., Ltd. share the same goal of creating a payment system that is convenient for customers.
For the start of this partnership, the first 1,000 customers will receive an instant $ 5 discount on every WR QR code payment to purchase goods and services at nearly 30 stores in Aeon Mall Phnom Penh. And Aeon Mall Sen Sok City, from food and beverage outlets to clothing and electronics stores.
Wing Specialized Bank has established a strong brand through its Wing Smartphone app and more than 7,500 Wing agents across Cambodia that can provide convenient, secure and fast financial services.
