The approval of this draft law took place in the 4th session of the National Assembly of the 6th legislature under the chairmanship of Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, in the presence of 111 members of the National Assembly at the beginning of the session on the morning of June 5. 2020.
"Draft Law on Mutual Legal Aid in the Criminal Field" consists of 6 chapters and 44 articles, with Dr. Pen Panha, Chairman of the Legislative and Justice Committee of the National Assembly, reporting to the National Assembly on the results of the study. The draft law and Mr. Keut Rith, Minister of Justice, and his associates representing the Royal Government defended the draft law.
"Draft Law on Mutual Legal Aid in the Criminal Sector" has the following contents:
Within the framework of legal cooperation in the field of criminal law, the Kingdom of Cambodia has signed bilateral and multilateral treaties with many countries, especially treaties related to extradition, transfer of prisoners and mutual assistance. Law in the criminal field.
Although the Kingdom of Cambodia has provided legal assistance in the field of criminal law to many countries, including countries that have had treaties with Cambodia and countries that have not had treaties with Cambodia in the past, the Kingdom does not yet have an internal law. Clear to ensure the implementation of requests for mutual legal assistance in the criminal field yet.
The purpose of this law is to provide legal assistance in the field of criminal affairs between the Kingdom of Cambodia and foreign states in relation to criminal proceedings, as well as to freeze, seize and confiscate property in order to strengthen And expand international cooperation.
* Seeking legal assistance in the field of criminal justice from all requesting states, even if the requesting state does not have an agreement with the Kingdom of Cambodia. This law does not apply to legal mutual assistance in the criminal field in accordance with bilateral or multilateral treaties or conventions ratified by the Kingdom of Cambodia.
