Discover the origins of the clock and the evolution of modernization
(Phnom Penh): The history of the clock began in the early 16th century in Europe, as it evolved from a portable watch, which first appeared in the 15th century. The evolution of the clock during the 16th to mid-20th centuries is that it is all mechanical, equipped with a magnetic wire with a rotating pointer to tell the time.
Peter Henlein is a young designer who is often praised by teachers as well as mathematics professors for his intelligence. Because he was able to transform many shapes, from ordinary metal shapes into watch shapes.
In the 1960s, electric clocks were able to display the time and minutes on a type of crystal glass, marking a significant development for the industry. During the 1980s, this type of crystal watch completely invaded the watch market, leading the masses to call the event a "crystalline presence crisis."
This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen inspects the magnificent and beautiful building of the Cambodian People's Party (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party, inspects the building on June 05, 2020. The CPP headquarters is located along Norodom Blvd. in Tonle Bassac commune, Chamkar Mon district, next to the Senate building.
The new building of the CPP headquarters was built on the site of the old building, which is about 1.6 hectares and has a height of 5 floors, building area of more than 50,000 square meters. The headquarters of the Cambodian People's Party, the ruling party of the Royal Government, was built with a fine and elegant Khmer style. From the outside, the whole building is highlighted in white, a symbol of sincerity for the nation and its people.
The CPP headquarters building is almost complete, about 95%. The sublime and beautiful presence of the CPP headquarters building is highlighted on the occasion of the 69th anniversary of the CPP.
The majestic presence of the building is also a demonstration of the strength and symbol of the great unity and prosperity of the Cambodian People's Party, which is an indispensable reference for the nation and the people of Cambodia from the past to the present and to The future. ASEAN, ASEAN + 3 trade ministers discuss economic recovery from Kovid 19 crisis
(Phnom Penh): The Ministers of Trade and Economy of ASEAN and ASEAN Plus 3 on June 4, 2020, met through a video system to discuss ways to recover the economy after the severe crisis caused by Kovid. 19.
The meeting was chaired by Tran Tuan Anh, Minister of Industry and Trade of Vietnam, the host of ASEAN 2020, and attended by the ASEAN Economic Ministers of Japan, China, South Korea and the ASEAN Secretary-General.
For the special meeting, the ASEAN Economic Ministers noted and discussed the proposal to establish a High-Level Special Commission on the Response to Kovid 19 and Economic Recovery of the ASEAN Business Council. The meeting also exchanged experiences on the fight against Kovid 19 and discussed strengthening ASEAN economic cooperation and supply chain linkages in response to the Kovid 19 outbreak.
At the ASEAN + 3 Economic Ministers' Special Meeting, ASEAN Economic Ministers exchanged views on the situation of Kovid 19 in the region and shared measures to fight Kovid 19.
During these two important meetings, Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce and Minister of Economy for ASEAN, shared and recommended to ASEAN Member States to diversify the supply chain and use Industry 4.0 to achieve Set goals.
The Minister also encouraged quick and consistent response and cooperation through existing ASEAN Plus Three mechanisms to combat Kovid 19. Mr. Pan Sosak also thanked China, Japan, South Korea for helping Cambodia to fight Kovid 19 through financial, technical and medical assistance. The Minister of Justice and the Chinese Ambassador supported the strengthening of cooperation. Bilateral to be stronger
On that occasion, the Minister of Justice and the Ambassador expressed their support for further strengthening and expanding bilateral cooperation through cooperation on law enforcement, capacity building and infrastructure construction.
According to the Ministry of Justice, the two sides also praised the excellent and comprehensive cooperation between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the People's Republic of China in the past, including Human resource development, law enforcement and strengthening social security.
The two leaders also expressed concern over the impact of the Covid19 epidemic on both the economic and social sectors, and the two leaders also expressed their support for each other. To contribute to reducing the effects of this disease.
