Very symphonic! 1-year-old baby dies after falling from bed in sewer in Chamkarmon
(Phnom Penh): A 1-year-old baby died while sleeping with his three brothers and sisters and his aunt forgot to fall from the bed into the sewer, causing drowning at 9:30 am on the 4th. June 2020, Group 31, irregular construction in Village 5, Sangkat Phsar Doeum Thkov, Khan Chamkarmon, Phnom Penh.
The body of a 1-year-old boy named Rin Thearith lives with his aunt at the scene. His father, 41-year-old Rin Piseth, is a scavenger.
According to her aunt, Prum Srey Touch, 40, a scavenger, she got up at about 2 o'clock before the incident and left her children to sleep with three other siblings after returning from scrap collecting. The youngest son disappeared and went to find the child fell between the walls into the sewer and died, causing a surprise and immediately reported to the authorities to come down to the scene to control Check.
The district police confirmed that the victim's family did not complain to any person, but the police wanted to clarify the contact of the Phnom Penh Municipal Forensic Office to come to the scene to examine the body and confirmed that the boy really died from drowning. Of course, after making the record, the body was handed over to the relatives for the traditional ceremony, the police only expressed their condolences and advised to be careful to avoid any future incidents.
