The signing ceremony was held in the presence of General Meas Virith, Secretary General of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, with Mr. Tho Meas Kay, President of AIDS Cambodia on the afternoon of June 4, 2020 at the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs. Addicted.
Lt. Gen. Lim Tong Huot said that the purpose of the K-Twilight Agreement was to raise awareness of the dangers posed by drugs to vulnerable groups through the participation of all members of society through community movements for drug addicts. Addicts volunteer to come and receive quality and reliable treatment services.
Tho Meas Kay stated that AIDS Care China is committed to supporting policies and strategies to reduce the dangers of drugs and community-based treatment of drug addicts in Cambodia. In the past, we have conducted joint trials to encourage drug addicts to receive treatment for drug addicts in the communities of Sangkat Chbar Ampov 1 and Chbar Ampov 2.
