(Phnom Penh): More than 130 tons of illegal drugs and counterfeit products were burnt on May 4, 2020 after the Anti-Counterfeit Products Committee, which poses a high risk to health and social safety of the Ministry of Interior. Surface cracked in the past.
The cremation ceremony was presided over by Professor Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, with the permission of the judiciary and with the approval of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior.
According to the report of General Miech Sophanna, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior and Chairman of the Committee, the burnt goods included: 225 kinds of expired medicines equal to 6 tons, Chinese traditional medicine, food supplements. , Counterfeit cosmetics and general counterfeit products, many other types of expired food products.
General Miech Sophan claimed that the current demolition ceremony is a message to some crooks who produce, store and distribute counterfeit products that as long as illegal activities destroy the health, well-being of the people and social security. Meanwhile, the committee is still trying to prevent and confiscate and destroy without exception or mitigation.
