Joint reporters help elderly journalists in traffic accidents with broken legs when returning from covering news in Sihanoukville
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ou Chantha, 73 years old, working as a journalist on Koh Santepheap, had a traffic accident with a broken right leg on the night of June 1, 2020, when he returned from covering the news of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia. In Sihanoukville.
On the night of June 1, 2020, at 12 o'clock on the night of returning from Sihanoukville to Phnom Penh, Mr. Ou Chantha rode a motorcycle back home in Sangkat Kilometer 6, Khan Russey Keo. Occasionally, while riding a motorcycle back home, it was raining and windy. The wind and rain forced Ou Chantha to fall on the flyover on January 7 and broke his right leg after heavy rain and strong winds.
After the motorcycle crashed, Mr. Ou Chantha's consciousness was normal, so he called his family and took the tricycle to the hospital.
After working for the Evening News for two years, in 2002 Mr. Chantha moved to work for Koh Santepheap until today. During his 18 years at Koh Santepheap, Mr. Chantha was assigned by the unit to cover the case of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
In his career as a journalist for almost 30 years, Mr. Ou Chantha is still in a situation where his living conditions are not much better. Currently, the source of income for his career as a journalist is no longer stable, as his unit no longer provides the same monthly salary as before, switching to paid articles instead.
Mr. Ou Chantha stated, "In exchange for paying this amount of articles, some months I get paid only $ 30."
Seeing the shortcomings and difficulties of Mr. Ou Chantha, reporters following Samdech Techo and journalists from various institutions have jointly raised funds to help treat his injuries.
In addition to the journalists mentioned above, there are also journalists from other media units who have come together to help solve Ou Chantha's difficulties.
In addition to his colleagues, the Royal Government of Cambodia and an assistant advisor to Samdech Techo Hun Sen also donated money to help Mr. Ou Chantha. Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Samdech Techo Hun Sen's personal assistant, who was always willing to help all the difficulties of the journalists, donated $ 250.
Mr. Muth Khieu, Personal Adviser to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Secretary of State of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, donated 1 million Riels.
This donation is a valuable contribution to solve the difficulties of Mr. Ou Chantha. Through Fresh News, Mr. Ou Chantha expressed his sincere gratitude to Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Mr. Huy Vannak, President of the Federation of Cambodian Journalists, Mr. Lim Chea Vutha and all journalists.
The National Assembly issues a press release on the results of the 4th National Assembly meeting of the 6th legislature (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The General Secretariat of the National Assembly on June 4, 2020 6 National Assembly chaired by Samdech Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly of Cambodia.
According to the press release of the National Assembly received by Fresh News on June 4, 2020, the meeting discussed and approved the agenda with the following two results:
First, the draft law on combating financing for the proliferation of weapons of mass destruction. This draft law has 8 chapters and 24 articles.
* Mr. Hun Neng, Chairman of the Committee on Interior, National Defense and Public Function of the National Assembly, reports to the National Assembly on the results of the study of the draft law. * Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior Defend the draft law * The members of the National Assembly who spoke in the discussion of this draft law were Ms. Kheng * The National Assembly approved the whole draft law with 119 votes.
Second, the draft law on "anti-money laundering and terrorist financing". This draft law has 9 chapters and 47 articles.
* Mr. HUN Neng reports to the National Assembly on the results of the study of the draft law * Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng and his colleagues representing the Royal Government defend the draft law * The number of members of the National Assembly who commented on the discussion of this draft law Two are Mr. Chheang Vun and Mr. Serey Kosal. * The National Assembly approved the entire draft law by 118 votes.
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Kampong Thom Province, reminded all heads of departments to pay attention to improving their units and have a high sense of responsibility for work and increase human resources to be effective. Help solve problems and provide public services to the people more quickly, timely and transparently.
Mr. Sok Lou said this this morning, June 4, 2020, at the 12th Ordinary Meeting of Kampong Thom Provincial Council of the third mandate at Kampong Thom Provincial Hall with the participation of Provincial Councilors. Also a member of the provincial council, chairman, deputy director of departments around the province.
Mr. Sok Lou also instructed the local officials to strengthen their work. In addition, the team must meet with the people often to help solve and consult all the problems that people face and submit plans to local officials in Management of security, public order, as well as disseminating the Royal Government's regulations to the people.
It should be noted that the agenda of this meeting is: Review and approve the minutes of the 11th Ordinary Meeting of the Provincial Council, Review and approve the report for May 2020 of the Provincial Administration, Review and approve the decision on the calendar of the Convention Of the Provincial Council of the third mandate, second year, 2020-2021, other issues.
209 Families Living in Natural Village, Choam Ksan District Lottery Lottery for Preah Vihear Provincial Authority
(Preah Vihear): 209 families living in Thomcheat village, Sra Em commune, Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province, this morning, June 4, 2020, participated in the lottery to receive agricultural plots, which are social land concessions given by the Royal Government through the authorities. Preah Vihear province is the second step after the first step, 99 families have been selected.
The draw for the agricultural land was held in the presence of Mr. Prak Sovann, Governor of Preah Vihear Province and Chairman of the Provincial State Land Management Committee, Lt. Gen. Srey Duek, Commander of Intervention Division 3, with the participation of the provincial leadership. Departments, relevant units and local authorities, villages, communes and districts.
Mr. Prak Sovann stated that the agricultural land given to the people started from Sub-Decree No. 2, dated January 6, 2016 on the demarcation of community area within the Kulen Prom Tep Wildlife Sanctuary area. 5,000 hectares in Yeang and Kantuot communes, Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province.
The provincial governor further stated that Preah Vihear province received a sub-decree to define community areas in 2016 in the previous mandate of the provincial governor. In particular, in 2020, during his term as the provincial governor, he assigned the working group of the Provincial Land Allocation and Use Committee to provide social land concessions (agricultural land) to 1,045 families who have already received residential land in natural villages.
At the same time, Mr. Prak Sovann also instructed the local authorities and relevant authorities to comply with the laws, regulations and laws in force as well as the regulations of the Royal Government effectively and with a high sense of responsibility to prevent land encroachment. New states are strictly prohibited in order to preserve the country's natural resources for future generations.
The Chinese Embassy believes that the direct export of mangoes to China will also promote the development of Cambodia's agricultural sector.
"On Tuesday morning next week, the ministry will sign a formal protocol to export fresh mangoes to China," he said.
This is the second success in the negotiations to export fresh fruits from Cambodia directly to China, the first success in the export of fresh bananas to China. Apart from mangoes, Cambodia is also trading with China to export Tangen (Mien Pelin), dragon fruit and radish directly to China. Currently, five Cambodian agricultural products are allowed to be exported directly by the Chinese side: rice, cassava chips, cashews and bananas.
Cambodia and South Korea have already signed an agreement to allow Cambodian fresh mangoes to be exported directly to Korea.
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of June 5, 2020, Cambodia and Japan will sign an exchange of letters and minutes of discussions on the provision of grant financing totaling 4,501 million yen (approximately 41 $ 4 million) for the implementation of three projects in Cambodia.
