By: Chao Chak Smok, Kamchay Mear District, Prey Veng Province, June 4, 2020 Koh Kong Provincial Administration: A group of people who are detained by the authorities to keep bicycles, not to ride a bike to exercise
(Koh Kong): The Koh Kong provincial administration has confirmed that a group of 17 people, including Rong Chhun, president of the Cambodian Confederation of Trade Unions, did not ride bicycles to exercise, but it was against the law. Notification to the authorities and in support of the "Mother Nature" organization, which has been removed by the Ministry of Interior.
On June 3, 2020, a group of 17 people who pretended to be environmental youths rode their bicycles from Koh Kong province to Phnom Penh to submit a petition to the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen. To support the Koh Kong Krao area.
When they gathered to travel, they were questioned by the authorities and asked for cooperation to maintain safety and health for the trip, they did not cooperate, so the authorities decided to keep their bikes. After the authorities confiscated the bicycles, there were some advertisements on social media and some information that the authorities and the Koh Kong provincial authorities blocked the people's right not to exercise.
On the other hand, the visit of the authorities in order to help maintain their safety in travel, as well as help keep their health from the 19 cases of Kovid.
The Koh Kong Provincial Administration stated its intention that "the gathering of cyclists with a distance of several kilometers must cooperate to protect the safety and prevent accidents that occur and on the other hand, this group of individuals did not notify the decision. Local authorities to cooperate. The rallies and rallies during the crisis-code 19 are contrary to the guidelines of the Royal Government and the Ministry of Health.
The Koh Kong Provincial Administration added that the activities of the local authorities and the doctors who visited the cycling team were to measure the temperature and to request the cooperation of the authorities, but this group did not cooperate, so the authorities stopped their bikes. Temporarily stored at the Koh Kong District Police Inspectorate.
The Koh Kong provincial administration has stated that "this is not a violation of individual rights, but to maintain security, safety and public order, and to participate in preventing the spread of the disease and fighting the 19 Code."
In this statement, the provincial administration claimed that the Koh Kong provincial administration always pays attention to the cooperation of all legal organizations and youths to promote environmental protection activities in accordance with national political principles.
