(Phnom Penh): On the morning of June 4, 2020, the National Assembly convened a plenary session to discuss and approve four draft laws proposed by the Royal Government.
The plenary session of the National Assembly was chaired by Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly of Cambodia, and was attended by 119 members of the National Assembly as well as representatives of the Royal Government.
The agenda of this plenary session is:
First, the discussion and approval of the draft law on anti-financing for the proliferation of weapons of mass destruction.
Second: Discussion and approval of the draft law on anti-money laundering and terrorist financing.
Third: Discussion and approval of the draft law on legal mutual assistance in the field of criminal
Fourth: Discussion and approval of the draft law on the approval of the Kingdom of Cambodia to be a party to the Bern Convention on the Protection of Literature and Art in 1886 and the 1979 amendment.
