Cambodia, Timor-Leste agree to boost tourism cooperation
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia-Timor-Leste have expressed common intentions to expand cooperation in the field of tourism, in which the Cambodian side also urged Timor-Leste to expedite the signing of a Memorandum of Understanding on Tourism Cooperation. Also between the two countries, as the memorandum was initiated a long time ago but has not been signed.
Minister Thong Khon welcomed Ambassador Kupa's proposal, as it was in line with his desire to expand and strengthen cooperation with other countries, such as Cambodia-Timor-Leste. And later also become brothers in the same area.
Regarding the wishes of the people of Timor-Leste who want to visit Cambodia, Minister Thong Khon expressed his satisfaction as Cambodia has been working hard to better prepare for the return of international tourists in the future. At the end of the global Kovid crisis, Cambodia will look forward to welcoming Timor-Leste.
At the same time, Minister Thong Khon requested the Timor-Leste government through Ambassador Kupa to expedite the signing of a Memorandum of Understanding on Tourism Cooperation between Cambodia and Timor-Leste. For a long time, the aim was to bring the two countries' cooperation closer. The proposal was immediately accepted by Kupa to report to his government.
Mr. Try Chhiv, Director of the Department of International and ASEAN Cooperation, stated that the Memorandum of Understanding focuses on the development of tourism products, providing mutual experience, promoting the development of human resources in the field of tourism and increasing the attraction of tourists. Come and go for more.
Mr. Trivich said that at the end of the Kovid-19 crisis, both sides will also consider the possibility of connecting Cambodia-Timor-Leste direct flights.
