WASHINGTON (Reuters) - The Pentagon on Tuesday confirmed that it had accepted South Korea's proposed plan to provide more than $ 200 million for the wages of South Korean workers. All who work at US military bases from now until the end of the year. This is according to the release by the Xinhua News Agency on Wednesday, June 3, 2020.
However, the two allies have not yet reached an agreement on sharing the cost of the US military presence in South Korea (SMA). "We strongly encourage our allies to reach an agreement on equality as soon as possible," the Pentagon said in a statement.
Note that since September 2019, the two countries have held several rounds of talks on the 11th SMA, but the two sides have not reached any joint agreement after Washington demanded Seoul increases its contribution
Since 1991, South Korea has helped share the cost of US military bases in its country, including the cost of South Korean civilians working for the US military. There are currently about 28,500 US troops stationed in South Korea.
Ministry of Tourism decides to introduce safety rules and special codes of conduct for 4 major tourism businesses in and after Kovid 19
(Phnom Penh): In order to contribute to the effectiveness of the prevention of the spread of Covid-19 disease that the Royal Government and the Ministry of Health have launched and after detailed consultation with the Ministry of Health and the private sector, the Ministry of Tourism has decided Issued a Prakas on Tourism Safety Rules for Tourism Services Businesses and Code of Conduct for four major businesses.
In the meeting of the leaders of the Ministry of Tourism on June 3, 2020, chaired by Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, the meeting presented the four types of tourism services business, including: * Tourism accommodation business * Restaurant business and canteen tourism * Business, transportation, tourism, waterway, land * Tourism business, tourism, community, tourism.
These tourism safety rules also define a number of conditions, including the essential requirements and the optional conditions that the tourism service business must be prepared to meet.
Along with the implementation of the above tourism safety rules and codes of conduct, the Ministry of Tourism has also issued "Do's and Don'ts" guidelines for tourism in the Kovid 19 phase in Khmer and foreign languages. .
According to Minister Thong Khon, the Prakas on Tourism Safety Rules and Code of Conduct for implementation will be announced on June 5, 2020.
