Minister of Public Works: This year suspends the recruitment of new staff to save money to prevent Kovid 19 (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Minister of Public Works, Mr. Prum Sokha, said that in 2020, the Ministry will suspend the recruitment of staff of all ministries and institutions Units across the country to reduce the cost of the national budget to be used in the fight against Kovi-19.
The statement of the Minister of Civil Service was made during the inauguration ceremony of the leaders and civil servants of the Ministry of Civil Service on June 3, 2020 at the Royal School of Administration.
Minister Prum Sokha further stated that the suspension of the recruitment of new staff is in all institutions involved in the field of public functions, even the judiciary. He said that before the Royal Government announced that the national budget is sufficient to spend, but at that time there was no Kovid disease, when there is a Kovid crisis, it is necessary to save.
He also revealed the plan to request the suspension of the promotion of civil servants for one year, for the common benefit of saving the national budget to spend on the fight against Kovid-19, because the Ministry of Public Works must have Manage the framework and manage the salary with savings.
He explained to the civil servants that this campaign against Kovid is not the responsibility of the Ministry of Health alone, but involves all ministries, institutions, departments and units that must work together for the common public health of the Cambodian people. .
