Ministry of Labor informs nearly 50,000 workers of 165 factories to pay allowances from the Royal Government after receiving a text message (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training on the 3rd In June 2020, a notice was issued to 49,960 workers from 165 factories in the garment and tourism sectors who received permission to suspend employment contracts to pay government allowances.
Ministry of Labor Announcement Received by Fresh News on the morning of June 3, the Ministry of Labor calls on the workers of all 165 factories to pay government subsidies at Wing after receiving Message about the payment of government subsidies to the telephone number you provided to the Ministry through the factory administration in the past.
This allowance will be paid in KHR and depends on the number of days of contract suspension, in which amount:
In order to avoid the difficulty of reimbursing the Royal Government, in case the factory applies to work before the end of the contract period, the allowance will be divided in two times for those who have suspended the contract from 21 days to 1 Monthly, and will be divided into 4 times for those who hang their work contract for 2 months, each time equal to the budget of 82,000 Riels (US $ 20).
The Ministry of Labor states that Wing Specialized Bank will return this subsidy to the Royal Government if you fail to pay this allowance within 10 days after receiving a text message from Wing Specialized Bank. To pay this allowance, you need to bring your Cambodian ID card and the phone number that received the message to the nearest Wing agent.
Please note that you are not required to pay the service fee to Wing Agent when paying this allowance. In case the workers working in these 165 factories do not receive a phone message from Wing Specialized Bank, please contact for more information or update their phone number to their factory administration immediately.
