Japanese grant to launch large-scale automatic garbage collection equipment in Phnom Penh
The inauguration ceremony took place on the morning of Tuesday, June 2, 2020, with the participation of the Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh, First Secretary of the Embassy of Japan in Cambodia, Japan Cooperation Agency in Cambodia ( JICA), CTI Consulting, and the project's TOA construction contractor.
According to a senior JICA official, the mechanical screen is an automatic mechanical system that can help collect garbage in front of sewers at four pumping stations built in the second phase of the flood protection project. This machine is installed in 4 locations, at 4 pumping stations, including: Chaktomuk, Preah Komlong, Central Market and Old Market.
It should be noted that in the previous process, people were required to dive into the pit to remove garbage from the screen, while the new mechanical screen, the garbage is removed by automatic machines and transferred out by mechanical equipment. In addition, the new mechanical screens will contribute to maintaining the city's sewer system, providing operational safety and protecting the aquatic environment by eliminating debris from the sewer system.
The Royal Government of Japan plans to provide the Royal Government of Cambodia with a grant of 12,299,000,000 yen (approximately 114,148,868 US dollars) for flood protection, which is divided into four phases.
