Obey the traffic law, do not violate the speed limit! 6 killed and 21 injured in traffic accidents nationwide on June 1 yesterday
(Phnom Penh): According to the report of the General Commission of the National Police, on June 1, 2020, there were 9 traffic accidents nationwide, resulting in 6 deaths, 6 minor injuries and serious injuries. 15 people.
According to the same source, the causes of traffic accidents include: competition, drunkenness, disrespect for rights, disrespect for the right and vehicle factors.
Please be informed that in order to facilitate the people who have questions about the traffic law, especially the implementation of fines for traffic violations under the new sub-decree, the National Police has officially launched the 117 hotline with officials. Standing 24 hours a day. Call 117 for questions related to traffic rules, there is no charge for all systems.
Spokesman of the General Commission: In the past 32 days, 45,779 vehicles have been inspected and fined according to the new sub-decree
(Phnom Penh): For 32 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to June 1, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected and fined 45,779 vehicles, including 33,585 motorcycles and 12,194 vehicles of all types. This was confirmed by Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun, Deputy Commissioner General and spokesman for the National Police General Commission, to Fresh News.
According to the lieutenant general, for June 1, 2020, there were 9 traffic accidents, killing 6 people and injuring 21 people (15 seriously injured).
Notable offenses for motorcycles are no helmet, offense without license plate, overweight and using a mobile phone, while offense noticing for a car is speeding, no seat belt, offending signal, using an unlicensed phone and getting drunk.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun continued that during the 32 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine the offending vehicle went well.
He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
