Phnom Penh Capital Administration announces traffic diversion at Chom Chao flyover and subway construction site for 60 days
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Capital Administration on June 1, 2020 issued a notice to people who travel through the construction site of the flyover and subway Choam Chao know that as of May 29, 2020 results The construction of the Chom Chao flyover and subway has reached 41% of the project, which is planned to be completed by the end of 2021.
Therefore, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration requests the people to be kind, tolerant and to divert traffic along the following road directions:
A: Vehicles traveling in the direction of entering Phnom Penh on National Road No. 4 are: * On the way to the Boulevard of the Russian Federation, turn left in front of the construction site to National Road No. 4, which has two newly created traffic lanes. Take Veng Sreng Road straight to the former Chom Chao roundabout and continue towards Veng Sreng Road * On the way to National Road 3, go straight to the former Chom Chao roundabout and turn right onto National Road 3
B: Vehicles traveling in the direction of entering Phnom Penh on National Road No. 3 are: * On the way to the Boulevard of the Russian Federation, must reach the former roundabout Chaom Chao and then go straight as usual * On the left turn towards the national road No. 4: Go to the former Chaom Chao roundabout and turn left onto National Road No. 4 * On the way to Veng Sreng road, take the former Chom Chao roundabout and turn right onto Veng Sreng road
Receiving this announcement, Phnom Penh Municipal Police, Phnom Penh Gendarmerie Command, Po Sen Chey District Administration, Phnom Penh Department of Public Works and Transport, Cambodian Overseas Investment Companies and relevant authorities must cooperate to implement this notice responsibly. And highly effective.
