(Siem Reap): The Intangible Heritage Registration Team of the APSARA Authority decided to register 711 pieces of art objects collected from the people and at the 91 temples in the Angkor resort to be safe and have a valid identity for the purpose of use. The next day.
The listing of the 91 artefacts is intended to document the identification of the artefacts in order to prevent them from being moved or lost in the long run. In this form of identification is provided specific information about the type of sculpture, source, material, size, location, date, photographs and descriptions, and this information alone can facilitate the repair work and the return claim in Any lost case.
