Cambodia's Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen (R) shakes hands with Cambodian Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra in Phnom Penh on June 1, 2013. This year 2020 has sent a message criticizing some countries that have attacked the Cambodian health sector, as the country is experiencing a series of 19 deaths from Kovid and Cambodia has not had a single 19 Kovid patients.
Speech by Samdech Techo Hun Sen was made during a meeting with officials and technical team for road infrastructure construction in Sihanoukville, Preah Sihanouk Province after inspecting the construction process of concrete road from Ream coast Towards Otres and Ochheuteal beaches.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that the world era of Kovid 19 outbreak did not think that rich or poor countries, if they are not careful or lack measures to control their people, will definitely face great challenges. Cambodia is not a medically advanced country, but it has taken this issue seriously.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "Some countries that have advanced medicine and rich countries lack masks, protective equipment for doctors and let doctors get infected and write bad things about us." "Cambodia's health care system is weak, Laos' health system is weak, Myanmar is weak, this country is weak, but the developed country itself can not find the land to bury and then have the right to write to mock others."
According to the Prime Minister of Cambodia, the prince once told the doctors that if you do not have enough equipment, do not fight, this is different from fighting in battle, because we can sacrifice our lives, but we can save someone, but Fighting with Kovid, if there is no way to protect himself, it is clear that the doctor will die and the patient will die.
Some countries with advanced medicine and rich countries still lack masks, lack of protective equipment for doctors and leave doctors infected, and then they write badly about us that Cambodia's health system is weak, Laos' health system is weak, Myanmar is weak. This country is weak, but the country itself is too advanced to find a burial ground and has the right to write to ridicule others.
In connection with the case of doctors in Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also said that in the past they insulted Cambodian doctors, but now, seeing the sacrifices of doctors and front-line fighters against Kovid 19, the feelings of the people began to change. Doctors and Samdech also praised and thanked Cambodian doctors who have fought against Kovid 19 in the past.
In addition, Samdech Techo Prime Minister praised all provinces, which, after issuing the order, set up more than 3,000 rooms for Kovid patients in time, and Samdech stressed that the first wave is gone, but Concerned about the second wave of Kovid 19 outbreak due to specific cases in China and South Korea.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the people who defended themselves from Kovid 19 and also praised the tens of thousands of Cambodian workers from Thailand who did not bring Kovid 19 to Cambodia even in one case. In particular, more than 90 percent of workers have accepted the Royal Government's request without taking time off during the New Year, and only a small number have stopped going to the New Year.
As of 6:00 pm on Monday, June 1, 2020, Kovid 19, designated by the World Health Organization as a "global epidemic", has invaded a total of 213 countries and territories. And all over the world, it has spread to every continent on the planet except Antarctica.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen: If you do not want the traffic police to get a lot of money, all citizens must respect the traffic law (Video inside) (Preah Sihanouk): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, on June 1, 2020 That if people do not want the traffic police to get a lot of money to fine the enforcement of the law on road traffic, then all citizens must respect the traffic law.
This statement was made on the occasion of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's meeting with officials and technical team to build road infrastructure in Sihanoukville, which is the road of the strategic plan to make Sihanoukville a tourist and commercial city. Civilized karma on the afternoon of June 1, 2020.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that some critics criticized the implementation of restricting road traffic and fined soldiers for paying salaries to the police because they did not have the money to pay their salaries. To protect the lives of the people by enforcing the road traffic law, and if you do not want the police to have money, the only way to obey the traffic law.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also continued to call on the people to respect the traffic law to save their own lives and the lives of others under the slogan "Today, tomorrow, do not have a traffic accident."
According to Director General Him Yan, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police for Traffic Planning, within one month of implementing the enforcement of the land traffic law under Sub-Decree No. 39, the traffic police force fined vehicles about 3 Billion riels, which is equivalent to more than 700,000 US dollars.
Director General Him Yan added that in the past month, five traffic police officers have been fired and suspended for violating traffic rules and regulations. This statement in the press conference shows the results of a month of traffic law enforcement on the morning of June 1, 2020.
The signing ceremony took place under the co-chairs of the Project Council, Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, and Ms. Pauline Tamesis, United Nations Resident Coordinator in Cambodia, on June 1, 2020 at the Ministry of Labor.
The total budget for the second phase of the DEY program is $ 8.48 million, of which $ 4 million is provided by the Swiss Agency for Development and Cooperation (SDC) and $ 4.48 million. Funding from the core funds of the participating agencies, from other private sector donors from the Royal Government of Cambodia. The project will run for four years from January 1, 2020 to December 31, 2023.
The program will provide innovative and vulnerable young people with innovative study packages that include technical, entrepreneurial, soft and business skills, as well as career guidance needed to ensure they They can meet the needs of the job market and be ready for quality work.
Ms. Carin Salerno also stated that the Swiss Agency for Development and Cooperation (SDC) is pleased to join and continue to work in partnership with the Royal Government and the United Nations in Cambodia to support young people in Countries, especially those affected by epidemics, to overcome current employment problems and be ready for future job needs after the disaster.
Mr. Sam Heng said that during the outbreak of Kovid-19, the program also supported the government's policy in responding immediately to Kovid-19 and after Kovid-19.
Please be informed that this Phase 2 Youth Employment Approach Program aims to support young women and men in Cambodia so that they can have more productive opportunities by ensuring that they are more able to respond to market needs. Work and be prepared to get quality work. In total, 170,000 young people (50% female) will directly benefit from the Phase II Youth Appropriate Employment Program.
