Samdech Techo Hun Sen called on people not to worry about spending 1 dollar, 2 dollars and 5 dollars, because all banks still accept this type of banknote.
Please be informed that on May 28, 2020, the National Bank of Cambodia held a meeting to discuss the challenges of circulation of US $ 1, $ 2 and $ 5 banknotes in Cambodia with representatives of banking and financial institutions. In managing these types of banknotes.
Considering that both the Banking and Financial Institutions and the National Bank of Cambodia have stockpiled $ 1, $ 2, and $ 5 US dollars, this indicates that demand for these banknotes is low in the assembly market. Agreed to set out some measures as follows:
* The National Bank of Cambodia will provide 3 months from June 1, 2020 to August 31, 2020 to the Banking and Financial Institutions to bring US $ 1, $ 2 and $ 5 banknotes. National Bank of Cambodia to ship abroad free of charge.
* After August 31, 2020, the National Bank of Cambodia will transfer the shipping costs abroad in US $ 1, $ 2 and $ 5 to the Banking and Financial Institutions as insurers. There is no fee for receiving US $ 10 or more.
* The National Bank of Cambodia will continue to consult with banking and financial institutions to reach an appropriate time to suspend the receipt of small US dollars from banking and financial institutions.
The National Bank of Cambodia also stated that the implementation of the above measures does not mean a ban on the circulation of these small denomination banknotes in the market.
