(Banteay Meanchey): Banteay Meanchey Provincial Authority and Sa Kaeo Provincial Authority on the afternoon of June 1, 2020, met at the Cambodia-Thailand Friendship Bridge in Poipet to find a solution after a group of traders, motodup, tricycle riders and Workers pulling carts to protest want to cross the border into Thailand as Thailand announces further border closures to prevent Kovid 19.
The Cambodian side was led by Mr. Ngor Mengchruon, Deputy Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province and Mr. Koeung Vannak, Deputy Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, and was attended by Mr. Bun Nam Eang, Deputy Commander of the Provincial Armed Forces and Brigadier General Mak, Deputy Provincial Police Commissioner for Border Affairs and other relevant institutions. Separately, the Thai side led by Mr. Vara Phan Siphannon, Governor of Sa Kaeo Province and many other relevant authorities.
