In late May 2020, Banteay Meanchey provincial governor Ou Rath issued a letter refusing to allow traders in Rong Klue Market to demonstrate for the opening of the Poipet border crossing for reasons to prevent the spread of Kovid 19.
The refusal was made in response to a request by the president of the Foreign Economic Association, which announced an attempt to gather traders in Rong Klue market, Aranyaprathet district, Sa Kaeo province, Thailand, including cart-pullers, motorbike taxi drivers and taxi drivers. About 1,500 tricycle riders and informal workers are scheduled to demonstrate at the Poipet International Gate from June 1 to 7, 2020.
The demonstration was to demand that Thailand open the border and allow Cambodians to come and go and shop at Rong Klue Market near the Poipet border.
Construction of 34 roads in Sihanoukville has reached 94%
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and senior officials of the Royal Government of Cambodia, including Preah Sihanouk Provincial Authority, on June 1, 2020, inspected the first results of road construction in Sihanoukville. Strategic plan to make Sihanoukville a civilized tourist and commercial city.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen traveled from the Kang Keng International Airport of Sihanoukville to the Ream Sea, passing through many beaches and valleys, and then to Otres Beach, Ochheuteal Beach, the ring road of Sihanoukville and the inner city. Sihanoukville 34 lines, which is now completed about 94%.
The Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to release a budget of about 300 million US dollars to build the 34 roads under construction, which is the first luxury road in Cambodia. These 34 roads were opened by Samdech Techo on November 16, 2019.
The Royal Government has set a plan to develop a land use master plan in Sihanoukville with the vision of 2030: to design and develop Sihanoukville as a sustainable national development pole in the coastal areas of Cambodia through the development of modern cities with coastal resorts. The most beautiful in the world and a multi-purpose special economic zone that will attract more tourists and new investment from abroad and serve a better life for our people.
The construction of this road has really contributed greatly to the realization of the vision of the Royal Government set in the land management plan of Sihanoukville Province Vision 2030 to develop Sihanoukville as a pole for sustainable national development in the coastal area. Cambodia to become a multi-purpose special economic zone, a national growth center and a national logistics center through the development of smart cities and the integration of Cambodia's coastal areas.
