Mr. Srun Pov, President of the Cambodian Breeders' Association, stated that he was interested in the purpose of this workshop, which is a special occasion and a forum for discussion with the General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production. Livestock Breeders and Development Bank to find tips to promote animal husbandry in Cambodia to adequately supply the Cambodian meat market.
He said that while the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries as well as the General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production in restricting and reducing the import of animals, he reminded farmers to be careful. "We forget the disease, but the disease does not forget us," he said.
Mr. Ros Seng Hak, Representative of the Rural Development Bank, mentioned that the special capital for the promotion of agriculture as well as animal husbandry, with this special capital is very favorable and easy to get a loan.
Mr. Tan Phannara, the Royal Government Delegation, talked with the whole workshop about today's workshop, which is a special opportunity for experts and farmers to meet, which is an open forum for people to ask questions directly and experts. What you are struggling to find a suitable solution to promote animal husbandry.
He further mentioned that the reduction of imports of animals, especially pigs and chickens, in line with the recommendation of Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to control the price of animals in the market to be stable, which is the key to boosting livestock. Domestic animals of farmers.
He also shared his experiences with farmers on the prevention of animal diseases, the prevention of illegal pig trade, the promotion of animal husbandry and the attention of Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and Correspondence with the entire workshop.
