(Banteay Meanchey): An old canal, 1,089 meters long and 6 meters wide, to Tuol Prasat Dang Khchas, located in Poi Wat village, Changha commune, Ochrov district, was built as a dirt road with a gift from Mrs. Oknha Hem Chitta, a Buddhist disciple of Mao Malay. Ke Kim Yan was cut the ribbon to be officially inaugurated.
Under her presidency, Ms. Noum Sophoan, Member of Parliament of Banteay Meanchey, Mr. Ou Rathrey, Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, and the leaders of relevant departments and units also participated in the celebration. The ceremony took place on the morning of May 30, 2020.
Mr. Ream Pon, a representative of the people living in Poi Wat village, Changha commune, expressed his happiness with receiving one of the above roads, which before the old road was a canal to travel only in the dry season and when the rainy season is difficult to do Travel by water canal.
He also said that this 1,089-meter road is really important for the people in Poi Wat village as well as Changha commune by:
First, make it easier for farmers as they transport other agricultural products Second: This road can easily reach Tuol Prasat Dang Khchas for the shrine of the people in the village who always believe in various religious ceremonies Especially when there is drought, lack of water, etc., people come to pray, it is as desired.
The people's representative also thanked Mrs. Oknha Hem Chetta, a Buddhist devotee of Mao Malay Ke Kim Yan, for providing this road to the local people to travel easily as well as make it easier to transport various agricultural products and I wish you and General Ke Kim Yan to meet only the four Buddhas: age, class, happiness, and strength.
