Spokesman for the General Commission: In the past 30 days, 43,530 vehicles have been inspected and fined according to the new sub-decree
(Phnom Penh): Within 30 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fines according to Sub-Decree No. 39, ie on May 30-30, 2021, the traffic police nationwide inspected and fined 43,530 vehicles. Of which, 31,755 motorcycles and 11,775 vehicles of all types. This was confirmed by Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun, Deputy Commissioner General and spokesman for the National Police General Commission, to Fresh News.
According to the lieutenant general, for May 30, 2020, there were 14 traffic accidents, killing 4 people and injuring 26 people (16 seriously injured).
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that during the 30 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine the offending vehicles went well.
