(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia has declared its neutrality in its international relations and treated it fairly for all friendly countries.
Despite the Royal Government's policy of international relations, it is seen that in dealing with the economic powers of the United States and China, Cambodia has closer ties with China than the United States. Because of this, some have argued that Cambodia's closeness to China is not as profitable as its relationship with the United States.
In the discussion on the geopolitical confrontation between China and the United States, organized by the Royal Academy of Cambodia on May 29, 2020, a group of experts on history and geopolitics also responded to this view.
Historians and geopolitical experts see that the Royal Government of Cambodia is not inclined to any country, but that Cambodia must also see its economic benefits. This means that any country that benefits Cambodia, Cambodia also provides good relations with the same friendly countries.
A panel of experts, including Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, Dr. Kin Phea, President of the Institute of International Relations of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, Mr. Puy Kea, Correspondent for Kyodo News Agency, and Dr. Diep Sophal, Professor of History and International Relations, saw China Has provided a lot of benefits for the economy in Cambodia just made the relationship between Cambodia and China.
These experts also said that if the United States wants to have good relations with Cambodia, it must also reconsider its relations with Cambodia. Experts say good relations, not just democracy, human rights, and economic politics.
According to data from the Council for the Development of Cambodia (CDC), investment between China and the United States in Cambodia varies widely, with China at the top for investment in Cambodia.
The report shows that from 1994 to January 2019, Chinese investment in Cambodia amounted to 23 billion US dollars. US investment in Cambodia is just over $ 936 million.
