Mr. Pan Sosak: The Royal Government will revive Khmer silk
(Siem Reap): Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, affirmed that the Royal Government of Cambodia will revitalize the Cambodian silk industry and aim to make her child-raising silk modern, modern and sustainable. Also.
The Minister added that in order to promote and develop the Cambodian silk sector, the project to promote the market for small-scale agriculture is the first starting point of the partnership between the private and public sectors to the leading silk business in developing contract farming projects. To produce raw silk for their operations.
These private-public partnerships also provide for the supply of better quality nestlings and promote quality tree planting through private cultivation. Through these activities, the project is expected to increase the profits of small-scale raw silk production and supply of raw silk for weaving and designing into finished silk products.
It should be noted that the Market Promotion Project for Small-Scale Agriculture is a joint project of the Royal Government of Cambodia and the International Fund for Agricultural Development (IFAD). The project is led by the Ministry of Commerce and aims to promote the prosperity of Cambodia's smallholder farmers by increasing profits by linking agro-trade and markets.
Police crack down on suspects and confiscate nearly half a kilo of drugs in Meanchey district
(Phnom Penh): Meanchey district police cracked down on a suspect and confiscated nearly half a kilo of drugs on the morning of May 30, 2020 at a house with no street number in Prek Ta Kong 2 village, Chak Angre Leu commune, Meanchey district.
Mr. Ou Ratana, Chief of Chak Angre Leu Police Station, Meanchey District, said that at 1:30 AM on May 30, 2020, the police patrolling the area to prevent local crimes later found the suspect woman. Pheng Sok Khy, Female, 24 years old, Nationality Khmer, Occupation: House cleaner, Living in a rented house, Phum Prek Ta Kong 3, Sangkat Chak Angre Leu, Khan Meanchey and a trafficker.
After the arrest, the police found three large packages of drugs in the suspect's hand and brought her to the police station for questioning.
Police said that on the same day, Mr. Meng Vimean Dara, Meanchey District Police Inspector, led a search of the suspect's house in cooperation with the village chief and the commune chief, confiscating some exhibits.
