(Phnom Penh): General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, on May 30, 2020, shared his condolences to the Cambodian Blue Hat Army who died in Mali due to the 19-year-old disease.
A Cambodian Blue Hat soldier, General Tos Savy, died of Kovid 19 while on a UN humanitarian mission in Mali on May 29, 2020.
General Vong Pisen considered the loss of the lives of Cambodian fighters abroad as a great and priceless sacrifice for the motherland, especially humanitarian work under the United Nations umbrella.
