The US government of President Donald Trump on May 27 removed Hong Kong's "special status" from its list. The ruling means Hong Kong will no longer receive special treatment under US law, as it could lose its privilege of doing business with the United States, the world's largest economy.
The removal comes after the United States accused Beijing of trampling on the World Financial Center's autonomy after Beijing stepped up its passage of a new national security law to apply to Hong Kong. The Donald Trump administration sees this as an assassination of Hong Kong's freedoms.
Delegation of the Ministry of Planning Visits and Distributes Donations to the National Police Force Standing on the Cambodian-Thai Border in Samlot District, Battambang Province
(Battambang): A delegation of the Ministry of Planning led by Mr. Hou Taing Eng, Secretary of State, on behalf of the Honorary Minister Dr. Chhay Thorn, Minister of Planning, on May 30, 2020, visited and distributed gifts to the National Police Force. The 310th and 823rd Battalions are defending the Cambodian-Thai border in Samlot District, Battambang Province.
During the meeting, the Secretary of State delivered a message from Mr. Kittisetha Bandit, Senior Minister, Minister of Planning, to all the standing forces. On behalf of the Honorary Senior Minister, Mr. Hu Taing Eng also briefed on the current situation both in the country and around the world.
The delegation brought gifts such as sausages, noodles and some money, which is a precious gift from the leadership of the entire Ministry of Planning to our forces for use in the time of the impact of the epidemic. Global Kovid-19 disease.
Secretary of State Hou Taing Eng also expressed his deep gratitude and wished all the members of the Armed Forces and their families good health and join the Royal Government in safeguarding peace, prosperity and development. People and our society as a whole. UNDP Condemns Death of Cambodian Blue Hat Soldiers in Mali 19
It should be noted that General Tos Savy, who went on a humanitarian mission under the auspices of the United Nations, died at a hospital in Mali on May 29, 2020, after contracting Kovid 19.
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, expressed his deep sorrow over Sar Savy's death. Samdech Picheay Sena considered the loss of the lives of Cambodian fighters abroad as a huge and invaluable sacrifice for the motherland, especially humanitarian work under the United Nations umbrella.
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh also confirmed that the Cambodian side has worked closely with the United Nations to prepare the bodies of Cambodian fighters for humanitarian causes.
Recently, seven Cambodian Blue Hat military personnel serving in Mali contracted 19 cases of Kovid. Of those, one died, two were cured and four were being treated.
Lt. Gen. Phal Samorn, spokesman for the National Center for the Management of Peacekeeping Forces, Demining and Remnants of War, said that Cambodia currently has 298 troops working in Mali, including 30 women.
Lt. Gen. Phal Samorn said that there are currently 1,194 cases of 19 Kovid cases in Mali, including 73 UN officials, including seven Cambodians.
