Minister Chea Vandeth Introduces Revision and Preparation of "One-Stop-Shop" Regulations to Accelerate Public Service Delivery
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chea Vandeth, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications, recommended the revision and preparation of additional regulations and the establishment of a "one-stop shop" to speed up the provision of public services faster, more transparent, more efficient and more beneficial. To users of services in the field of post and telecommunications.
This introduction was made in a monthly meeting with the participation of relevant leaders under the Ministry at the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications on the afternoon of May 28, 2020. The meeting focused on the presentation of work, reform, revision of work procedures, the establishment of working groups, the preparation of key policies that have been set in the past and other issues.
During the meeting, the Minister informed the meeting about the reform of the Ministry's internal administrative procedures and procedures for generating revenue collection, especially the share of revenue in accordance with the Telecommunications Law.
A number of working groups have been set up to address urgent needs, such as draft government policies, digitalization, ministry digitalization, frequency management and distribution, and e-learning.
