Natural disasters! Rain mixed with gusts of wind caused the roofs of 4 houses to open and lightning killed a total of 5 cattle in Kampong Chhnang province
(Kampong Chhnang): Four houses had their roofs blown off and a chicken farm collapsed, while two cows and three buffaloes were struck by lightning and died in natural disasters caused by rain and strong winds.
This incident happened on the evening of May 28, 2020 in three districts in Kampong Chhnang province, including: Boriboun district, Kampong Tralach district and Kampong Leng district.
* In Boribo district: strong wind and rain caused the collapse of 1 house in Trapeang Po village, Khon Rong commune * Meters in Sre Prey village, Or Russey commune * Two cows of villagers in Chambok Khpos village, Svay Rumpear commune, Kampong Leng district were killed by lightning while eating grass in the rain.
The information we received from the authorities on the afternoon of May 29, 2020 said that at 2:30 pm on May 29, 2020, there was rain and wind, including thunder. Meanwhile, three buffaloes belonging to the people tied under a tree at Potanon point in Taor Rolum village, Kampong Hav commune, Kampong Leng district were also killed by lightning.
The above-mentioned natural disasters occurred in all three districts in Kampong Chhnang province on the evening of May 28, 2020 on the same day.
(Kampong Cham): Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham Province and Chairman of the Provincial Branch Committee, this morning, May 30, 2020, led a working group to bring humanitarian donations from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross. Presented to 61 elderly people, widows and families from 8 communes in Chamkar Leu district, Kampong Cham province.
On that occasion, Mr. Un Chanda said that the Cambodian Red Cross, led by Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, is a national association that always thinks about the well-being of people everywhere, especially vulnerable victims. Regardless of race, ethnicity or political affiliation, in line with the slogan "Where there is suffering, there is the Cambodian Red Cross."
At the same time, Mr. Un Chanda also urged the district sub-branch, as well as the working group of the Red Cross, commune and all volunteers to continue to conduct educational campaigns, disseminate and raise awareness about the transmission of this deadly disease 19 to the people. In its locality on a regular basis as Cambodia finds one more new case while one patient recovers.
The Branch Committee Chairman also reminded that if you have any doubts about anyone or yourself, please call 115 toll free.
Minister of Agriculture Visits Kampong Cham Province to Examine Farming, Development and Key Challenges of Agricultural Communities
Due to the high demand for seeds in 2020, the General Department of Agriculture has prepared a plan to plant 150 more hectares and so far 50 hectares have been planted.
Talking with farm leaders, officials, staff, farm workers, Minister Veng Sakhon encouraged and appreciated the sense of responsibility to manage the farm and take care of farmland owned by the state.
Regarding technical work, Mr. Veng Sakhon requested that farm officials pay attention to increase technical knowledge related to the breeding and selection of all types of highland crops in order to disseminate crop varieties and special techniques to farmers throughout the region. With the name of the farm and especially in line with the development of modern agricultural technology that reduces labor, time, production efficiency and high economy.
In the morning of the same day, Minister Veng Sakhon continued his visit to Sopheas commune, Stung Trang district to inspect the cultivation work, development and important challenges of the Sambo Meanchey farming community.
During the meeting, Mr. Theng Thong, Community President, reported to the Minister that the community was established in 2010 with the aim of strengthening the authority to negotiate agricultural prices with traders and companies, solve problems and protect the interests of members in order to increase income. Families through agricultural products. At present, the community has a total of 659 families (379 women) with a total capital of 1,666,444,500 riels, about more than $ 416,000.
As for the business of agricultural products, community marketing and contract farming, the Minister supported the community to expand to seize the opportunity, in line with the words of the Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen, in order to turn the community into a medium and large enterprise. The future absorbs the local workforce, especially students who have graduated from the country.
The Cambodian Veterans Association holds its general assembly every five years to adjust the composition of the leadership, members of the Central Committee, as well as the Standing Committee. But in 2020, due to the spread of Kovid 19, the association will not be able to hold its general assembly like every year.
Despite the absence of the General Assembly, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, as the Association's top leader, has decided to assign General Kun Kim, Senior Minister in charge of the Special Mission, as the Vice President and Secretary General of the Association to lead the implementation. On the work of the association for the new mandate.
In addition to the decision to appoint Senior Minister Kun Kim as Vice President and Secretary General of the Association, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also decided to recognize the composition of the association's 38 additional leaders to increase efficiency and accountability. Timely on issues arising for Cambodian veterans.
The composition of the association's leadership that Samdech Techo Hun Sen decided to recognize includes: 3 vice presidents, 7 deputy secretaries, 17 members of the Central Committee and 11 members of the Standing Committee.
The three Vice-Chairmen are: Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, Minister of Economy and Finance, Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, and Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation.
The Royal Government has decided to provide social land and housing and have a monthly salary for them and their families. Senior Minister Kun Kim, Secretary General of the Association, was seen to be very active and visited the veterans' residences to inspect and study directly to put in place mechanisms to ensure livelihood improvement and solve all problems. Of Veterans.
Senior Minister Kun Kim, as Samdech Techo's talented staff, has worked tirelessly to promote the work of veterans.
