(Phnom Penh): During the 29 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fines according to Sub-Decree No. 39, that is, on May 1-29, 2021, the traffic police nationwide inspected and fined 42,376 vehicles in That 30920 motorcycles and 11456 all kinds of cars. This was confirmed by Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun, Deputy Commissioner General and spokesman for the National Police General Commission, to Fresh News.
According to the lieutenant general, for May 29, 2020, there were 8 traffic accidents, killing 5 people and injuring 18 people (11 seriously injured).
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that during the 29 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine the offending vehicles went well.
On May 29, 2020, a group of Chinese geopolitical experts and observers of the political situation in Cambodia claimed that mainland China is still trying to embrace Hong Kong territory and Hong Kong itself will not. Can shake hands from the rule of mainland China.
Dr. Sok Touch said that the reason for the almost exploding heat between the two powers is because Donald Trump is competing for popularity in this election with Joe Biden.
Dr. Kin Phea, President of the Cambodian Institute of International Relations of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that the Hong Kong issue is one of the US strategies to keep the Chinese government busy and weak if Hong Kong continues to struggle because of the protests. Hong Kong could lose its status as a financial center in Asia, which is the lifeblood of China's economy and the weakening of its economy.
In particular, Dr. Diep Sophal, a professor and historian, said that "Hong Kong is a sovereign territory of China, so the Chinese government has enough rights to maintain stability in its territory, but what can be seen is the opposition. "And the effectiveness of Beijing's problem-solving, I would believe that China will use all means to solve the problem in Hong Kong, because China can not lose Hong Kong territory."
He said the Chinese government is now capable of resolving the crisis in Hong Kong and the United States is reluctant to intervene in China's sovereignty.
