More than 400 Families in Anlong Chrey Commune, Stung Treng Province Apply for Legal Occupation of Farmland
(Stung Treng): Residents in Anlong Chrey commune, Thala Borivat district, Stung Treng province, have applied to the authorities for legal possession of farmland and plantations after they have lived and enjoyed the land for many years.
On May 29, 2020, Mr. Youk Mao, Chief of Anlong Chrey Village, said that 412 families want 4656 hectares of farmland and plantation land for their children to own in Anlong Chrey Commune. They do not want to see migrants own land legally, while those who live locally have no land to enjoy.
They still hope for the leadership of the head of the Royal Government, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, by giving them the right to legally occupy their farmland in Anlong Chrey commune, Thala Parivat district, Stung Treng province.
