The Cambodian Embassy in Malaysia informs Cambodians wishing to travel to Malaysia about the requirements of the Malaysian Government (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Embassy in Malaysia on May 29, 2020 Inform the Cambodian people who wish to travel to Malaysia about some of the requirements set by the Malaysian government.
The announcement from the Cambodian Embassy in Malaysia, obtained by Fresh News today, states that from June 1, 2020, the Malaysian Government will implement the following procedures:
1: Ask for permission to enter Malaysia in advance from the Malaysian Embassy in each country at least 3 days before departure.
2: Present the above letter of approval to the airline or public transport company and Malaysian immigration officials.
3. Upon arrival at Malaysia's international entrance, all passengers will be subject to immigration and health checks for Kovid 19.
In case of 19 cases of Kovid, the passenger will be sent to a hospital organized by the Malaysian government. Organized by the Malaysian government at a fixed rate set by the Malaysian government with the hotel (from RM150 / day).
