Rohingya refugee woman recounts two months of life at sea without expecting to return to Bangladesh (Video inside): A Rohingya Muslim woman recounts a tragic story about Attempted to cross the border into Malaysia but eventually returned to a refugee camp in Bangladesh after wandering on a boat in the middle of the sea for about two months with hundreds of other Rohingya refugees.
In February 2020, Khadiza decided to sell her jewelry for $ 750 so that smugglers could prepare a boat for them to leave Bangladesh for Malaysia. According to her, traveling on the boat was very difficult as it was overcrowded and lacked water and sanitation. But days later, there were the first deaths on the boat, and that did not end there.
After a seven-day journey through storms and rain, the Rohingya refugees finally see the coast of Malaysia for the first time. At that point, they also waited for small boats to bring them to the mainland, but no boat came because the Malaysian Coast Guard tightened security in the face of the COVID-19 outbreak.
