(Phnom Penh): Wing Specialized Bank (Cambodia) Limited and Rural Development and Agriculture Bank have partnered to provide easy access to financial services for small and medium enterprises and agribusiness in Cambodia.
Kao Thach, Director General of the Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture, said: “This partnership is a testament to our commitment to supporting small and medium enterprises and agribusiness in Cambodia to provide access to financial services. Convenient stuff. "Even now, even if you are in a remote province, you can still get support from us through Wing's financial system."
The Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture was established in 1998 to fill the gap between demand and supply of financial services in rural areas and to contribute to reducing poverty in Cambodia. The Bank's operations are under the technical and financial guardianship of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and under the supervision of the National Bank of Cambodia.
Manura Chan, CEO of Wing Specialized Bank, said: “We are confident that our partnership will allow us to provide diversified remittance and loan repayment services to small and medium enterprises and agribusiness in Cambodia. Safe, secure and fast. It will help them focus more on expanding their business operations and contribute to Cambodia's economic growth. ”
Cambodia is a country with more than 500,000 small and medium enterprises that contribute to economic growth by creating jobs, generating income for low-income people, promoting social stability and the growth of the private sector. Strong.
Both Wing Specialized Bank and Rural Development and Agriculture Bank share a vision of facilitating access to financial services to communities that improve the lives of Cambodians. Wing has established its brand as a bank that provides secure, secure and fast money transfer services through the state-of-the-art Wing smartphone app and a network of professional Wing agents across the country.
The Rural Development Bank and Agriculture is recognized for its commitment to contribute to poverty reduction and improving the livelihoods of rural Cambodians through the provision of financial assistance to small and medium enterprises and organizations. Agriculture to contribute to Cambodia's economic growth.
