Please be informed that on the afternoon of May 28, 2020, the National Bank of Cambodia issued an official statement clarifying that the US $ 1, $ 2 and $ 5 notes are still available as usual in the market without any restrictions. However, in the future, the National Bank of Cambodia will only suspend the acceptance of these US dollars from banking and financial institutions.
The confirmation of the National Bank of Cambodia was made during a meeting with representatives of banking and financial institutions on the challenges of circulation of US $ 1, $ 2 and $ 5 banknotes and the consequences of banking and financial institutions and the National Bank of Cambodia. In managing these types of banknotes.
According to the press release, in the warehouses of banking and financial institutions and the National Bank of Cambodia, there is a flood of US $ 1, $ 2 and $ 5 banknotes, which indicates that the demand for these banknotes Low level in the market The meeting agreed to set out some measures as follows:
* The National Bank of Cambodia will provide 3 months from June 1, 2020 to August 31, 2020 to the Banking and Financial Institutions to bring US $ 1, $ 2 and $ 5 banknotes. National Bank of Cambodia for free overseas shipping
* After August 31, 2020, the National Bank of Cambodia will transfer the shipping costs abroad in US $ 1, $ 2 and $ 5 to the Banking and Financial Institutions as insurers. There is no fee for receiving US $ 10 or more.
It should be noted that the discussion in the above meeting was also attended by representatives from some retail sectors. The National Bank of Cambodia would also like to emphasize that the implementation of the above measures does not imply a ban on the circulation of these small denomination banknotes in the market.
The President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia said this on Friday, May 29, 2020 at a roundtable discussion on "geopolitical confrontation between China and the United States."
Dr. Sok Touch said that although Cambodia has always declared that it adheres to the policy of non-alignment, but the interests are one thing that plays a very important role. He recalled that during the recent 19 cases of Kovid, the United States and Japan provided funding to Cambodia to prevent the disease, but China was the first to do so.
Dr. Sok Touch reminded not to worry about the Chinese presence in Cambodia, because China has just entered Cambodia for a short time, but has changed the face of this country through investment and rapid development. In comparison, China's presence has developed Cambodia faster than the United States and France, which have been in Cambodia for a long time.
He stressed that "do not worry about the presence of China in Cambodia, because the United States came to Cambodia in 1975 turned into a two-story Tuol Kork villa, France came to Cambodia turned into a house in Cambodia only 7 floors, such as Monorom and Phsar Thmei China came to Cambodia in just 2 years, it changed very fast. "So if you want to influence Cambodia, invest, invest, not just put democracy, not just draw it for people to follow."
It should be noted that from 1994 to January 2019, Chinese investment in Cambodia amounted to 23 billion US dollars, while US investment in Cambodia from 1994 to 2019 was just over 936 million US dollars. This is according to data recorded by the Council for the Development of Cambodia (CDC).
