More than 11 tons of frozen shrimp filled with jelly were cracked down by professional officers in Kambol and Dangkor districts
(Phnom Penh): With the attention of the leadership of the Ministry of Commerce and under the direct command of Mr. Phan Oun, Director General of the General Department of Consumer Protection, Competition and Anti-Fraud (CPC) in At 1:30 am on May 29, 2020, an operation was launched to crack down on the import of frozen shrimp with jelly added to increase weight, causing harm to consumers and possibly affecting health.
In this operation, the General Department of PPR requested the cooperation of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police with the approval of the Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court to intercept three seafood trucks.
One vehicle was intercepted along National Road 4 in Kambol district and two vehicles were intercepted along National Road 3 in Dangkor district. Immediately, the professional officers of the General Department of PPR conducted a preliminary test on the frozen shrimp contained in the three vehicles above and found that there was a real jelly addition.
According to preliminary claims from the drivers of the three trucks, the seafood goods included: 449 cases of frozen shrimp, crab and squid, about 11 tons, sourced through the Prek Chak International Gate and undocumented. Comes with no.
Please also note that with the approval of the Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, the vehicle and the exhibits were sent to the General Department of KPD. To proceed with legal proceedings.
According to the General Department of KPR Will continue to research, investigate and perform the duties assigned by law in relation to the quality, safety of goods and services and consumer protection to protect the health and interests of consumers and call on people to cooperate in providing information in case of relevant suspicion. Counterfeiting the quality, safety of goods and services. The Governor of Kampong Cham encourages police officers to continue to deal with congested cases.
