This morning, the Royal Academy of Cambodia held a discussion on "Geopolitical confrontation between China and the United States."
(Phnom Penh): On Friday, May 29, 2020, the Royal Academy of Cambodia will hold a roundtable discussion on "Geopolitical Confrontation between China and the United States."
This morning's roundtable was attended by speakers from historians and journalists experimenting with China-US geopolitics. Speakers at the forum included: Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, Mr. Diep Sophal, Professor and Historian, and Mr. Puy Kea, a journalist with extensive experience in geopolitics between China and the United States.
The rivalry between China and the United States in Asia, Southeast Asia, as well as in Indochina is not new. China and the United States have been vying for influence in the region for decades. Their rivalry for influence has put countries in the region, including Cambodia, in serious crisis. The rivalry between China and the United States from the 1960s to the 1980s left Cambodia in the throes of a devastating crisis.
The renewed rivalry between China and the United States In the 21st century, Cambodia, an Indochina country, has suffered because it is seen as a platform for rivalries between China and the United States.
Mr. Sok Touch claimed that tomorrow's forum is a message to warn Cambodian politicians and young people to prepare their qualifications so that they do not become meat that has been cut like in the past. In particular, find ways to escape the competition that can easily lead to danger for Cambodia.
