The Director General of the Rural Development Bank urges farmers to raise fish, raise animals and grow vegetables in a clear plan to supply market demand and reduce imports from neighboring countries
(Kampong Cham): Mr. Kao Thach, Director General of the Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture, on May 28, requested farmers, fish farmers, animal husbandry, vegetable growers to prepare a clear planting plan to supply in the market. Demand and sustainability to help reduce imports from neighboring countries.
Mr. Kao Thach's request was made on the occasion that he continued to disseminate the loan policy and loan conditions under the special government financing program of US $ 50 million to the community, animal husbandry, fish farming, vegetable and fruit growing and handicraft groups. Small and medium enterprises in the field of agricultural products, agro-industry and agriculture in Kampong Cham province, a total of more than 200 people.
The event was also presided over by Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham, Mr. Khlot Phorn, Chairman of the Provincial Council, Mr. Hav Viseth, Deputy Director General of Fisheries Administration, Representative of the General Department of Agriculture of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Director General of Animal Health and Veterinary Production and Deputy Governors, District Governors and specialized departments around the province.
The Director General said that the loan under the Royal Government's special financing program of 50 million US dollars was established to be able to expand the business and improve the production chain in order to create more jobs, strengthen competitiveness and expand the base. Domestic production to boost both exports and reduce imports at a time when the Cambodian economy is facing a number of challenges, including COVID-19 and EBA.
On that occasion, Mr. Kao Thach also disseminated the decision of the Royal Government of Cambodia under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia decided to adjust the special financing program $ 50 million through the Rural Development and Agriculture Bank by expanding Scope of coverage and adjustment of credit terms, such as:
* Adjust the maximum loan term from 5 years to 7 years for working capital while keeping the maximum loan term for 2 years for working capital.
* Provides flexibility on registration conditions, in which small and medium-sized enterprises that have not yet been officially registered can apply for a loan by completing the registration conditions one month after receiving the loan.
Europe vows to continue unwavering cooperation and help develop Cambodia's tourism after Kovid crisis
(Phnom Penh): The European Union (EU) has continued to support the development of Cambodia's tourism sector as the Kovid 19 crisis disappears from the world, especially the development of ecotourism and human resources in the tourism sector, with a commitment to strengthen cooperation with the Royal Government. The government as well as the Ministry of Tourism of Cambodia.
On that occasion, Minister Thong Khon mentioned the current state of tourism in Cambodia, which is being severely affected by the Kovid 19 crisis, causing some people who used to work in the service sector to lose their jobs. Recently, Cambodia has also received some domestic tourists, with nearly 400,000 domestic tourists visiting the country in the first three weeks of May.
In this regard, Cambodia has put in place a number of measures, including planning to recruit unemployed people from the tourism sector to receive additional tourism skills training to be ready to return to work when tourists return. That is why Minister Thong Khon called on the European Union to support this important work, especially digital teaching or e-learning.
The Minister also requested the European Union to support and provide special cooperation, share experiences on the preparation of measures to address the disease and the restoration of tourism in the New Normal life in Cambodia, as well as in The entire ASEAN region.
In addition, the Minister requested the European Union, which has experience in the design of smart cities (Smart City) to continue to support Cambodia, as this is also considered an important tourism product and at the same time. Cambodia is preparing to host the "ASEAN Tourism Forum 2021 and the ASEAN Tourism Ministers' Meeting" and preparations to host the 2023 SEA Games.
These proposals were warmly welcomed by Ambassador Cameron Marino and pledged to continue closer cooperation with the Royal Government of Cambodia, especially in the field of tourism with the Ministry of Tourism.
Ms. Khamin also praised Cambodia's efforts to develop sustainable and responsible tourism. That is why the European Union continues to support the development of this sector and hopes that cooperation will improve after the Kovid crisis.
The European Ambassador also pledged to bring information related to tourist destinations in Cambodia, as well as the readiness of the Cambodian people to receive tourists from Europe, especially the humanitarian reputation is not dry, which also Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. For example, Cambodians have helped bring international visitors aboard the Westerdam to the European tourism market.
