The call by the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia was made in congratulatory messages on the 71st anniversary of International Children's Day, June 1, the 19th anniversary of the World Day Against Child Labor, June 12 and Cambodian Children's Day 2020.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his full congratulations for the celebration of this important day. The celebration of this significant day shows the strong will and commitment of the Royal Government to continue to promote the implementation of children's rights and encourage our compatriots to continue to improve the welfare of children for the better. The benefits of children in Cambodia.
In the spirit of contributing to the 71st Anniversary of International Children's Day, June 1, the 19th Anniversary of the World Day Against Child Labor, June 12 and Cambodian Children's Day 2020, at the time of the 19 outbreak of Kovid, Key points such as:
1: Relevant ministries and institutions must continue to strictly implement the guidelines of the Ministry of Health to prevent the spread of the disease to all children everywhere, especially children with disabilities, children living in poor families, children living in foster care and children Live in all detention centers.
2: All ministries and institutions must strive to ensure that all children everywhere, especially children living in poor families, have equal access to education, hygiene and clean water during the Kovid epidemic. 19 This.
3. All measures taken by the relevant ministries and institutions to prevent Kovid 19 must take into account the best interests of all children, especially children living in foster care and children living in detention. Emphasis on the mental and official health support of children directly or indirectly affected by Kovid 19 and allowed to participate in decisions that affect children.
4: Ministries, institutions, local authorities, communities and all citizens must continue to participate in the implementation of the policy of safe villages, communes, especially measures to protect children from all forms of violence, educate children on how to protect themselves against all forms of sexual abuse and harassment. All forms of intimidation to stay away from drugs and to make children understand how to report abuse to authorities or adults in all its forms.
5. Ministries and institutions must continue to implement the core signs of the International Labor Organization to eliminate all forms of child labor, raise awareness, train and disseminate the use of child labor in all economic activities, and strengthen child labor inspection measures, as well as mobilize resources and public movements. Finding appropriate solutions to save child labor. Instant 10% discount from Safe Home Technology on the latest 2020 GPS series
