(Stung Treng): Stung Treng Provincial Authority on May 28, 2020, prepared to replace the old sewer system with new one to facilitate the living of the people along the house along Street 54 with a length of 700 meters to release sewage and congestion in The rainy season, which was previously flooded due to the small drainage system not yet flowing.
Vendors in Thmor Lat village, Orussey commune, Stung Treng city, near this road, confirmed that along this road, the authorities have prepared a small drain and the water is shallow and no longer flows when there is a heavy rain, flooding time. Roads and entrances are also available.
She said that this problem, whether when it rains more or less, always affects the lives of people, such as traffic to and fro, and some traders have to miss during the rain.
Mr. Phou Say, a resident of Street 54, acknowledged that the new sewer system could be more effective because it would release all the dirty water to help eradicate mosquitoes and keep the city clean. More than before.
He added that the new drainage system, when done, both sides of our living space is clean, no mosquito nests, children are comfortable, do not worry about mosquito bites.
Mr. Van Mony, the contractor for the construction of the drainage system, acknowledged that the drainage system was really congested because the system was small in the past and was affected by the flooding of the Mekong River for many years and lacked the maintenance of Residents also cause the canal to be congested during the rainy season.
He confirmed that with this new arrangement, the provincial authorities will install a large-scale sewer system with a diameter of 1 meter instead so that there will be no chronic waterlogging as before, and this time, the people are requested to help clean up the environment and not dump garbage. Maintain roads and sewers when completed.
