The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and the ACE School provide 2,000 scholarships to 12th grade students who are preparing for the 2020 high school diploma exam.
The e-Learning English Scholarship is part of ACE Social Work to support the Royal Government of Cambodia's efforts to continue to provide education to students across the country through distance learning e-learning programs. Prevention of Kovid 19 infection.
The school has six branches in Cambodia and 25,000 students. ACE has shifted its approach from classroom instruction to distance-based e-learning with live teachers using state-of-the-art technology.
Mr. Mao Sreng said that "distance English e-learning scholarships will help strengthen the English language skills and the opportunity to get better results in English subjects in the upcoming high school diploma exam."
The 2,000 scholarship recipients will start their courses from the end of June until September 2020.
