(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ouch Phea, Governor of Takeo Province, confirmed to Fresh News on May 28, 2020 that since the measures to restrict entry and exit through the border to prevent the spread of Kovid 19, the Vietnamese side has set up a tent. 83 military bases on the border of Takeo province in the territory of the Vietnamese side, located 30 meters from the border post.
According to the governor of Takeo province, so far the provincial authorities bordering the two countries have been monitoring this issue and the Cambodian side has been monitoring to prevent the Vietnamese side from moving any tents into Cambodian territory.
In this case, the governor of Takeo province confirmed that the Vietnamese military camp at this point is in Vietnamese territory, not into Cambodian territory, and the border at this point has already been agreed. The main goal of the Vietnamese military camp at this point is to prevent illegal immigration.
It should be noted that for the time being, measures to restrict border crossings to prevent the spread of Kovid 19, the Vietnamese side has also set up 31 military tents along the border of Leuk Dek district in Koh Thom district, Kandal province. Consensus on the border line yet.
However, after the request from the Cambodian side until May 28, 2020, Vietnam has dismantled nine locations.
