A project on the challenges of Cambodian society has been selected to receive financial assistance from the International Fund for Combating COVID-19
(Phnom Penh): On May 26, 2020, with the participation of nearly 2,000 projects proposed by 79 countries, one project on the challenges of Cambodia's society was selected to receive financial assistance. From the International Fund for Combating COVID-19.
This project is led by a group of professors, students and young researchers from the University of Battambang (Cambodia) with an international organization as a partner. The project studies the current situation of smallholder farmers in the provinces along the borders of the Kingdom of Cambodia and identifies solutions and means in and after the Kovith outbreak.
