The request and request of Senior Minister Kun Kim was made during a visit to inspect the cultivation of 310 families of veterans in Kon Khleng village, Poi Char commune, Phnom Srok district, Banteay Meanchey province on May 27, 2020. This.
Cambodian Veterans receive the highest attention from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, in return for their sacrifices and sacrifices for the nation. The Royal Government has provided social land to build houses for veterans so that they can build a decent living.
The 310 families of veterans living and enjoying the social land provided by the Royal Government of Cambodia have done their best to grow crops and raise livestock to support their livelihoods. Through hard work and diligence, the veterans, despite their disabilities, have helped to improve their lives to another level.
Mr. Kun Kim, Secretary General of the Veterans Association and an important figure of Samdech Techo on the work of veterans, has always been active in solving and responding to the problems of veterans. Seeing firsthand the diligent efforts of cultivating and raising animals to build the lives of veterans, Mr. Kun Kim was amazed and highly appreciated by the diligence of veterans.
"I really enjoy seeing you work so hard to grow and raise animals to make a living like this. Even though you are disabled because of the war, you are not completely dependent on the Royal Government. I sincerely appreciate your efforts. ” This is Senior Minister Kun Kim's statement to the veterans.
During the meeting, the Senior Minister also advised all veterans to pay high attention to health and to follow the hygiene rules of the Ministry of Health to prevent themselves from Kovid 19.
In front of the Senior Minister, the veterans expressed their deep gratitude to Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, who have always taken great care of their lives and livelihoods. Veterans also thanked Senior Minister Kun Kim, who has always been on a regular basis to understand the plight of veterans and submit to Samdech Techo to find a solution for them.
