Kampong Thom Province is located in the center of Cambodia, 168 km from Phnom Penh, bordering Preah Vihear, Stung Treng, Kratie, Kampong Cham, Kampong Chhnang, Pursat and Siem Reap. Equivalent to 804,409 people, 407,989 females, population density 53 people / km2.
Water Resources and Meteorology: The province has 261 irrigation systems (restored, renovated and built 67 new places) that can irrigate agricultural land: 133,169 hectares of wet rice, equivalent to 62%, 25,096 hectares of dry rice. Equal to 63%. The main water sources are: Stung Sen flows through Kampong Thom province for 265 km, Stung Stong for 153 km, Stung Tang Krasang for 103 km and Stung Chinit for 293 km.
Tourism: Kampong Thom province has 6 main tourist resorts, cultural and historical sites, Sambor Prei Kuk temple, historical cultural resorts, Kuk Nokor temple, Phnom Santuk natural cultural resort, Stung Prey Pros natural resort, Boeung Samreth processing resort and Stung Chinit processing resort.
Power Sector: The province has one substation which EDC has commissioned in the first phase of the 115KV transmission line from Preah Vihear province with 22MW power and from Kampong Cham province with 4MW. There are 21 power generation and distribution stations throughout the province, of which 19 are already connected to the national grid and 2 are diesel-powered.
Health Sector: Throughout the province, there are 54 health centers, 4 health posts, 3 referral hospitals, a total of 411 beds. Private services include: 3 clinics, 134 clinics, 12 dental clinics, 1 ophthalmology room, 235 nursing rooms, 88 maternity wards, 59 pharmacies, 4 sub-pharmacies, 9 sub-pharmacies and 1 traditional medicine.
