The Secretary of State added that the Smallholder Market Promotion Project is a joint project of the Royal Government of Cambodia and the International Fund for Agricultural Development (IFAD) and is led by the Ministry of Commerce and aims to promote the prosperity of smallholder farmers in Cambodia. Increase profitability by connecting agribusiness and marketing.
The project operates in 18 provinces and intervenes in five commercial value chains, such as vegetables, chicken, rice, cassava and raw silk. Cultivate financial and business planning, irrigation, credit and marketing.
