(Pursat): On May 26, 2020, from 9:00 am to 2:30 pm, Mr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Pursat Province, continued to solve challenges as well as requests to parents and people. More than 100 different cases, most of which were resolved, and some of which were later resolved.
Addressing the challenges as well as suggestions to the people now made as usual 2 days a week, every Tuesday and Friday or Thursday at the Provincial Hall Forum with the participation of Pursat MPs, members Provincial Council, Ladies and Gentlemen, Deputy Governors, Departments, Offices under the Provincial Hall and a large number of people.
Mr. Kim Chantha, Director of Pursat Provincial People's Office, stated that Mr. Mao Thunin's extra-judicial settlement was always in line with the win-win policy of the Prime Minister of the Royal Government of Cambodia, which always gave results to all parties. Win together without losing.
The director of the People's Office said that in the mechanism of the provincial leadership for more than 6 years, the provincial governor has focused on justice and impartiality, because the people who come to rely on and help solve is like a father, mother, brother. Brothers in the same family, without making them resentful of him.
Mr. Kim Chantha added that for May 26, 2020, from 9:00 am to 2:30 pm, Mr. Mao Thunin used and fulfilled his role as a servant of the people by trying to coordinate and solve Of the more than 100 challenges that have arisen, most have been resolved and some will be addressed later.
Mr. Kim Chantha added that sometimes people come to solve at the provincial hall and not finished, he will write the letter to the district authorities to solve. Within 7 days, if the district does not resolve the issue, a report must be made to the province so that Mr. Mao Thunin can lead the relevant departments to the actual dispute location.
