(Battambang): Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, said that the protection of customers of banking and financial institutions is an important issue that must be addressed together, especially in the situation affected by the spread of Kovid 19. .
Mr. Chea Chanto's remarks on the occasion of participating in the dissemination workshop on banking and finance in Cambodia under the theme "Customer protection of banking and financial institutions in the situation of the spread of Kovid 19" in the province Battambang on May 26, 2020.
The Governor said that in order to stabilize the banking system and alleviate the burden of customers while facing the spread of Kovid 19 virus, the National Bank of Cambodia needs to continue to put in place measures to help the sector to address and alleviate the burden of customers. Borrow money, especially during the Kovid 19 epidemic.
He said that in the past, the National Bank of Cambodia has also introduced a number of measures for banking and financial institutions, such as setting credit interest rates and methods to calculate interest rates, credit restructuring during the impact of the spread of Kovid 19, Request for Banking and Microfinance Institutions to ease credit-related fees and waive penalties for clients.
He said that with this, a telephone system has been set up for the public to communicate when there are problems or questions related to financial services and the implementation of this financial literacy campaign.
Mr. Rath Sovannarak, Director General of the National Bank of Cambodia, an expert in this field, confirmed that the banking and financial sector is now in a normal state after the National Bank of Cambodia has introduced a series of measures to stabilize the banking system and alleviate the burden. Clients from the effects of the spread of Kovid 19 virus.
He also requested the local authorities to cooperate in implementing and taking further legal action against some opportunists who spread false information with the intention of polluting the social environment for personal gain, especially in the affected situation. Impact of the spread of Kovid 19.
Mr. Rath Sovannarak stated that if customers or consumers use loans through legal banking and financial institutions, they will receive constructive support in practice. On the other hand, illegal borrowers who make loan agreements between individuals will inevitably face many challenges.
Kea Boran, Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Cambodian Microfinance Association, said that in response to this problem, the members of the Association of 103 Institutions have expressed their commitment to solve problems with their clients with gentleness and win-win.
The Royal Government has started to pay benefits to more than 30,000 garment and tourism workers who have suspended their employment contracts (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training on May 26, 2020 One told 33,231 workers working in 111 factories in the garment and tourism sectors who had been granted suspension contracts.
Through this announcement, the Ministry also confirmed that Wing Specialized Bank will send a message to the telephone number that the workers have provided to the Ministry through the factory administration in the past.
Heng Sour, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, said that the amount that the Royal Government will pay to workers in the first round is about $ 684,295. The workers are from 83 garment factories and 28 hotels and restaurants.
It should be noted that in order to alleviate the hardships of workers in the garment and tourism sector who lost their jobs during the crisis due to Kovid 19 disease, the Royal Government has decided to provide $ 40 per month to workers.
Mr. Samleang Try claimed that as a current strategy, the Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Public Works manages 800 kilometers of roads in all provinces, of which about 400 kilometers are paved roads (national and provincial roads). According to the director of the provincial public works department, roads have been developed from DBST to AC type roads, while some roads in the provincial town have been developed from rubber roads to reinforced concrete roads and have side drains.
As for the future direction, Mr. Samleang Try pointed out that the province will develop the red gravel road into a paved road, and the old paved road will be reinforced into a reinforced concrete road or AC paved road. . Separately, the remaining roads in the province will be regularly maintained without any chicken coops.
Mr. Samleang Try stressed that in Preah Vihear province, the roads managed by the Department of Public Works and Transport are still free of chicken coops, although some roads are not as clean as the new ones. He said the department has six teams working on the streets to check and repair this case.
