The following is the press release of the Royal Government of Cambodia: "Phnom Prampi" resort in Battambang province was established by the Royal Government as a natural heritage site
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to establish "Phnom Prampi" resort in Buor commune, Phnom Preuk district, Battambang province as a natural heritage site.
According to the Sub-Decree on the Establishment of the Seven Mountains Heritage Site, signed by Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen on May 25, 2020, the "Seven Mountains" natural heritage site covers an area of 353 hectares and 9 acres. 353.9 hectares).
The decision to establish the "Seven Mountains" as a natural heritage site also aims to provide natural and cultural services for sustainable use and promote the participation of local communities as well as the public in contributing to the management, protection and conservation of biodiversity. Diversified natural resources and local cultural heritage.
The sub-decree designates the Ministry of Environment as the authority to organize and manage the Phnom Prampi Natural Heritage Site in collaboration with the relevant ministries, institutions, the Battambang Provincial Administration and the Armed Forces in charge to ensure environmental protection, biodiversity conservation and the use of natural resources. Sustainable in accordance with the provisions of the law in force.
"Phnom Prampi" is a popular natural tourist site in Phnom Preuk district, Battambang province. Seven Mountains Resort is a resort connected by seven mountains and has a beautiful view.
There are three big caves in this mountain resort:
1: 100 caves: In this cave, there are many small caves, including bridesmaids, bridesmaids, box beds, stoves, her wings, nets, chests, bells, white cloth, crocodiles, lotus flowers, elephants and four-faced Brahma caves, etc. These caves are sacred to pray for happiness, and before every day, the nearby villagers always heard Pin Peat music coming out of a hundred caves. At the entrance of 100 caves, there is a statue of Grandma Sam that the locals pray for and that is sacred.
Legend has it that the Seven Mountains used to be a ship that sailed, and later this area was called the Sampov Loun area. Phnom Seven is a historical place because there is an old barracks right on top of the highest mountain.
