In addition, she also highlighted the vision of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, which is based on the culture of sharing, and this $ 1 million was raised from philanthropy on the occasion of the 157th anniversary of the World Day. Mr. Red Cross and Red Crescent, May 8, 2020. This was confirmed by Mr. Taing Samoeun, Secretary to Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen.
Ms. Annie Sok An added that the Cambodian Red Cross continues to support Kantha Bopha Hospital to save the lives of Cambodian children under any circumstances, including the fight against Kovid 19.
Today, the Cambodian Red Cross is also actively involved in the campaign against Kovid 19, in particular, bringing some medical equipment and food received from philanthropists to distribute and distribute to branches of the Cambodian Red Cross throughout the country to continue to help People in the community, in addition to educating and disseminating measures to prevent and combat Kovid 19 according to the Ministry of Health.
Ms. Annie Sok An said that at present, in addition to Kovid 19, people are also suffering from natural disasters due to wind and fire, so the Cambodian Red Cross, headed by His Excellency Dr. Bun Rany Hun Sen, continues to assign colleagues. Visit and give gifts of food and some money to alleviate the hardships of the people in time.
On that occasion, Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth expressed his deep gratitude to this special sharing culture of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen for continuing to provide $ 1 million to the Kantha Bopha Foundation.
This is the third time that the money will be distributed directly to Kantha Bopha Hospital, and the ninth time that the hospital has received funding from the Cambodian Red Cross to be used to save the lives of Cambodian children.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth confirmed that the $ 1 million he received from the Cambodian Red Cross, he promised to organize the fund according to the needs of Kantha Bopha Hospital, especially to ensure the sustainability of this hospital. Also.
It should be noted that on that occasion, Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth also handed over 1 million dollars to Kantha Bopha Hospital immediately.
