(Banteay Meanchey): Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, said that in the situation affected by the Kovid 19 virus, the National Bank of Cambodia needs to take measures to stabilize the banking system and reduce the burden on customers.
Mr. Chea Chanto made this remark during the opening of a seminar on "Customer Protection of Banking and Financial Institutions in the Situation of Kovid 19 Outbreak" in Banteay Meanchey Province on 25 May. 2020.
Mr. Chea Chanto said that the protection of customers of banking and financial institutions in the situation of the spread of Kovid 19 is a new topic that the National Bank of Cambodia held the first outreach workshop in Banteay Meanchey.
"In order to stabilize the banking system and alleviate the burden of customers while Cambodia is facing the unfinished spread of Kovid 19 virus, the National Bank of Cambodia needs to continue to put in place measures to help this sector," he said. "And to help ease the burden of borrowers, especially during the spread of Kovid 19."
Rath Sovannarak, director general of the National Bank of Cambodia, said that while Cambodia was facing 19 cases of Kovid, more than 80,000 Cambodians returning from Thailand could not afford to repay their micro loans. Finance. Under these circumstances, the Royal Government is taking measures to prevent and help the people affected by Kovid 19.
He added that the current outreach workshop to provide local authorities, people and stakeholders to understand the importance of challenges and solutions in the microfinance sector and work together to solve.
Kea Boran, Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Cambodian Microfinance Association, said that in the difficult circumstances caused by Kovid 19, the association has been actively working with its members and stakeholders, especially the National Bank of Cambodia, to help clients. Affected.
