Expert: Students at risk of contracting Kovid 19 and other diseases due to e-smoking
Dr. Mom Kong, executive director of the Cambodian Movement for Health, said that because the use of e-cigarettes (Vape) causes serious harm to the lungs, if you use e-cigarettes infected with Kovid 19, he will have a higher risk. He added that e-cigarettes and Sisha were banned from sale and used by the National Anti-Drug Authority.
Despite the ban, the sale of e-cigarettes (Vape) on social media under the name of smoking cessation machine. For this reason, the authorities should tighten the ban on the sale and use of e-cigarettes to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 and other diseases, especially among young students.
The warning came after the widespread use of e-cigarettes among young people, especially schoolchildren, the doctor said.
The use of e-cigarettes (Vape) among young schoolchildren is usually done in groups. Sharing tobacco products can increase the risk of transmitting Kovid 19 from one person to another, as well as motivating and easily motivating them to use other drugs.
