Chief Prelate of Prey Chhlak Pagoda: Pagodas are playing an important role for Cambodians
(Svay Rieng): In an interview with Fresh News Agency on the morning of May 24, 2020, His Holiness Yorn Soksan, Preah Vinay Thor, Svay Rieng City Sub-Committee and Chief Inspector of Prey Chhlak Pagoda, said that the Buddhist pagoda And is playing an important role for the Cambodian people.
The chief priest of Prey Chhlak pagoda said that the pagoda is a place for monks to educate morality, spread the word to the Buddhists and also a place for people to connect their lives to Buddhism. The location of Buddhism is also for Buddhists to rely on as a mental support and as a place of physical and mental education and as a shrine.
Rev. Yorn Soksan said that the temple is a place for Cambodians to perform various ceremonies that are Buddhist traditions according to the traditions of the Cambodian people, such as Kathin, Pchum Ben, Meak Bochea, Visak Bochea, rainy season, New Year and so on. . The temple is also a place for refining the mind to create a clear desire to feel calm, a place of residence for students who are the children of the poor and a hospital for the treatment of mental illness.
In addition, the pagoda is also a meeting place for people of all walks of life, regardless of race, color, nationality, social status, regardless of poverty or other beliefs.
Yorn Soksan added that the temple is also a place to help build society, such as bridges, roads, schools, hospitals, ponds, wells and planting valuable trees, fruit trees for medicine and so on. In particular, the temple is a storehouse of knowledge, a library, a museum of culture and civilization, etc., without regard for people of different faiths.
Wat Aram is also a tourist attraction that attracts people to visit, relax and get rid of boredom. Therefore, Buddhist pagodas are very important in relieving the burden of the state economy to some extent and also helping to solve social problems. Notification on the disappearance of Lin Non's title deed in Serey Dey Dus Village, Sangkat Prey Veng, Khan Dangkor
