Kampong Cham Provincial Authority continues to inspect the construction of Prek Koy embankment in Kang Meas district, so far more than 50%
(Kampong Cham): Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham Province and Chairman of the Provincial Disaster Management Committee, together with the technical officers of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, on May 24, 2020, inspected the progress of the construction of the temporary protection of Prek Koy bank and Emergency 250 meters in Anlong Koki village, Prek Koy commune, Kang Meas district.
According to Kampong Cham Provincial Hall officials, the construction of the Prek Koy embankment protection foundation started on February 29, 2020 and has reached more than 50% so far. The Gabion box continues to rise along the creek, as well as the groundwater drainage system and landfilling work to pave the way for the return trip, which is scheduled to be completed 100% before the start of this year's rainy season.
