Police crack down on 3 restaurants in Siem Reap that illegally cook wild animals
(Siem Reap): Police from Sangkat Forestry Administration, Prasat Bakong, Siem Reap Forestry Administration, in cooperation with the Forestry Administration's Mobile Wildlife Crime Intervention Team, cracked down on wildlife crime at three restaurants in Siem Reap immediately after these restaurants. Illegal use of wild animal meat to sell to guests
The Forestry Administration of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries said that the crackdown took place on May 24, 2020, while the restaurant and exhibits include:
1: Mlup Moha Heng Restaurant in Treang Village, Sangkat Slor Kram, Siem Reap City, confiscated 11 dead vultures, 50 dead doves and 230 dead rice sparrows.
