The tortoise has been identified by Hul as a rare and endangered species (governed by the Sites Convention, which strictly prohibits trade) and is currently only found in Koh Kong province, while in the world only in India, Malaysia and Bangladesh. Cambodia, and only in Koh Kong province, which has a natural environment, water, feed and sand, spawning is better for this animal to live and reproduce.
