The working group of the Cambodian People's Party provided food donations to 34 families, each of whom received 50 kg of rice, 2 boxes of noodles, 3 cans of fish, 1 mosquito net, 1 blanket, 1 sarong, 1 scarf and 50,000 Riels. This is the third time that the team has distributed to the poor, the first time distributed to 160 poor families and the second time to 150 families.
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - A U.S. naval vessel has successfully tested a powerful laser-guided laser-guided missile that can destroy flying drones, the US Navy has said. This is according to a quote from CNN on Sunday, May 24, 2020.
The U.S. Navy did not provide details on the exact location of the test, but said it took place in the Pacific on May 16. The power of the laser power used in the test was also not disclosed, but according to a 2018 report, the laser weapon may be at least 150 kilowatts.
The U.S. Navy says the laser weapon could be highly effective in protecting ships against drones or small warships. Car burning helps people in Stung Treng earn income to support their livelihood
(Stung Treng): Kralan is a kind of food that Khmer people like, leaving it since the time of our ancestors. Car burning has become a popular occupation for the people of Stung Treng province and helps the business to earn a decent income.
At present, the people living in Hang Koban village, Samaki commune, Stung Treng city, Stung Treng province continue the tradition of burning cars to make a living.
Ms. Po Heng, 35 years old, said that the car was made with ingredients such as young bamboo for making rice husks, sourdough rice, beans, coconut paste and salt. Before making the car, they wash the sour rice and leave it to drain, then mix it with the beans.
She described that later, they put the rice into a bamboo tube that was cut into pieces and put coconut milk in the bamboo tube. As for the coconut left over from squeezing the paste, it is used to cover the mouth of the bamboo tube. She claims that the burning of cars in Stung Treng is different from Kratie, Kampong Cham and other provinces.
In the beginning, there were about 28 families in Hang Koban village who started a car-burning business like Ms. Po Heng. Until now, they continue to do this business because it helps increase income and improve their family life to a more comfortable level.
Please note that kralan is a delicious food, this dish is made with sour rice mixed with beans and coconut milk, add a little salt and put in a bamboo tube about 3 to 4 meters long. When grilled, it is placed vertically and then boiled to be eaten.
The Stung Treng Provincial Department of Tourism has called on the people of this province to continue their business to strengthen local tourism as well as attract national and foreign visitors to visit the village. Especially know the taste of kralan, the food of Khmer ancestors.
