Spokesperson of the General Commission: In the past 22 days, 33,404 vehicles were inspected and fined according to the new sub-decree
(Phnom Penh): During the 22 days of tightening the land traffic law by increasing the fines according to Sub-Decree No. 39, that is, on May 1-22, 2021, the traffic police nationwide inspected and fined 33,404 vehicles in That 24417 motorcycles and 8987 cars of all kinds. This was confirmed by Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun, Deputy Commissioner General and spokesman for the National Police General Commission, to Fresh News.
Notable offenses for motorcycles are helmet, offense, no license plate, overweight and mobile phone use, while offenses noted for cars are speeding, no seat belt, overweight, using a phone and drunk.
He said that during the 22 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine the offending vehicle went well.
