(Phnom Penh): Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, confirmed that the Ministry of National Defense will record a number of events related to the fight against COVID-19 in Cambodia into history, including Support and support from the Chinese government and Samdech Techo Hun Sen's humanitarian activities.
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh made this remark on the occasion that he allowed a group of Chinese specialists to pay a courtesy call and say goodbye on the afternoon of May 22, 2020 at the Office of the Council of Ministers.
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh said that for the first event, it is historic that Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen led a delegation to visit Beijing, China, while China was under threat due to But the COVID-19 pandemic and the first foreign leader to enter Chinese territory at a time of crisis.
The fourth event is a historic event in which the Royal Government of China sent its military medical team to present to the Cambodian military medical team in Cambodia suffering from COVID-19. In addition, the Chinese government not only sent a team of medical specialists, but also sent COVID-19 virus prevention and control equipment.
In addition, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh confirmed that for this event, the Ministry of National Defense has been cooperating with the Ministry of Health to collect important elements for historical inscriptions. He also thanked the Chinese government and Ministry of Defense for sending military doctors to teach COVID-19 prevention methods to Cambodian military doctors.
