The working group for resolving this case congestion includes: The first group led by Mr. Kim Santepheap in charge of Phnom Penh, Kandal, Prey Veng and Svay Rieng provinces with the most cases, the second group led by Mr. Long Narin Tbong Khmum Provincial Court of Appeal, the third group led by Mr. Chiv Songhak is in charge of Battambang Provincial Court of Appeal, and the fourth group is led by Mr. Chin Malin in charge of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Court of Appeal.
Mr. Keut Rith said in a press conference that in order to ensure the integrity, integrity and accuracy of the campaign, the Ministry of Justice has set out two approaches:
* Approach 1: Campaign to resolve the congestion of this case must be carried out on the basis of the law, especially the action to solve the case must be strict and properly implemented in accordance with the law and procedures in force. In addition to the laws and regulations in force, the Ministry of Justice has issued legal guidelines to ensure the implementation of this approach.
* Approach 2: The campaign to resolve the congestion of this case must be based on justice, honesty and integrity, without having to absolutely have the situation of dry eggs in this campaign.
Along with the announcement of the campaign, Mr. Keut Rith instructed the President of the Capital-Provincial Court to focus on three principles, including: principles in the prosecution phase, principles in the investigation phase and principles in the trial phase.
