Senior Minister Sun Chanthol: 10 speed cameras will be installed on National Road 3 after construction
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, said that on National Road No. 3, which is more than 134 kilometers long, after the construction is completed, cameras will be installed at 10 different speeds. In addition, there is also a speed camera on the mobile phone that can detect vehicles exceeding the speed limit in all locations.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol stated this on May 21, 2020, when he led a delegation of the Ministry to inspect the quality of construction and expansion of National Road No. 3 from Chom Chao to Kampot. From General Him Yan, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, including relevant professional officers, representatives of construction companies, representatives of technical inspection companies and many other stakeholders.
The purpose of this inspection is to check the quality of the construction, whether it conforms to the specified technical standards and load books to ensure long-term use through the use of drilling machines, inspection of the foundation and inspection. Look at the installation of traffic lights and traffic signs to ensure the safety of people traveling.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also stated that the installation of cameras to catch vehicles exceeding the speed limit in order to reduce traffic accidents on the road, so people should not drive faster than the speed limit of the law. "Today, most of the traffic accidents that cause deaths and injuries are caused by speeding, which is up to 37 percent," he said.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol added that the new roads that are planned to be built, such as Street 31, Street 33, Street 41, have already prepared the budget to buy speed cameras on all these roads. And for the construction of new roads, there will be a budget already for this speed camera.
Please note that the construction project of National Road No. 3 Phnom Penh-Kampot, more than 134 kilometers long, so far has been completed about 74% and by the end of 2020 will be ready to pour a layer of rubber is no longer causing a lot of dust. On the people again.
