(US): More than 500 doctors have sent a letter to US President Donald Trump expressing concern about the possible negative health effects of austerity measures aimed at curbing COVID-19. Restricting people in the home to reduce the risk of infection will do more harm than good. This is according to the press release from Sputnik on the evening of Thursday, May 21, 2020.
Doctors believe that austerity measures against COVID-19 put millions of Americans at risk because they are forced to miss routine health check-ups, which could help them find out. See serious diseases such as cancer or can prevent stroke and heart attack.
According to the same doctors, restrictive measures can also lead to increased stress due to isolation and job loss, which can lead to suicide, drug and alcohol abuse. Original. Some studies have found similar consequences. The letter was sent to Tram on Tuesday.
As the economy has hit hard and infection rates have peaked, most U.S. governors have begun to lift regulations requiring residents to stay home and allow certain businesses to operate. Reopening has been gradual, but the security gap is expected to continue until at least the summer of this year.
