Speaking at a press conference on "Restricting the import of live pigs into Cambodia" on the afternoon of May 21, 2020, Mr. Tan Sophannara confirmed that after receiving the recommendation of the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, the Minister of Agriculture. Introduce various measures so that local people can raise more animals.
He added that the price of live pigs in the country also maintained a good stability, which used to fall to only 8,000 riel per kilogram, but now can ensure a stable price between 11,000-12,000 riel.
Mr. Srun Pov, President of the Cambodian Livestock Breeders Association, said that for many months, the price of live pigs was between 11,000 and 12,000 riel, which is a good price, which shows that the Ministry of Agriculture's actions make the livestock sector. Pigs resurrected.
Mr. Srun Pov continued, "The Cambodian Livestock Breeders Association supports the actions of the General Department of Health and Animal Production on the grounds that after the introduction of measures, the livestock production of farmers has increased, so tens of thousands of farmers Beneficial families have contributed to reducing poverty and migration. On behalf of the association, please support the actions of the ministry as well as the department.
An explanation for the closure of a pig importing company in violation of the principles of the General Department of Health and Animal Production was made at a press conference on restricting the import of live pigs into Cambodia, held at the General Department of Health and Animal Production in the afternoon. May 21, 2020.
He said the ministry had allowed only seven companies to import pigs from neighboring countries, dividing them into equal numbers. However, one company violated the law by overcrowding and using another company's animal health certificate, which affected the animal's health if the animal had a problem.
Mr. Tan Sophannara said that with care to reduce the number of pigs imported locally, the head of the Royal Government, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, recommended to Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to start cutting. Reduced from February 2020.
Mr. Tan Sophannara said that after receiving the recommendation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the General Department of Health and Animal Production has started to reduce the import of live pigs by about 70 percent to give you access. Raising pigs as well as local animal husbandry communities can be re-supplied.
At the same time, Mr. Tan Sophannara also informed the public that the Department of Health and Animal Production of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries is following the recommendations of the Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen as well as the Minister of Agriculture. Reduce the number of companies importing pigs, the Department of Health and Animal Production only reduces the number of imports.
