It should be noted that Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and Chairman of the National Commission for Organizing the ASEM13 Summit this morning, May 21, 2020, chaired a meeting to discuss the process. Ministry Office, with the participation of senior officials of various relevant ministries and institutions. ASEM13, hosted by Cambodia, was announced on March 10, 2020.
Cambodia became a member of ASEM in 2004 and has been given the confidence to host the event, which is scheduled to take place on 16-17 November 2020 under the theme: "Strengthening Multilateralism for Joint Growth". With the participation of the top leaders of 51 countries in Europe and Asia, the ASEAN Secretariat and the European Union.
The ASEM Summit is a biennial meeting of the Heads of State and Government, the President of the European Council, the President of the European Commission and the Secretary-General of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN). It has become an important platform for partnership cooperation in maintaining peace, stability, social and sustainable economic development.
Spokesperson of the General Commission: In the past 21 days, 3201 vehicles were inspected and fined according to the new sub-decree
(Phnom Penh): For 21 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, that is, on May 1-21, 2021, the traffic police throughout the country inspected and fined 3,011 vehicles in That 23447 motorcycles and 8,564 cars of all kinds. This was confirmed by Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun, Deputy Commissioner General and spokesman for the National Police General Commission, to Fresh News.
According to the lieutenant general, the notable offenses for motorcycles are not wearing helmets, breaking lights, not having license plates and using mobile phones. Notable offenses for cars are speeding, lack of seat belts, overweight, using a phone and no license plate.
He said that during the 21 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine the offending vehicle went well. He thanked and commended all the compatriots who use the road for their good obedience to the traffic law for the past time.
