CRC Donates Medical Equipment to Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital and Chak Angre Health Center for Combating Kovid 19 (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): CRC Presided Over by Dr. Bun Rany Hun Sen Provide medical equipment to the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital and Chak Angre Health Center for the fight against Kovid 19.
The ceremony of handing over and receiving this material was held at the headquarters of the Cambodian Red Cross on the morning of Thursday, May 21, 2020, under the chairmanship of Mrs. Pum Chantyny, Secretary General. Cambodian Red Cross.
On that occasion, the Secretary General brought the appreciation and greetings from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross to the front line doctors who have worked hard to dedicate their physical and mental strength to treat patients. All 122 Kovids have recovered and returned to their respective countries and homes. In particular, to contribute to the prevention, control and fight against Kovid 19 very well.
At the same time, the Secretary-General also called on people all over the country to join the Royal Government in preventing the second wave of transmission of 19 Kovid virus in Cambodia through the implementation of a series of measures by the Ministry of Health, especially Clean hands, wear a mask (if necessary), use a towel or scarf or paper towel to cover mouth when coughing or sneezing, and keep a safe social and personal safety gap.
Please be informed that during this meeting, the Cambodian Red Cross donated 200 pieces of PPE to the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital and 100 to Chak Angre Health Center.
