Stung Treng Provincial Governor Calls on All Donors to Donate Materials and Resources for Humanitarian Causes
(Stung Treng): Mr. Mom Saroeun, Governor of Stung Treng Province and Chairman of Stung Treng Branch of the Cambodian Red Cross called on all philanthropists to donate materials and resources for humanitarian causes to help vulnerable people, the elderly, widows, orphans and families. Poverty, people living with HIV and other diseases.
Mr. Mam Saroeun made this call on the morning of May 21, 2020, on the occasion of chairing a fundraising meeting for the World Red Cross and Red Crescent Day on May 8.
Mr. Mom Saroeun said that in 2020, the Cambodian Red Cross branch in Stung Treng province is preparing to organize the Red Cross Day under the theme "I love peace", but due to the issue of Kovid 19 and the guidance of the Central Committee of the Cambodian Red Cross.
He added that although the Red Cross Red Crescent Day on May 8 was not organized, the Provincial Red Cross Branch Committee appealed to the benefactors to share materials and resources in their generosity and strength to contribute to the Red Cross. Sincerely with all my heart and sincerity.
It should also be reminded that during 2019, the CRC Branch Committee of Stung Treng Province has collected and raised 213,460,000 Riels and 20,525 USD from philanthropists for humanitarian activities in Stung Treng Province. Kandal Province Inaugurated, Minister Reminds Officials to Work Cleanly and Prohibit Corruption
(Kandal): The new Kandal Provincial Department of Commerce building was inaugurated on May 21, 2020 to facilitate officials in providing services to the people.
The inauguration ceremony of the new building of Kandal Provincial Department of Commerce was presided over by Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce and attended by Mr. Kong Sophoan, Governor of Kandal Province, as well as many officials of the Ministry of Commerce and Kandal Province. Another picture.
On that occasion, the Minister expressed his congratulations to the new administrative building of Kandal Provincial Department of Commerce and thanked Mr. Kong Sophorn and provincial officials who have cooperated with the Department of Commerce to achieve the results. Pretty good.
The Minister also mentioned the achievements of the Ministry in the past and some other important tasks that the Ministry has been actively working on, including the preparation of various legal documents for the trade sector. Two laws, the law on e-commerce and the law on consumer protection, were promulgated by the King on November 2, 2019.
In addition, other legal documents are also being drafted, including: Law on Trade Contracts, Law on Competition, Law on Food Safety. The ministry is also considering a number of amendments to the law to modernize it in response to the current context.
On that occasion, the Minister also instructed and requested the officials of the Department of Commerce to continue to pay attention to expand their knowledge, both in terms of skills and foreign languages through further study, research and experience from civil servants in the Department of Commerce. Ministry of Commerce.
The Minister also requested that officials of the Department of Commerce continue to cooperate more closely with local authorities in order to participate in the widespread dissemination of the Royal Government's in-depth reform program. In particular, the Ministry of Commerce's in-depth reform of trade policies aimed at facilitating trade and facilitating exports.
Mr. Pan Sosak urged to strictly avoid demanding informal fees from producers and traders, which is contrary to the content of the joint declaration on public service packages between the Ministry of Commerce and the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
It should be noted that the trade sector is considered by the Royal Government of Cambodia as a key sector to promote national economic growth because our country has high potential for expanding domestic production and for diversifying exports to international markets.
The Cambodia Trade Integration Strategy 2019-2023 is a roadmap that is consistent and intertwined with the Rectangular Strategy, National Development Strategic Plan, Industrial Development Policy 2015-2025 and some other national policies. Three people arrested in connection with the fraud case of $ 1.5 million in the sale of wind land in Udong district, Kampong Speu province
(Phnom Penh): The Criminal Police Department of the National Police General Commission has arrested three people in connection with a case of fraud involving 1.5 million US dollars in the sale of nearly 200 hectares of wind land in Sdok Slat village, Phnom Touch commune, Udong district, Kampong Speu province.
According to the complaint of the victim, Yorn Senghan, on September 5, 2019, he entered into a contract to purchase and sell land with Ros Sokun and Ung Bunthon on an area of 191 hectares located at Sdok Slat village, Phnom Touch commune, Oudong district.
After signing the contract to buy and sell the land, the victim paid the land purchase price to Ros Sokun and Ung Bunthon in succession up to $ 1,500,000. According to the contract, the victim has the right to clear land for development and has the right to enjoy splitting lots or renting to customers.
Regarding the clearing, the victims contacted the three suspects to ask for permission to clear the land from the Udong District Administration, but they were always evaded by the three suspects, so the victims asked their lawyers to apply. Authorize the land clearing law to the Udong district administration directly.
The Udong district administration later responded that Ung Bunthorn's land use application documents and Ros Sokun's land use applications were forged documents to enter into a land purchase agreement to defraud the victims. Accident.
The suspect is currently being investigated by the Criminal Police Department for further investigation.
