Renewable Energy Museum and Samdech Hun Sen Kampot National Park to be built on more than 8 hectares in the community area of Monivong "Bokor" National Park, Teuk Chhou District, Kampot Province
(Kampot): Mr. Keo Rattanak, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) and Mr. Chiao Tay, Governor of Kampot Province, on May 21, 2020, chaired a consultation meeting on the implementation of the project to build a museum of renewable energy and parks. National Samdech Hun Sen Kampot. The meeting was attended by officials representing the relevant ministries, departments, units and local authorities.
The purpose of this meeting is to focus on the consultation of stakeholders, study the impact and encourage additional cooperation from local authorities to pave the way for this national project to implement construction as a contribution to the achievement. One more new from Kampot province.
The project to build the Museum of Renewable Energy and Samdech Hun Sen Kampot National Park is a project implemented in accordance with the sub-decree of the Royal Government to provide EDC to implement the construction project in 2020 and will be completed in 2022. It is located in the community area of Monivong "Bokor" National Park on an island of 8.60 hectares in Snom Prampi village, Mak Prang commune, Teuk Chhou district, Kampot province.
Although this project does not yet know the size of the budget, but the size of the construction of infrastructure is quite large to serve both research, research, experience and curiosity about hydropower technology in Cambodia and serve the tourism sector in This area of Kampot province as well.
Mr. Chiao Tai expressed his support for the implementation of this important national project in the spirit of cooperation to make the implementation of the project a national achievement for the benefit of the public, especially in the field of tourism. In the area of Teuk Chhou resort, Kampot province.
Therefore, the goal of this project is to focus on two issues, including:
* First: Refers to the creation of hydropower collections in some provinces in Cambodia to provide curiosity of national, international tourists or all Cambodians to visit here just by visiting In this museum, about the hydropower system in Cambodia can be learned without having to visit the place.
* Second: The placement of this national park is intended to attract more national and international tourists or people to visit this area and also a new national achievement, as well as achievements for Kampot province.
Mr. Keo Rattanak also confirmed the name of the project of the Museum of Renewable Energy and Samdech Hun Sen National Park, Kampot, which was presented in the current meeting that is the name of a temporary project if we have wind or solar energy in the future In addition, we will be able to revise.
