US provides $ 7.5 million grant to Cambodia for economic recovery after quake 19
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, and Mr. Patrick Murphy, US Ambassador to Cambodia, presided over a press conference on May 21, 2020. US government compensation for economic recovery after being affected by Kovid-19.
At the launch, Patrick Murphy announced that the US Government will provide a total of US $ 7.5 million in grant funding, including US $ 5 million for Cambodia's economic rehabilitation. Affected by Kovid-19 and another $ 2.5 million in additional funding to respond to health protection against Kovid-19 in Cambodia.
In the short term, this grant will be used to improve the daily lives of Cambodians affected by the epidemic, and in the medium term will be used to organize vocational training programs. Back to the victims in the private sector.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, on behalf of the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia, expressed his gratitude to the Government and people of the United States for providing targeted and timely intervention, a meaningful gesture for the Cambodian people.
He added that Kovid-19 has not only seriously affected public health, but also threatened the social and economic development of the world, and that Cambodia, as well as other countries, has suffered. Side effects of the disease.
In this context, Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth also emphasized that the Royal Government of Cambodia, under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, has launched a series of measures to balance the affected business activities. Serious impact, alleviating the lives of workers and the people of Cambodia.
The Deputy Prime Minister also stated that the Royal Government will launch social assistance programs to alleviate hardships and stabilize people's lives through the implementation of cash transfer programs for poor families, Cash for work program. , Short-term skills training to increase the ability to start your own business and lead to employment in new fields.
Taking that opportunity, both sides emphasized that 2020 is the 70th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between the two countries, Cambodia and the United States. The two sides pledged to continue to work for the maintenance of the long-standing friendship between the two countries and to further strengthen and deepen the existing foundation of friendship and cooperation.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol stated this on the morning of May 21, 2020, when he led a delegation of the Ministry to inspect the quality of construction of the extension of National Road No. 3 from Chom Chao to Kampot with the participation. From relevant professional officers, representatives of construction companies, representatives of technical inspection companies and stakeholders as well.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol further stated that for National Road No. 3, it was technically correct and the foundation was well compacted, however, the Ministry will continue to monitor this road until it is completed. National Road No. 3, if done correctly like this, until it is completed and can guarantee that people can travel up to 10 years without damage.
The senior minister added that the project to expand National Road No. 3 from Phnom Penh to Kampot city, with a total length of more than 134 km, is divided into two phases, the first phase: from Chom Chao to Bek Kus, the length of 69.90 km to be widened The road body up to 24.5 meters is a type of concrete road (AC) 9 cm thick, divided into 4 lanes.
The second phase from Bek Kous to Kampot city, 64,926 km long, 7 cm thick AC road, will be widened to 12 m wide, divided into 2 lanes. The project will be completed up to nine months ahead of schedule by the end of 2021.
