(Phnom Penh): Workers who used to work at The Great Duke Hotel Phnom Penh, formerly the Intercontinental Hotel, this morning, May 21, protested again in front of The Great Duke Hotel Phnom Penh after not receiving much compensation Months ago.
According to the tourism workers' union of The Great Dukes Phnom Penh, the resumption of protests is to ensure that hotel owners comply with the Arbitration Council's directives by compensating workers. Meanwhile, The Great Duke Phnom Penh Hotel, a former InterContinental Phnom Penh hotel, has closed down and refused to pay workers.
On February 20, 2020, the Arbitration Council issued an order for hotel owners to pay workers three points: First: to pay seniority benefits before 2019 by the base wage plus a minimum, second: compensation. Provide notice and third: Compensation for the remaining annual leave.
Kampong Thom Provincial Administration Calls on People Who Have Enjoyed the Land of "Nupheap Sophy" to Participate in Solving for the Common Benefit
(Kampong Thom): Kampong Thom Provincial Administration appealed to the people who have enjoyed the land of "Nupheap Sophy" to participate in the solution for the common benefit of both the people and the company based on two principles: 50% equality And 40% to the company, 60% to the people.
Mr. Sok Hay, Deputy Governor of Kampong Thom Province and Chairman of the Dispute Resolution Working Group between "Nupheap Sophy" and the people on May 20, 2020, said that the solution is based on the mediation for the people who are actually enjoying. On Nupheap Sophy in Kraya commune, Santuk district, Kampong Thom province, it started in March 2020 and until now, some people have accepted the principle without any coercion.
He said that 152 families whose land is growing large cashew crops, the company provides 60% of the land and people who grow potatoes get 50% of the land they are actually enjoying.
He added that the implementation of this work is scheduled to be completed during June 2020, and the company will have to register the company's land in 2021 as an economic land concession with a clear contract with the Royal Government. The company has received land investment from the Royal Government legally.
Meanwhile, the people who are enjoying the company's land also said that their acceptance was made voluntarily because in the past they already knew that it was the group's land, but they were still encroaching on it. Enjoy to feed the stomach, now they are happy to get the land legally occupied.
Meanwhile, Mr. Khchao Bunhim, Deputy Governor of Santuk District, said that the coordination principle of the provincial administration as well as the local authorities has taken into account the common interests, which are expressed through clear written principles between the company and the people and can not No company or citizen can violate mutual trust.
It should be noted that "Nupheap Sophy" has been investing in this land since 2007, which covers an area of nearly 3,000 hectares, and now the company has planted more than 900 hectares of cashew, mango and Today, the company employs about 60 to 70 people a day to take care of various crops to improve their livelihood.
