(Kampong Thom): Mr. Khan Khon, Advisor to the Ministry of Cults and Religions and Director of the Gospel Mission Association, called on all people to do more good deeds to live in harmony.
Mr. Khan Khon made this appeal during the distribution of humanitarian aid to 80 vulnerable and vulnerable families in Sala Visay commune, Prasat Balong district and Sroyov commune, Stung Sen city on May 21, 2020. Invitation from Mr. Heng Cheng, Advisor to the Ministry of Cults and Religions and Chairman of the Board of the Christian Association of Cambodia, local authorities and many people.
Mr. Khan Khon said that the Gospel Mission Association is a local Christian organization established for the purpose of spreading the Christian faith in Jesus Christ and contributing to the Royal Government in the development of the nation through humanitarian work as much as it can. Yes.
He added that the Gospel Mission Association always pays attention to the well-being of the people, especially vulnerable people, the elderly, the disabled, widows, orphans or other vulnerable people, regardless of political affiliation. No. In fact, vulnerable families, widows and the elderly receive humanitarian donations from the Gospel Mission to alleviate suffering for a time, even though the gifts distributed at this time are small.
At the same time, Mr. Khan Khon also advised all people to consider health care by drinking clean water, sleeping under a mosquito net and cleaning the environment around the house to avoid the occurrence of malaria and dengue fever. In addition, efforts must be made to raise animals and increase the cultivation of various crops in order to improve the standard of living and reduce daily expenses.
He also instructed people to be careful of thunder, lightning, wind, convulsions, to educate children to stay away from drugs and when driving to wear helmets and seat belts to avoid traffic accidents and participate in the prevention of Kovid 19 by practicing As directed by the Ministry of Health.
Gifts to be distributed to 80 families, each family received rice, noodles, fish sauce, health food and some other materials. It should be noted that 80 families, including 40 families in Sala Visay commune and 40 families in Srayov commune.
Nearly 200 Families in Krouch Chhmar District Receive Donations from Samdech Kittipritthbandit and Tbong Khmum Red Cross Branch
The event was led by Mr. Seak Leng, Chairman of the Provincial Council, Mr. Cheam Chansophoan, Chairman of the Provincial Red Cross Branch Committee and Governor of Tbong Khmum, along with the Deputy Governor, district authorities and other working groups.
