108 needy families in Chhep district receive donations from the Cambodian Red Cross, Senior Minister Meas Sophea calls on people to continue to protect themselves from Kovid 19
(Preah Vihear): 108 poor families from 3 communes in Chep district, Preah Vihear province, this morning, May 21, 2020, received humanitarian donations from the Cambodian Red Cross.
The ceremony was held in the presence of Senior Minister Meas Sophea, Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group for Preah Vihear Provincial Assistance and Honorary Chairman of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch, with the participation of Mr. Prak Sovann, Governor of Preah Vihear Province and Chairman of the Joint Committee of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch. With the leadership of government officials and the Cambodian Red Cross team in many provinces and districts.
At the same time, Senior Minister Meas Sophea also called on people to continue to pay attention to hygiene by following the guidelines of the Ministry of Health, such as washing hands and soap or alcohol, wearing a mask when in town. Do not be negligent, as long as there is no vaccine for protection.
