At a press conference on the progress and direction of the Pursat provincial administration, organized by the Royal Government Spokesperson, Mr. Mao Thunin, confirmed that the two projects are one of the hydropower planned to be built on the Pursat River and the other production site. Solar power in Krakor district.
Mr. Mao Thunin said, "Currently, there will be another construction project related to an 80-megawatt Stung Pursat hydropower plant and a 60-megawatt solar power plant in Krakor district." "We are studying and preparing for this work."
The provincial governor pointed out that what has been used so far is the Atai hydropower plant in O'Som commune with a capacity of 120 megawatts. As for the budget to be spent on the work of these two power plants, he has not been able to confirm yet, this is the decision and thought of the head of the Royal Government with the Ministry.
Mr. Mao Thunin claimed that the construction of this power plant is not only for use in Pursat province, but can be distributed and used throughout the country.
